{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201550098,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa59c703001WBfB0g3pReIp1T","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa59b59c0012zRFbnI863KuIL","type":"tool","id":"call_76fd1ddcdd6903aad3d87e01","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md, lines 1-334\n1: ---\n2: name: deep-review\n3: description: \"Autonomous iterative code-review loop with externalized state, convergence detection, P0/P1/P2 findings, fresh context per pass.\"\n4: argument-hint: \"[target] [:auto|:confirm] [--max-iterations=N] [--convergence=N] [--stop-policy=convergence|max-iterations] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--extend=N]\"\n5: version: 1.13.0.0\n6: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task]\n7: ---\n8: <!-- Note: Task is for the command executor (loop management); @deep-review agent is LEAF-only (no Task). No WebFetch: review is code-only. -->\n9: \n10: # Autonomous Deep Review Loop\n11: \n12: Iterative code review and quality auditing protocol with fresh context per iteration, externalized state, convergence detection, and severity-weighted findings (P0/P1/P2).\n13: \n14: Runtime path resolution:\n15: - OpenCode runtime: `.opencode/agents/*.md`, a link to the `.skilled/agents/*.md` source\n16: - Claude runtime: `.claude/agents/*.md`\n17: - Other runtimes: see `.skilled/bin/agent-mirror-crosswalk.md`\n18: \n19: Convergence threshold semantics and sibling-parity notes (deep-review 0.10 vs deep-research 0.05) live in `references/convergence/convergence.md` §1 under \"Threshold Semantics and Sibling Parity\".\n20: \n21: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n22: \n23: ### When to Use This Skill\n24: \n25: Use this skill when:\n26: - Code quality audit requiring multiple rounds across different review dimensions\n27: - Spec folder validation requiring cross-reference checks between docs and implementation\n28: - Release readiness check before shipping a feature or component\n29: - Finding misalignments between spec documents and actual code\n30: - Verifying cross-references across documentation, agents, commands, and code\n31: - Iterative review where each dimension's findings inform subsequent dimensions\n32: - Unattended or overnight audit sessions\n33: \n34: ### When NOT to Use\n35: \n36: - Simple single-pass code review (use `sk-code`'s code-review mode instead)\n37: - Known issues that just need fixing (go directly to implementation)\n38: - Implementation tasks (use `sk-code` or `/speckit:implement`)\n39: - Quick one-file checks (use direct Grep/Read)\n40: - Fewer than 2 review dimensions needed (single-pass suffices)\n41: \n42: ### FORBIDDEN INVOCATION PATTERNS\n43: \n44: This skill is invoked EXCLUSIVELY through the `/deep:review` command. The command's YAML workflow owns state, dispatch, and convergence.\n45: \n46: **NEVER:**\n47: - Write a custom bash/shell dispatcher to parallelize iterations (ad-hoc shell fan-out)\n48: - Invoke any CLI executor (cli-codex, cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-cursor, cli-devin, cli-pi, cli-deepseek-harness) directly in a loop to simulate iterations\n49: - Manually write iteration prompts to `/tmp` and dispatch them via `copilot -p`\n50: - Dispatch the `@deep-review` LEAF agent via the Task tool for iteration loops (the agent is LEAF, a single iteration, and MUST be driven by the command's workflow)\n51: - Skip the state machine: `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-config.json`, `deltas/`, `prompts/`, `logs/`\n52: - Manage iteration state outside the resolved local review packet under `{spec_folder}/review/`\n53: \n54: **COMMAND-DRIVEN FAN-OUT IS SUPPORTED:** use `--executor`/`--executors`/`--concurrency` flags on `/deep:review`. The command's YAML `step_fanout_spawn` owns multi-lineage dispatch; `fanout-merge.cjs` applies strongest-restriction (any lineage with an active P0, or a required quality gate still failing at its stop → merged FAIL). This is not ad-hoc shell dispatch — it is the canonical fan-out path. Intra-lineage wave orchestration remains deferred.\n55: \n56: **ALWAYS:**\n57: - Invoke via `/deep:review :auto` or `/deep:review :confirm`\n58: - Let the command's YAML workflow own dispatch (auto: `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`)\n59: - Record each leaf iteration through the append gateway (`runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory <spec folder> --event-json <file>`) — the gateway is the SINGLE state-log writer: it authorizes, fences, and receipts the write, then refreshes `{state_paths.state_log}` from the ledger\n60: - Treat `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` as the reducer for DERIVED artifacts only (finding registry, dashboard metrics, strategy updates); it never writes the state log\n61: - Require every iteration to produce BOTH the markdown narrative AND the JSONL delta (dispatch scripts must fail if either is missing)\n62: - Use `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs` to locate the canonical review root\n63: \n64: ### Trigger Phrases\n65: \n66: - \"review code quality\" / \"audit this code\"\n67: - \"audit spec folder\" / \"validate spec completeness\"\n68: - \"release readiness check\" / \"pre-release review\"\n69: - \"find misalignments\" (between spec and implementation)\n70: - \"verify cross-references\" (across docs and code)\n71: - \"deep review\" / \"iterative review\" / \"review loop\"\n72: - \"quality audit\" / \"convergence detection\"\n73: \n74: ### Keyword Triggers\n75: \n76: `deep review`, `convergence review`, `iterative review`, `review loop`, `release readiness`, `spec folder review`, `convergence detection`, `quality audit`, `find misalignments`, `verify cross-references`, `pre-release review`, `audit spec folder`\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n81: \n82: The `system-deep-loop` hub routes an iterative review loop here, and its `review` mode signal selects this packet.\n83: The signal fires when a request names a deep review, a convergence review, a review loop, a release readiness check or a request to audit the diff.\n84: The loop runs only through `/deep:review`, whose workflow owns state, dispatch and convergence.\n85: \n86: `references/protocol/quick-reference.md` loads first on every invocation.\n87: The review phase named by the dispatch context then selects the loop protocol, the convergence documents or the state documents.\n88: \n89: The routing pseudocode in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) is the one route from a request to a resource set.\n90: A request whose intent scores stay under the threshold returns `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK` with a disambiguation checklist, never a silent default.\n91: Read [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting skill-local resources; open only the matched files.\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n96: \n97: ### Architecture\n98: \n99: `/deep:review` owns the loop. The YAML workflow initializes state, dispatches one LEAF review iteration at a time, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `review-report.md`, and saves continuity. The LEAF agent reads state, reviews one dimension, writes `iteration-NNN.md`, updates strategy, and appends JSONL. Full 4-phase lifecycle: `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`.\n100: \n101: ### Resource Map Coverage Gate\n102: \n103: When `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` exists at init, it is a mandatory audit input: one iteration audits `target_files` coverage against it, and synthesis adds the `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` report section. `--no-resource-map` disables this, and an absent map skips it without failing the loop.\n104: Full sequencing: `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` (init 9a, iteration 3b, synthesis 4). Schema: `references/state/state-format.md`.\n105: \n106: ### Bounded Context Snapshot Replacement\n107: \n108: During initialization, capture a bounded, pointer-based context snapshot in `deep-review-strategy.md` `Known Context` before the first dimension runs: target pointers, the claimed behavior to verify, reuse pointers and risk areas.\n109: Do not create a context-loop report or widen scope beyond the declared target.\n110: \n111: ### State Packet Location\n112: \n113: The review state packet always lives under the target spec's local `review/` folder.\n114: Root-spec targets use `{spec_folder}/review/` directly.\n115: Child-phase and sub-phase targets use **flat-first** placement: the first run writes flat, and a `pt-NN` sibling packet is allocated only when prior content already exists for a different target.\n116: Full resolution rule and worked examples: `references/state/state-format.md` §1.\n117: \n118: Core artifacts: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, `.deep-review-pause`, `resource-map.md`, `review-report.md`, and `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\n119: \n120: The loop writes `review/review-report.md` itself at synthesis from the findings registry and the JSONL state; `create.sh --level review` is only for a review packet authored by hand.\n121: \n122: ### Core Innovation: Fresh Context Per Iteration\n123: \n124: Each agent dispatch gets a fresh context window; state continuity comes from files, not memory, preventing accumulated findings from biasing later dimensions. Init writes config/strategy/JSONL; each loop reads state, checks convergence, dispatches one dimension, records findings, and reduces state; synthesis compiles the report and saves continuity.\n125: \n126: ### Review Dimensions\n127: \n128: The four primary review dimensions (configured in `assets/review-mode-contract.yaml`; configure them by the id in parentheses, because any other name counts as a custom dimension):\n129: \n130: | Dimension | Focus | Key Questions |\n131: |-----------|-------|---------------|\n132: | **Correctness** (`correctness`) | Logic, behavior, error handling | Behavior matches claims? Edge cases handled? |\n133: | **Security** (`security`) | Vulnerabilities, exposure, trust boundaries | Inputs validated? Credentials exposed? |\n134: | **Spec-Alignment / Traceability** (`traceability`) | Spec vs. implementation fidelity | Code matches spec.md? Planned items present? |\n135: | **Completeness / Maintainability** (`maintainability`) | Coverage, dead code, documentation | TODOs resolved? Code self-documenting? |\n136: \n137: ### Lifecycle + Reducer Contract\n138: \n139: Review mode is lineage-aware.\n140: \n141: - **Lifecycle modes:** `new`, `resume`, `restart`, and `completed-continue` (set by `--extend=N` on a completed run; see `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`).\n142: - **Required lineage fields:** `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, and `releaseReadinessState`.\n143: - **Reducer contract:** consumes the latest JSONL delta, the new iteration file, and prior reduced state, then emits finding registry, dashboard metrics, and strategy updates.\n144: \n145: ### Severity Classification\n146: \n147: | Severity | Criteria | Blocking |\n148: |----------|----------|---------|\n149: | **P0** | Correctness failure, security vulnerability, spec contradiction | Yes, blocks PASS verdict |\n150: | **P1** | Degraded behavior, incomplete implementation, missing validation | Conditional, triggers CONDITIONAL verdict |\n151: | **P2** | Style, naming, minor improvements, documentation gaps | No, PASS with advisories |\n152: \n153: P0 and P1 also follow the reach calibration in `sk-code-review`'s `references/review-core.md` §2.\n154: A blocking finding names an input or call path the code's stated contract allows, or a real caller that sends the failing input.\n155: \"Missing validation\" is P1 only when the unvalidated input is in reach. Validation the code never claimed, for input outside its stated contract, is P2 hardening.\n156: At a trust boundary every value the outside can send is in reach.\n157: \n158: The scale has exactly three tiers, and no fourth is reserved.\n159: A severity outside P0/P1/P2 is not a fourth tier. That covers a `P3` inherited from an older four-level convention, and any unlisted word.\n160: Collapse it to the tier its impact actually matches (a `P3` becomes `P2`) and keep the original rating visible in the finding, so the rating is converted rather than lost.\n161: An unconverted out-of-scale severity reaches the cross-lineage merge unranked, where it sorts below every P2 and cannot raise the merged verdict.\n162: \n163: ### Verdicts\n164: \n165: | Verdict | Condition |\n166: |---------|-----------|\n167: | **PASS** | No P0/P1 findings and no open search debt, P2 findings recorded as advisories (`hasAdvisories: true`) |\n168: | **CONDITIONAL** | P1 findings present, or open search debt remains, with remediation plan included in report |\n169: | **FAIL** | Any P0 finding confirmed after adversarial self-check, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop |\n170: \n171: ### Acceptance-Coverage Signal\n172: \n173: When the review target is a spec folder, deep review reflects the `AC_COVERAGE` validation signal in synthesis for Level 2+ folders.\n174: The signal applies only once `checklist.md` exists and `implementation-summary.md` is in-progress or later. Level 1 folders and fresh scaffolds are exempt.\n175: It is advisory while the validation rule stays INFO/default-on (non-blocking, and `RULE_STATUS` stays `pass`).\n176: It can add traceability context and planning-seed work, but must not alter the iteration final-line contract below unless a later enforcement rollout explicitly changes severity.\n177: \n178: ### Iteration Final-Line Contract (MANDATORY)\n179: \n180: Every `iteration-NNN.md` MUST end with exactly one of the following plain-text lines as the **absolute final line** (no trailing whitespace, no variation), and every review MUST emit exactly one parseable verdict:\n181: \n182: ```\n183: Review verdict: PASS\n184: ```\n185: \n186: ```\n187: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n188: ```\n189: \n190: ```\n191: Review verdict: FAIL\n192: ```\n193: \n194: **Mapping rule:** PASS if no P0 or P1 findings in this iteration. CONDITIONAL if any P1 (but no P0) findings. FAIL if any P0 findings. P2-only findings → PASS.\n195: \n196: **VERDICT_LOCK:** Any confirmed active P0 forces the exact final line `Review verdict: FAIL` -- never relabel that state as conditional, partial, mixed, or advisory, and truncated/partial output is not a valid substitute for the final line. An optional advisory `riskScore` may appear in narratives/JSONL for relative risk calibration but never changes the `PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` mapping.\n197: \n198: Downstream automation (including the synthesis phase and CI gate parser) parses this final line via exact string match, do not vary the format.\n199: \n200: **What the check proves:** the post-dispatch verifier validates the *shape* of this line, and nothing more: exactly one well-formed verdict line, and it is final.\n201: It does not read findings, so a `PASS` written above active P1 findings satisfies it, and no parser here makes the line true.\n202: The verdict a release decision reads is recomputed from the findings registry.\n203: In a fan-out run the cross-lineage merge is the authoritative rollup, where any active P0, or any lineage's required quality gate still failing at its stop, becomes a merged FAIL.\n204: Treat the final line as the leaf's self-report and the registry as the record.\n205: \n206: ### Executor Selection Contract\n207: \n208: Executor settings are owned by the YAML workflow and rendered prompt pack -- never hand-dispatch review iterations; each iteration stays LEAF-only and produces the required markdown plus JSONL delta. Full contract (per-iteration invariants, failure modes, JSONL audit field, config surface/precedence, TrustState surface): `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`.\n209: \n210: ### Stop Decision, Counters and Limits\n211: \n212: `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` computes the whole stop decision once per pass from the config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. `deep-review.yaml` renders no stop arithmetic of its own. The frozen stop reasons are `converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `manualStop`, `error`, `stuckRecovery`, `userPaused` and `maxDurationReached`. A missing graph decision blocks every non-terminal STOP.\n213: \n214: The stuck count and the consecutive failure count are rebuilt from the state log on every pass, so a resumed run counts the same as one that never paused. Under expansive depth with an active frontier node, the stuck count reads only that node's bound rows, and a bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress whatever its ratio. Failed iterations stay out of the ratio signals. Three trailing failed iterations stop the loop with stop reason `error`. In confirm mode only, the workflow first asks the operator Retry, Skip or Cancel. Auto mode has no such question.\n215: \n216: Each pass also compares `maxDurationMinutes` with the config `createdAt`. When the limit is reached the loop skips the dispatch and goes to synthesis with stop reason `maxDurationReached`.\n217: \n218: ### Expansive Depth Mode\n219: \n220: - `--depth-mode=expansive` is opt-in. It seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1 and grows them only through admitted `frontier_proposal` rows, stored in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`. An absent flag (`default`) runs exactly as before.\n221: - A defaulted `--max-iterations` is derived from the seed, up to 24, and an explicit value always wins.\n222: - While a node is open or active, the frontier veto turns a stop candidate into `CONTINUE` with reasonDetail `frontierOpen`. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the review floor.\n223: - Caps, budget arithmetic, admission checks, dimension steering, `frontier_drained` and fan-out partitioning: [loop-protocol.md](references/protocol/loop-protocol.md) §Expansive Depth Frontier and [convergence.md](references/convergence/convergence.md) §Expansive Depth Mode.\n224: \n225: ---\n226: \n227: ## 4. RULES\n228: \n229: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n230: \n231: 1. Read JSONL and strategy before review action.\n232: 2. Review one dimension per iteration and write findings to `iteration-NNN.md`.\n233: 3. Append JSONL with severity counts, finding detail, and `newInfoRatio`.\n234: 4. Cite every finding with `[SOURCE: file:line]`. Reject inference-only findings.\n235: 5. Re-read cited code before recording any P0.\n236: 6. Keep target files read-only.\n237: 7. Use `generate-context.js` for continuity saves. **Owner**: the workflow (`deep-review.yaml`) calls it at the save phase, not the reducer (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`) directly — don't expect continuity-save side effects from the reducer alone.\n238: 8. Emit setup `BINDING:` lines before workflow output.\n239: 9. Refuse nested dispatch with: `REFUSE: nested Task tool dispatch is forbidden for LEAF agents. Returning partial findings instead.`\n240: \n241: ### ⛔ NEVER\n242: \n243: 1. **Dispatch sub-agents**, `@deep-review` is LEAF-only. It cannot dispatch additional agents. When dispatch is requested, use the canonical REFUSE wording (ALWAYS rule 9).\n244: 2. **Hold findings in context**, Write everything to iteration files. Context is discarded after each dispatch.\n245: 3. **Exceed TCB**, Stay within `config.maxToolCallsPerIteration` tool calls per iteration. Breadth over depth per cycle.\n246: 4. **Ask the user**, The leaf agent never asks. It makes best-judgment decisions without pausing. The workflow asks only in `:confirm` mode, at its approval gates.\n247: 5. **Skip convergence checks**, Every iteration must be evaluated against convergence criteria before the next dispatch.\n248: 6. **Modify config after init**, review parameters in `deep-review-config.json` are read-only after initialization, apart from the workflow's own writes that `references/state/state-format.md` lists: the terminal status flip, `--extend=N`, `step_frontier_scope`, `step_frontier_budget` and a fan-out rerun's `step_fanout_root_config`.\n249: 7. **Modify files under review**, The review loop is observation-only. No code changes during audit.\n250: 8. **Use WebFetch**, Review is code-only. No external resource fetching is permitted.\n251: 9. **Implement fixes during review**, Report findings only. Implementation is a separate follow-up step.\n252: \n253: ### Iteration Status Enum\n254: \n255: `complete | timeout | error | stuck | insight | thought`\n256: \n257: - `insight`: Low newInfoRatio but important finding that changes the verdict trajectory.\n258: \n259: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n260: \n261: 1. **3+ consecutive failed iterations**, The loop stops with stop reason `error` and enters synthesis with partial findings. In confirm mode the workflow asks Retry, Skip or Cancel first.\n262: 2. **State file corruption**, Cannot reconstruct iteration history from JSONL or iteration files.\n263: 3. **All dimensions covered with P0 findings remaining**, Human sign-off required before shipping.\n264: 4. **Security vulnerabilities discovered in production code**, Escalate immediately. Do not defer to report synthesis.\n265: 5. **All recovery tiers exhausted**, No automatic recovery path remaining in convergence protocol.\n266: \n267: ---\n268: \n269: ## 5. REFERENCES\n270: \n271: The router discovers reference, asset and script docs dynamically.\n272: Start with these, in order:\n273: \n274: 1. `references/protocol/quick-reference.md`\n275: 2. `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`\n276: 3. `references/convergence/convergence.md`\n277: 4. `references/convergence/convergence-signals.md`\n278: 5. `references/state/state-format.md`\n279: 6. `references/state/state-outputs.md`\n280: 7. `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md`\n281: 8. `assets/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n282: 9. `assets/deep-review-strategy.md`\n283: \n284: Then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/`, and automation from `scripts/` when present.\n285: \n286: Scripts: `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, `scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`.\n287: \n288: Detailed contracts:\n289: \n290: - `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`: executor invariants, failure modes and config surface.\n291: - `references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md`: state transitions, error handling and STOP-decision gates.\n292: - `references/protocol/completion-criteria.md`: the full loop-completion, quality-gate and validation-success checklist.\n293: - `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md`: two-tier content-hash dedup.\n294: \n295: ---\n296: \n297: ## 6. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n298: \n299: A review loop is complete only when convergence and every quality gate agree.\n300: All of these must hold:\n301: \n302: - The composite stop score clears `compositeStopScore`, or `maxIterations` is hit without a false-positive STOP.\n303: - Every configured dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage, plus the core traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) when traceability is among the configured dimensions. An absent dimension list means the default four, which include it.\n304: - All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md` and `deep-review-dashboard.md` (a fan-out run keeps one per lineage instead), plus one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n305: - `review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate`.\n306: - Continuity is saved via `generate-context.js`.\n307: \n308: Nine binary quality gates, from config validity through adversarial P0 replay and acceptance coverage, must all pass before STOP is legal.\n309: The security-sensitive override also applies when the target touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence or shared policy (`minStabilizationPasses=2` plus fix-completeness replay).\n310: Full gate-by-gate criteria and rationale: `references/protocol/completion-criteria.md`.\n311: \n312: Validate a completed run with `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` (skill still surfaces) and `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` (exits 0).\n313: \n314: ---\n315: \n316: ## 7. INTEGRATION POINTS\n317: \n318: ### Framework Integration\n319: \n320: This skill operates within the behavioral framework defined in the active runtime's root doc (CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md).\n321: \n322: Key integrations:\n323: - **Gate 2**: Skill routing via `skill_advisor.py` (keywords: deep review, convergence review, iterative review)\n324: - **Gate 3**: File modifications require spec folder question per the root doc Gate 3. The spec folder determines the `{spec_folder}/review/` state packet location\n325: - **Continuity**: `/speckit:resume` is the operator-facing recovery surface, resolving context in the order `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`. During review, the agent writes iteration, strategy, and JSONL state; after synthesis, run `generate-context.js` to write canonical packet continuity\n326: - **Command**: `/deep:review` is the primary invocation point\n327: \n328: ### Code Graph Integration\n329: \n330: The review loop consumes the shared runtime graph and its strict mode-gate validator; packet-specific convergence and state rules remain in this skill.\n331: \n332: ### Related Skills\n333: \n334: Related skills: `deep-research` for investigation loops, `sk-code`'s code-review mode for single-pass review doctrine, and `system-spec-kit` for command-owned state and continuity saves.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md, lines 1-334\n1: ---\n2: name: deep-review\n3: description: \"Autonomous iterative code-review loop with externalized state, convergence detection, P0/P1/P2 findings, fresh context per pass.\"\n4: argument-hint: \"[target] [:auto|:confirm] [--max-iterations=N] [--convergence=N] [--stop-policy=convergence|max-iterations] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--extend=N]\"\n5: version: 1.13.0.0\n6: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task]\n7: ---\n8: <!-- Note: Task is for the command executor (loop management); @deep-review agent is LEAF-only (no Task). No WebFetch: review is code-only. -->\n9: \n10: # Autonomous Deep Review Loop\n11: \n12: Iterative code review and quality auditing protocol with fresh context per iteration, externalized state, convergence detection, and severity-weighted findings (P0/P1/P2).\n13: \n14: Runtime path resolution:\n15: - OpenCode runtime: `.opencode/agents/*.md`, a link to the `.skilled/agents/*.md` source\n16: - Claude runtime: `.claude/agents/*.md`\n17: - Other runtimes: see `.skilled/bin/agent-mirror-crosswalk.md`\n18: \n19: Convergence threshold semantics and sibling-parity notes (deep-review 0.10 vs deep-research 0.05) live in `references/convergence/convergence.md` §1 under \"Threshold Semantics and Sibling Parity\".\n20: \n21: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n22: \n23: ### When to Use This Skill\n24: \n25: Use this skill when:\n26: - Code quality audit requiring multiple rounds across different review dimensions\n27: - Spec folder validation requiring cross-reference checks between docs and implementation\n28: - Release readiness check before shipping a feature or component\n29: - Finding misalignments between spec documents and actual code\n30: - Verifying cross-references across documentation, agents, commands, and code\n31: - Iterative review where each dimension's findings inform subsequent dimensions\n32: - Unattended or overnight audit sessions\n33: \n34: ### When NOT to Use\n35: \n36: - Simple single-pass code review (use `sk-code`'s code-review mode instead)\n37: - Known issues that just need fixing (go directly to implementation)\n38: - Implementation tasks (use `sk-code` or `/speckit:implement`)\n39: - Quick one-file checks (use direct Grep/Read)\n40: - Fewer than 2 review dimensions needed (single-pass suffices)\n41: \n42: ### FORBIDDEN INVOCATION PATTERNS\n43: \n44: This skill is invoked EXCLUSIVELY through the `/deep:review` command. The command's YAML workflow owns state, dispatch, and convergence.\n45: \n46: **NEVER:**\n47: - Write a custom bash/shell dispatcher to parallelize iterations (ad-hoc shell fan-out)\n48: - Invoke any CLI executor (cli-codex, cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-cursor, cli-devin, cli-pi, cli-deepseek-harness) directly in a loop to simulate iterations\n49: - Manually write iteration prompts to `/tmp` and dispatch them via `copilot -p`\n50: - Dispatch the `@deep-review` LEAF agent via the Task tool for iteration loops (the agent is LEAF, a single iteration, and MUST be driven by the command's workflow)\n51: - Skip the state machine: `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-config.json`, `deltas/`, `prompts/`, `logs/`\n52: - Manage iteration state outside the resolved local review packet under `{spec_folder}/review/`\n53: \n54: **COMMAND-DRIVEN FAN-OUT IS SUPPORTED:** use `--executor`/`--executors`/`--concurrency` flags on `/deep:review`. The command's YAML `step_fanout_spawn` owns multi-lineage dispatch; `fanout-merge.cjs` applies strongest-restriction (any lineage with an active P0, or a required quality gate still failing at its stop → merged FAIL). This is not ad-hoc shell dispatch — it is the canonical fan-out path. Intra-lineage wave orchestration remains deferred.\n55: \n56: **ALWAYS:**\n57: - Invoke via `/deep:review :auto` or `/deep:review :confirm`\n58: - Let the command's YAML workflow own dispatch (auto: `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`)\n59: - Record each leaf iteration through the append gateway (`runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory <spec folder> --event-json <file>`) — the gateway is the SINGLE state-log writer: it authorizes, fences, and receipts the write, then refreshes `{state_paths.state_log}` from the ledger\n60: - Treat `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` as the reducer for DERIVED artifacts only (finding registry, dashboard metrics, strategy updates); it never writes the state log\n61: - Require every iteration to produce BOTH the markdown narrative AND the JSONL delta (dispatch scripts must fail if either is missing)\n62: - Use `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs` to locate the canonical review root\n63: \n64: ### Trigger Phrases\n65: \n66: - \"review code quality\" / \"audit this code\"\n67: - \"audit spec folder\" / \"validate spec completeness\"\n68: - \"release readiness check\" / \"pre-release review\"\n69: - \"find misalignments\" (between spec and implementation)\n70: - \"verify cross-references\" (across docs and code)\n71: - \"deep review\" / \"iterative review\" / \"review loop\"\n72: - \"quality audit\" / \"convergence detection\"\n73: \n74: ### Keyword Triggers\n75: \n76: `deep review`, `convergence review`, `iterative review`, `review loop`, `release readiness`, `spec folder review`, `convergence detection`, `quality audit`, `find misalignments`, `verify cross-references`, `pre-release review`, `audit spec folder`\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n81: \n82: The `system-deep-loop` hub routes an iterative review loop here, and its `review` mode signal selects this packet.\n83: The signal fires when a request names a deep review, a convergence review, a review loop, a release readiness check or a request to audit the diff.\n84: The loop runs only through `/deep:review`, whose workflow owns state, dispatch and convergence.\n85: \n86: `references/protocol/quick-reference.md` loads first on every invocation.\n87: The review phase named by the dispatch context then selects the loop protocol, the convergence documents or the state documents.\n88: \n89: The routing pseudocode in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) is the one route from a request to a resource set.\n90: A request whose intent scores stay under the threshold returns `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK` with a disambiguation checklist, never a silent default.\n91: Read [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting skill-local resources; open only the matched files.\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n96: \n97: ### Architecture\n98: \n99: `/deep:review` owns the loop. The YAML workflow initializes state, dispatches one LEAF review iteration at a time, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `review-report.md`, and saves continuity. The LEAF agent reads state, reviews one dimension, writes `iteration-NNN.md`, updates strategy, and appends JSONL. Full 4-phase lifecycle: `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`.\n100: \n101: ### Resource Map Coverage Gate\n102: \n103: When `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` exists at init, it is a mandatory audit input: one iteration audits `target_files` coverage against it, and synthesis adds the `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` report section. `--no-resource-map` disables this, and an absent map skips it without failing the loop.\n104: Full sequencing: `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` (init 9a, iteration 3b, synthesis 4). Schema: `references/state/state-format.md`.\n105: \n106: ### Bounded Context Snapshot Replacement\n107: \n108: During initialization, capture a bounded, pointer-based context snapshot in `deep-review-strategy.md` `Known Context` before the first dimension runs: target pointers, the claimed behavior to verify, reuse pointers and risk areas.\n109: Do not create a context-loop report or widen scope beyond the declared target.\n110: \n111: ### State Packet Location\n112: \n113: The review state packet always lives under the target spec's local `review/` folder.\n114: Root-spec targets use `{spec_folder}/review/` directly.\n115: Child-phase and sub-phase targets use **flat-first** placement: the first run writes flat, and a `pt-NN` sibling packet is allocated only when prior content already exists for a different target.\n116: Full resolution rule and worked examples: `references/state/state-format.md` §1.\n117: \n118: Core artifacts: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, `.deep-review-pause`, `resource-map.md`, `review-report.md`, and `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\n119: \n120: The loop writes `review/review-report.md` itself at synthesis from the findings registry and the JSONL state; `create.sh --level review` is only for a review packet authored by hand.\n121: \n122: ### Core Innovation: Fresh Context Per Iteration\n123: \n124: Each agent dispatch gets a fresh context window; state continuity comes from files, not memory, preventing accumulated findings from biasing later dimensions. Init writes config/strategy/JSONL; each loop reads state, checks convergence, dispatches one dimension, records findings, and reduces state; synthesis compiles the report and saves continuity.\n125: \n126: ### Review Dimensions\n127: \n128: The four primary review dimensions (configured in `assets/review-mode-contract.yaml`; configure them by the id in parentheses, because any other name counts as a custom dimension):\n129: \n130: | Dimension | Focus | Key Questions |\n131: |-----------|-------|---------------|\n132: | **Correctness** (`correctness`) | Logic, behavior, error handling | Behavior matches claims? Edge cases handled? |\n133: | **Security** (`security`) | Vulnerabilities, exposure, trust boundaries | Inputs validated? Credentials exposed? |\n134: | **Spec-Alignment / Traceability** (`traceability`) | Spec vs. implementation fidelity | Code matches spec.md? Planned items present? |\n135: | **Completeness / Maintainability** (`maintainability`) | Coverage, dead code, documentation | TODOs resolved? Code self-documenting? |\n136: \n137: ### Lifecycle + Reducer Contract\n138: \n139: Review mode is lineage-aware.\n140: \n141: - **Lifecycle modes:** `new`, `resume`, `restart`, and `completed-continue` (set by `--extend=N` on a completed run; see `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`).\n142: - **Required lineage fields:** `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, and `releaseReadinessState`.\n143: - **Reducer contract:** consumes the latest JSONL delta, the new iteration file, and prior reduced state, then emits finding registry, dashboard metrics, and strategy updates.\n144: \n145: ### Severity Classification\n146: \n147: | Severity | Criteria | Blocking |\n148: |----------|----------|---------|\n149: | **P0** | Correctness failure, security vulnerability, spec contradiction | Yes, blocks PASS verdict |\n150: | **P1** | Degraded behavior, incomplete implementation, missing validation | Conditional, triggers CONDITIONAL verdict |\n151: | **P2** | Style, naming, minor improvements, documentation gaps | No, PASS with advisories |\n152: \n153: P0 and P1 also follow the reach calibration in `sk-code-review`'s `references/review-core.md` §2.\n154: A blocking finding names an input or call path the code's stated contract allows, or a real caller that sends the failing input.\n155: \"Missing validation\" is P1 only when the unvalidated input is in reach. Validation the code never claimed, for input outside its stated contract, is P2 hardening.\n156: At a trust boundary every value the outside can send is in reach.\n157: \n158: The scale has exactly three tiers, and no fourth is reserved.\n159: A severity outside P0/P1/P2 is not a fourth tier. That covers a `P3` inherited from an older four-level convention, and any unlisted word.\n160: Collapse it to the tier its impact actually matches (a `P3` becomes `P2`) and keep the original rating visible in the finding, so the rating is converted rather than lost.\n161: An unconverted out-of-scale severity reaches the cross-lineage merge unranked, where it sorts below every P2 and cannot raise the merged verdict.\n162: \n163: ### Verdicts\n164: \n165: | Verdict | Condition |\n166: |---------|-----------|\n167: | **PASS** | No P0/P1 findings and no open search debt, P2 findings recorded as advisories (`hasAdvisories: true`) |\n168: | **CONDITIONAL** | P1 findings present, or open search debt remains, with remediation plan included in report |\n169: | **FAIL** | Any P0 finding confirmed after adversarial self-check, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop |\n170: \n171: ### Acceptance-Coverage Signal\n172: \n173: When the review target is a spec folder, deep review reflects the `AC_COVERAGE` validation signal in synthesis for Level 2+ folders.\n174: The signal applies only once `checklist.md` exists and `implementation-summary.md` is in-progress or later. Level 1 folders and fresh scaffolds are exempt.\n175: It is advisory while the validation rule stays INFO/default-on (non-blocking, and `RULE_STATUS` stays `pass`).\n176: It can add traceability context and planning-seed work, but must not alter the iteration final-line contract below unless a later enforcement rollout explicitly changes severity.\n177: \n178: ### Iteration Final-Line Contract (MANDATORY)\n179: \n180: Every `iteration-NNN.md` MUST end with exactly one of the following plain-text lines as the **absolute final line** (no trailing whitespace, no variation), and every review MUST emit exactly one parseable verdict:\n181: \n182: ```\n183: Review verdict: PASS\n184: ```\n185: \n186: ```\n187: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n188: ```\n189: \n190: ```\n191: Review verdict: FAIL\n192: ```\n193: \n194: **Mapping rule:** PASS if no P0 or P1 findings in this iteration. CONDITIONAL if any P1 (but no P0) findings. FAIL if any P0 findings. P2-only findings → PASS.\n195: \n196: **VERDICT_LOCK:** Any confirmed active P0 forces the exact final line `Review verdict: FAIL` -- never relabel that state as conditional, partial, mixed, or advisory, and truncated/partial output is not a valid substitute for the final line. An optional advisory `riskScore` may appear in narratives/JSONL for relative risk calibration but never changes the `PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` mapping.\n197: \n198: Downstream automation (including the synthesis phase and CI gate parser) parses this final line via exact string match, do not vary the format.\n199: \n200: **What the check proves:** the post-dispatch verifier validates the *shape* of this line, and nothing more: exactly one well-formed verdict line, and it is final.\n201: It does not read findings, so a `PASS` written above active P1 findings satisfies it, and no parser here makes the line true.\n202: The verdict a release decision reads is recomputed from the findings registry.\n203: In a fan-out run the cross-lineage merge is the authoritative rollup, where any active P0, or any lineage's required quality gate still failing at its stop, becomes a merged FAIL.\n204: Treat the final line as the leaf's self-report and the registry as the record.\n205: \n206: ### Executor Selection Contract\n207: \n208: Executor settings are owned by the YAML workflow and rendered prompt pack -- never hand-dispatch review iterations; each iteration stays LEAF-only and produces the required markdown plus JSONL delta. Full contract (per-iteration invariants, failure modes, JSONL audit field, config surface/precedence, TrustState surface): `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`.\n209: \n210: ### Stop Decision, Counters and Limits\n211: \n212: `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` computes the whole stop decision once per pass from the config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. `deep-review.yaml` renders no stop arithmetic of its own. The frozen stop reasons are `converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `manualStop`, `error`, `stuckRecovery`, `userPaused` and `maxDurationReached`. A missing graph decision blocks every non-terminal STOP.\n213: \n214: The stuck count and the consecutive failure count are rebuilt from the state log on every pass, so a resumed run counts the same as one that never paused. Under expansive depth with an active frontier node, the stuck count reads only that node's bound rows, and a bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress whatever its ratio. Failed iterations stay out of the ratio signals. Three trailing failed iterations stop the loop with stop reason `error`. In confirm mode only, the workflow first asks the operator Retry, Skip or Cancel. Auto mode has no such question.\n215: \n216: Each pass also compares `maxDurationMinutes` with the config `createdAt`. When the limit is reached the loop skips the dispatch and goes to synthesis with stop reason `maxDurationReached`.\n217: \n218: ### Expansive Depth Mode\n219: \n220: - `--depth-mode=expansive` is opt-in. It seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1 and grows them only through admitted `frontier_proposal` rows, stored in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`. An absent flag (`default`) runs exactly as before.\n221: - A defaulted `--max-iterations` is derived from the seed, up to 24, and an explicit value always wins.\n222: - While a node is open or active, the frontier veto turns a stop candidate into `CONTINUE` with reasonDetail `frontierOpen`. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the review floor.\n223: - Caps, budget arithmetic, admission checks, dimension steering, `frontier_drained` and fan-out partitioning: [loop-protocol.md](references/protocol/loop-protocol.md) §Expansive Depth Frontier and [convergence.md](references/convergence/convergence.md) §Expansive Depth Mode.\n224: \n225: ---\n226: \n227: ## 4. RULES\n228: \n229: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n230: \n231: 1. Read JSONL and strategy before review action.\n232: 2. Review one dimension per iteration and write findings to `iteration-NNN.md`.\n233: 3. Append JSONL with severity counts, finding detail, and `newInfoRatio`.\n234: 4. Cite every finding with `[SOURCE: file:line]`. Reject inference-only findings.\n235: 5. Re-read cited code before recording any P0.\n236: 6. Keep target files read-only.\n237: 7. Use `generate-context.js` for continuity saves. **Owner**: the workflow (`deep-review.yaml`) calls it at the save phase, not the reducer (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`) directly — don't expect continuity-save side effects from the reducer alone.\n238: 8. Emit setup `BINDING:` lines before workflow output.\n239: 9. Refuse nested dispatch with: `REFUSE: nested Task tool dispatch is forbidden for LEAF agents. Returning partial findings instead.`\n240: \n241: ### ⛔ NEVER\n242: \n243: 1. **Dispatch sub-agents**, `@deep-review` is LEAF-only. It cannot dispatch additional agents. When dispatch is requested, use the canonical REFUSE wording (ALWAYS rule 9).\n244: 2. **Hold findings in context**, Write everything to iteration files. Context is discarded after each dispatch.\n245: 3. **Exceed TCB**, Stay within `config.maxToolCallsPerIteration` tool calls per iteration. Breadth over depth per cycle.\n246: 4. **Ask the user**, The leaf agent never asks. It makes best-judgment decisions without pausing. The workflow asks only in `:confirm` mode, at its approval gates.\n247: 5. **Skip convergence checks**, Every iteration must be evaluated against convergence criteria before the next dispatch.\n248: 6. **Modify config after init**, review parameters in `deep-review-config.json` are read-only after initialization, apart from the workflow's own writes that `references/state/state-format.md` lists: the terminal status flip, `--extend=N`, `step_frontier_scope`, `step_frontier_budget` and a fan-out rerun's `step_fanout_root_config`.\n249: 7. **Modify files under review**, The review loop is observation-only. No code changes during audit.\n250: 8. **Use WebFetch**, Review is code-only. No external resource fetching is permitted.\n251: 9. **Implement fixes during review**, Report findings only. Implementation is a separate follow-up step.\n252: \n253: ### Iteration Status Enum\n254: \n255: `complete | timeout | error | stuck | insight | thought`\n256: \n257: - `insight`: Low newInfoRatio but important finding that changes the verdict trajectory.\n258: \n259: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n260: \n261: 1. **3+ consecutive failed iterations**, The loop stops with stop reason `error` and enters synthesis with partial findings. In confirm mode the workflow asks Retry, Skip or Cancel first.\n262: 2. **State file corruption**, Cannot reconstruct iteration history from JSONL or iteration files.\n263: 3. **All dimensions covered with P0 findings remaining**, Human sign-off required before shipping.\n264: 4. **Security vulnerabilities discovered in production code**, Escalate immediately. Do not defer to report synthesis.\n265: 5. **All recovery tiers exhausted**, No automatic recovery path remaining in convergence protocol.\n266: \n267: ---\n268: \n269: ## 5. REFERENCES\n270: \n271: The router discovers reference, asset and script docs dynamically.\n272: Start with these, in order:\n273: \n274: 1. `references/protocol/quick-reference.md`\n275: 2. `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`\n276: 3. `references/convergence/convergence.md`\n277: 4. `references/convergence/convergence-signals.md`\n278: 5. `references/state/state-format.md`\n279: 6. `references/state/state-outputs.md`\n280: 7. `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md`\n281: 8. `assets/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n282: 9. `assets/deep-review-strategy.md`\n283: \n284: Then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/`, and automation from `scripts/` when present.\n285: \n286: Scripts: `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, `scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`.\n287: \n288: Detailed contracts:\n289: \n290: - `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`: executor invariants, failure modes and config surface.\n291: - `references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md`: state transitions, error handling and STOP-decision gates.\n292: - `references/protocol/completion-criteria.md`: the full loop-completion, quality-gate and validation-success checklist.\n293: - `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md`: two-tier content-hash dedup.\n294: \n295: ---\n296: \n297: ## 6. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n298: \n299: A review loop is complete only when convergence and every quality gate agree.\n300: All of these must hold:\n301: \n302: - The composite stop score clears `compositeStopScore`, or `maxIterations` is hit without a false-positive STOP.\n303: - Every configured dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage, plus the core traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) when traceability is among the configured dimensions. An absent dimension list means the default four, which include it.\n304: - All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md` and `deep-review-dashboard.md` (a fan-out run keeps one per lineage instead), plus one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n305: - `review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate`.\n306: - Continuity is saved via `generate-context.js`.\n307: \n308: Nine binary quality gates, from config validity through adversarial P0 replay and acceptance coverage, must all pass before STOP is legal.\n309: The security-sensitive override also applies when the target touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence or shared policy (`minStabilizationPasses=2` plus fix-completeness replay).\n310: Full gate-by-gate criteria and rationale: `references/protocol/completion-criteria.md`.\n311: \n312: Validate a completed run with `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` (skill still surfaces) and `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` (exits 0).\n313: \n314: ---\n315: \n316: ## 7. INTEGRATION POINTS\n317: \n318: ### Framework Integration\n319: \n320: This skill operates within the behavioral framework defined in the active runtime's root doc (CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md).\n321: \n322: Key integrations:\n323: - **Gate 2**: Skill routing via `skill_advisor.py` (keywords: deep review, convergence review, iterative review)\n324: - **Gate 3**: File modifications require spec folder question per the root doc Gate 3. The spec folder determines the `{spec_folder}/review/` state packet location\n325: - **Continuity**: `/speckit:resume` is the operator-facing recovery surface, resolving context in the order `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`. During review, the agent writes iteration, strategy, and JSONL state; after synthesis, run `generate-context.js` to write canonical packet continuity\n326: - **Command**: `/deep:review` is the primary invocation point\n327: \n328: ### Code Graph Integration\n329: \n330: The review loop consumes the shared runtime graph and its strict mode-gate validator; packet-specific convergence and state rules remain in this skill.\n331: \n332: ### Related Skills\n333: \n334: Related skills: `deep-research` for investigation loops, `sk-code`'s code-review mode for single-pass review doctrine, and `system-spec-kit` for command-owned state and continuity saves."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795201550083,"end":1795201550098}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201550101,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa59c7040018MWHrIc6Fxw5Kw","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa59b59c0012zRFbnI863KuIL","type":"tool","id":"call_c3857cd7c336f40cfad23796","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek"},"output":"Read directory specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek, entries 1-7\n.executor-state/\ncontainment/\ndeep-review-audit-ledger/\ndeep-review-effect-ledger/\nlocks-and-fencing-v1/\nfrontier-nodes.jsonl\ninvocation-metadata.json","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read directory specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek, entries 1-7\n.executor-state/\ncontainment/\ndeep-review-audit-ledger/\ndeep-review-effect-ledger/\nlocks-and-fencing-v1/\nfrontier-nodes.jsonl\ninvocation-metadata.json"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek\"}"},"time":{"start":1795201550084,"end":1795201550101}}}}
