{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201555211,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa59d9bd002RXCRNFdhBwSUcZ","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa59d437001fgIXVR9zBcAwJw","type":"tool","id":"call_5c698e77b9d3c8b0e3ed4128","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml","offset":676,"limit":700},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 676-1259\n676:                 find \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name \"$(basename \"{state_paths.lock_file}\")\" -exec mv {} \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}/\" \\; || exit 1\n677:                 mkdir -p \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}\" \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}\" \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n678:               on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n679:               set:\n680:                 lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n681:               skip_to: step_create_config\n682:             on_cancel_choice:\n683:               halt: true\n684:               release_lock: step_release_lock\n685:               message: \"Review session preserved. Manually archive or edit review/ before re-running.\"\n686:         on_restart:\n687:           action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n688:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork is deferred and not runtime-supported in this release.\"\n689:         note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n690:         on_moved_legacy_state:\n691:           applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n692:           order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n693:           note: |\n694:             The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n695:             gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n696:             open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n697:             which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n698:             and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n699:           set_aside_command: |\n700:             STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n701:             LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n702:             if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n703:               echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n704:               exit 1\n705:             fi\n706:             mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n707:           open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n708:           replay_command: |\n709:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n710:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n711:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n712:             node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" replay-legacy-review \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n713:         on_completed_session:\n714:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n715:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n716:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n717:         on_invalid_state:\n718:           halt: true\n719:           release_lock: step_release_lock\n720:           message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n721:         on_fresh:\n722:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n723: \n724:       step_scope_discovery:\n725:         action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n726:         resolve:\n727:           spec-folder: |\n728:             1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n729:             2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n730:             3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n731:             4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n732:             5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n733:             6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n734:           skill: |\n735:             1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n736:             2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n737:             3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n738:             4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n739:             5. Set scope = all discovered files\n740:           agent: |\n741:             1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n742:             2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n743:             3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n744:           track: |\n745:             1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n746:             2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n747:             3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n748:           files: |\n749:             1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n750:             2. Validate all files exist\n751:             3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n752:             4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n753:         outputs:\n754:           - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n755:           - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n756: \n757:       step_order_dimensions:\n758:         action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n759:         algorithm: |\n760:           1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n761:           2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n762:              correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n763:           3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n764:           4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n765:              - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n766:              - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n767:           5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n768:           6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n769:         outputs:\n770:           - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n771:           - inventory_pass: true\n772: \n773:       step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n774:         action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n775:         outputs:\n776:           - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n777:           - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n778:           - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n779:           - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n780:         normalize: |\n781:           Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n782:             - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n783:             - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n784:             - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n785:             - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n786:           Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n787: \n788:       step_normalize_review_focus:\n789:         action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n790:         outputs:\n791:           - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n792:         normalize: |\n793:           Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n794:           fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n795: \n796:       step_resolve_session_id:\n797:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n798:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n799:         if_present:\n800:           bind:\n801:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n802:         if_absent:\n803:           bind:\n804:             session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n805: \n806:       step_create_config:\n807:         action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n808:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n809:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n810:         lineage_values:\n811:           generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n812:           lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n813:           parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n814:         populate:\n815:           topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n816:           mode: \"review\"\n817:           sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n818:           parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n819:           lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n820:           generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n821:           continuedFromRun: null\n822:           reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n823:           reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n824:           # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n825:           reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n826:           # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n827:           reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n828:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n829:           reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n830:           severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n831:           crossReference:\n832:             core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n833:             overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n834:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n835:           # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n836:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n837:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n838:           antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n839:           # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n840:           expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n841:           expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n842:           expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n843:           # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n844:           expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n845:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n846:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n847:           stuckThreshold: 2\n848:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n849:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n850:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n851:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n852:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n853:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n854:           status: \"initialized\"\n855:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n856:           executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n857:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n858: \n859:       step_frontier_scope:\n860:         description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n861:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n862:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n863:         note: |\n864:           Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n865:           commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n866:           list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n867:           <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n868:           label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n869:           too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n870:           other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n871:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n872:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n873:         outputs:\n874:           - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n875:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n876: \n877:       step_frontier_seed:\n878:         description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n879:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n880:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n881:         skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n882:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n883:         instructions: |\n884:           Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n885:           exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n886:           The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n887:           a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n888:           only once its config exists.\n889:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n890:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n891:         outputs:\n892:           - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n893:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n894: \n895:       step_frontier_budget:\n896:         description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n897:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n898:         skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n899:         skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n900:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n901:         note: |\n902:           The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n903:           is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n904:           where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n905:           traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n906:           custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n907:           the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n908:           A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n909:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n910:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n911:         outputs:\n912:           - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n913:           - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n914:         on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n915:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n916: \n917:       step_create_state_log:\n918:         action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n919:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n920:         note: |\n921:           The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n922:           it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n923:           rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n924:           commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n925:           the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n926:           in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n927:         command: |\n928:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n929:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n930:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n931:           node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n932:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n933:           STATUS=$?\n934:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n935:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n936:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n937: \n938:       step_record_restarted_run:\n939:         skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n940:         action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n941:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n942:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n943: \n944:       step_create_findings_registry:\n945:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n946:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n947:         content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n948:         output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n949: \n950:       step_create_strategy:\n951:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n952:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n953:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n954:         populate:\n955:           review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n956:           review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n957:           dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n958:           scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n959:           cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n960:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n961:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n962:           stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n963:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n964: \n965:       step_seed_coverage_graph:\n966:         action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n967:         fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n968:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n969:         transform: |\n970:           1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n971:           2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n972:              or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n973:           3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n974:           4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n975:           5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n976:              returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n977:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n978:         outputs:\n979:           - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n980:           - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n981:           - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n982:         on_warning:\n983:           log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n984:           proceed: true\n985: \n986:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n987:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n988:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n989:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n990:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n991:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n992: \n993:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n994:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n995:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n996:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n997:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n998: \n999:       step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n1000:         action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n1001:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n1002:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1003:         note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n1004:         command: |\n1005:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1006:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1007:         on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n1008: \n1009:       step_init_complete:\n1010:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n1011:         set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n1012: \n1013:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n1014:       gate_init_approval:\n1015:         applies_to: confirm\n1016:         type: approval_gate\n1017:         purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n1018:         present: |\n1019:           ## Review Initialization Complete\n1020: \n1021:           **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n1022:           **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n1023:           **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n1024:           **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n1025:           **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n1026:           **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n1027: \n1028:           **Files in scope:**\n1029:           {review_scope_files_summary}\n1030: \n1031:           Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n1032:           **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n1033: \n1034:           Options:\n1035:           A) Start review loop\n1036:           B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n1037:           C) Cancel\n1038:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1039:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1040:         on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1041:         on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n1042:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1043: \n1044:   # ════════\n1045:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n1046:   # ════════\n1047:   phase_loop:\n1048:     purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n1049:     repeat: true\n1050:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1051:     steps:\n1052: \n1053:       step_refresh_lock:\n1054:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n1055:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1056:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n1057: \n1058:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n1059:         action: \"Record the legacy review state move once per session, after the run is open\"\n1060:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1061:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n1062:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.migration\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"legacyArtifacts\":[\"deep-research-config.json\",\"deep-research-state.jsonl\",\".deep-research-pause\"],\"canonicalArtifacts\":[\"deep-review-config.json\",\"deep-review-state.jsonl\",\".deep-review-pause\"]}}'\n1063:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n1064: \n1065:       step_read_state:\n1066:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n1067:         read:\n1068:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1069:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1070:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1071:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1072:         extract:\n1073:           - iteration_count: \"Count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration'; a redispatched run counts once\"\n1074:           - highest_run: \"Highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration', else 0\"\n1075:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1076:           - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n1077:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n1078:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n1079:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n1080:           - traceability_in_run: \"true when reviewDimensions in deep-review-config.json is absent, which means the default four dimensions, or contains 'traceability'; false when it is a list without it\"\n1081:           - next_dimension: \"When max_iterations >= 2, current_iteration == max_iterations, unfinished_core_protocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, 'traceability': the last iteration under the cap finishes those core protocols. Otherwise, when depth_mode == 'expansive' and registry.frontier.activeNextDimension in {state_paths.findings_registry} is non-empty, that dimension: the active frontier node's next uncovered dimension. Otherwise the next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md.\"\n1082:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n1083:           - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n1084:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n1085:           - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n1086:           - p0_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P0 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, the reducer's deduplicated count of open findings, else 0\"\n1087:           - p1_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P1 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, else 0\"\n1088:           - p2_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P2 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, else 0\"\n1089:           - unfinished_core_protocols: \"registry.traceability.unfinishedCoreProtocols from {state_paths.findings_registry} as a JSON array, else []\"\n1090:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n1091:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n1092:           - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n1093:           - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n1094:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n1095:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n1096:           - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n1097:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n1098:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n1099:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n1100:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n1101:           - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n1102:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n1103:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n1104:           - depth_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.depthMode when it is 'expansive'; any other or missing value is 'default'\"\n1105:           - active_frontier_node: \"When depth_mode == 'expansive', registry.frontier.activeNodeId from {state_paths.findings_registry}; else, or when it is null, an empty string\"\n1106:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n1107:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n1108:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n1109:           - unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"Under the same condition as next_dimension's traceability case, return 'This is the last iteration under the cap. Finish these core traceability protocols: <ids, comma-separated>. Record one traceabilityChecks.results[] entry for each. A result raised from partial to pass needs a file:line reference in evidenceRefs, or it stays partial.' Else return an empty string.\"\n1110: \n1111:       step_check_max_duration:\n1112:         action: \"Stop the loop when the run has used its wall-clock budget, and still synthesize\"\n1113:         command: |\n1114:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs max-duration \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1115:         outputs:\n1116:           - duration_reached: \"reached from the JSON output\"\n1117:           - elapsed_minutes: \"elapsedMinutes from the JSON output\"\n1118:         note: \"The clock starts at the createdAt of the current generation's config. A resume keeps it and a restart resets it, so paused and waiting time counts.\"\n1119:         if_reached:\n1120:           when: \"duration_reached == true\"\n1121:           set: { decision: \"STOP\", reason: \"maxDurationReached\", stopReason: \"maxDurationReached\" }\n1122:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"elapsedMinutes\":{elapsed_minutes},\"maxDurationMinutes\":{config.maxDurationMinutes},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1123:           log: \"Duration limit reached after {elapsed_minutes} minutes. Skipping dispatch and entering synthesis with partial findings.\"\n1124:           run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1125:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1126:           note: \"The stop row is printed, not appended: the gateway refuses an event it has no ledger stem for. The reason reaches the synthesis report through the bound reason.\"\n1127:         if_not_reached:\n1128:           action: \"Continue with the iteration\"\n1129: \n1130:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n1131:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n1132:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n1133:         if_exists:\n1134:           set:\n1135:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n1136:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n1137:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n1138:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n1139:         if_not_exists:\n1140:           proceed: true\n1141: \n1142:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n1143:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n1144:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n1145:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1146:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1147:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n1148: \n1149:       step_graph_convergence:\n1150:         action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n1151:         fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1152:         inspect:\n1153:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1154:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1155:         transform: |\n1156:           1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n1157:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n1158:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n1159:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n1160:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n1161:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --depth-mode \"{depth_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" {convergence_write_arg}'\n1162:         note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output. On a BLOCKED decision, {convergence_write_arg} passes --record-blocked-stop on a live run, which makes the script append the deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded event for this iteration through the append gateway itself, once per iteration and blocker set, so a leaf that never reaches step_emit_blocked_stop still leaves the block in the ledger. It records on an empty graph and on a graph that cannot be read as well. The event names graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}, the graph_convergence_evaluated event this step appends after the script returns. A dry run binds {convergence_write_arg} to --read-only, so the script appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event.\"\n1163:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n1164:         dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1165:         on_missing_counters: \"If loop_counters_json is missing from the output, halt with stop reason error. Never bind a default counter. Run step_release_lock before the halt returns control.\"\n1166:         outputs:\n1167:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1168:           - stop_decision: \"Tool stop_decision object: decision, stopReason, reasonDetail, weightedStopScore, signals, gates, blockedBy, graphDecision, inputs\"\n1169:           - loop_counters_json: \"Tool loop_counters_json object: stuckCount and consecutiveFailureCount, both rebuilt from the state log on this pass; under expansive depth stuckCount counts only the active frontier node's own iterations\"\n1170:           - stuck_count: \"loop_counters_json.stuckCount\"\n1171:           - consecutive_failure_count: \"loop_counters_json.consecutiveFailureCount\"\n1172:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n1173:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n1174:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n1175:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n1176:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n1177:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n1178:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1179:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n1180:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n1181:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n1182:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n1183:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n1184:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n1185:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n1186:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n1187:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n1188:           - blocked_stop_record: \"Present only when stop_decision.decision == BLOCKED: status recorded, already_recorded or failed, the run, the recoveryStrategy code, the recoveryHint and the gateResults rows the event carries.\"\n1189:         on_blocked_stop_record_failed: \"When blocked_stop_record.status == failed the script exits with the gateway status after printing the decision. Treat it as a gateway refusal under state_write_protocol.refusal_handling: halt, and never write the event by hand.\"\n1190: \n1191:       step_check_convergence:\n1192:         action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n1193:         algorithm: |\n1194:           The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n1195:           The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n1196:           The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n1197:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n1198:           1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n1199:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n1200:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n1201:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n1202:           4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n1203:           4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n1204:           4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n1205:           5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n1206:           6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n1207:           Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n1208:             decision = stop_decision.decision\n1209:             stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n1210:             reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1211:             reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1212:             weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n1213:             stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n1214:             blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n1215:             blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n1216:             convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n1217:             convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n1218:             dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n1219:             dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1220:             dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1221:             p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n1222:             active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n1223:             evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n1224:             avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n1225:             hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n1226:             claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n1227:             claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n1228:             fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n1229:             security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n1230:             fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n1231:             fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n1232:             candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n1233:             candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n1234:             candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n1235:             graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n1236:             graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n1237:             graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n1238:             graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n1239:             graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n1240:             recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy: blocked_stop_record.recoveryHint when present, else built as follows. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, also say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n1241:           If stop_decision is missing from the step_graph_convergence output, do not decide by hand: halt and report the script output.\n1242:         outputs:\n1243:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n1244:           - reason: \"stop_decision.stopReason when set, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\"\n1245:           - reason_detail: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail, the fine cause behind the decision\"\n1246:           - weighted_stop_score: \"stop_decision.weightedStopScore, for diagnostics only\"\n1247:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1248:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1249:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1250:           - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n1251:           - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n1252:           - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n1253:           - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n1254:           - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n1255:           - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n1256:           - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n1257:           - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n1258:           - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n1259:           - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1260]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 676-1259\n676:                 find \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name \"$(basename \"{state_paths.lock_file}\")\" -exec mv {} \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}/\" \\; || exit 1\n677:                 mkdir -p \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}\" \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}\" \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n678:               on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n679:               set:\n680:                 lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n681:               skip_to: step_create_config\n682:             on_cancel_choice:\n683:               halt: true\n684:               release_lock: step_release_lock\n685:               message: \"Review session preserved. Manually archive or edit review/ before re-running.\"\n686:         on_restart:\n687:           action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n688:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork is deferred and not runtime-supported in this release.\"\n689:         note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n690:         on_moved_legacy_state:\n691:           applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n692:           order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n693:           note: |\n694:             The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n695:             gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n696:             open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n697:             which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n698:             and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n699:           set_aside_command: |\n700:             STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n701:             LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n702:             if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n703:               echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n704:               exit 1\n705:             fi\n706:             mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n707:           open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n708:           replay_command: |\n709:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n710:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n711:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n712:             node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" replay-legacy-review \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n713:         on_completed_session:\n714:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n715:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n716:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n717:         on_invalid_state:\n718:           halt: true\n719:           release_lock: step_release_lock\n720:           message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n721:         on_fresh:\n722:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n723: \n724:       step_scope_discovery:\n725:         action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n726:         resolve:\n727:           spec-folder: |\n728:             1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n729:             2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n730:             3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n731:             4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n732:             5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n733:             6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n734:           skill: |\n735:             1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n736:             2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n737:             3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n738:             4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n739:             5. Set scope = all discovered files\n740:           agent: |\n741:             1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n742:             2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n743:             3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n744:           track: |\n745:             1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n746:             2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n747:             3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n748:           files: |\n749:             1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n750:             2. Validate all files exist\n751:             3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n752:             4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n753:         outputs:\n754:           - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n755:           - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n756: \n757:       step_order_dimensions:\n758:         action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n759:         algorithm: |\n760:           1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n761:           2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n762:              correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n763:           3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n764:           4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n765:              - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n766:              - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n767:           5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n768:           6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n769:         outputs:\n770:           - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n771:           - inventory_pass: true\n772: \n773:       step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n774:         action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n775:         outputs:\n776:           - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n777:           - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n778:           - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n779:           - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n780:         normalize: |\n781:           Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n782:             - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n783:             - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n784:             - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n785:             - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n786:           Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n787: \n788:       step_normalize_review_focus:\n789:         action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n790:         outputs:\n791:           - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n792:         normalize: |\n793:           Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n794:           fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n795: \n796:       step_resolve_session_id:\n797:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n798:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n799:         if_present:\n800:           bind:\n801:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n802:         if_absent:\n803:           bind:\n804:             session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n805: \n806:       step_create_config:\n807:         action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n808:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n809:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n810:         lineage_values:\n811:           generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n812:           lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n813:           parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n814:         populate:\n815:           topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n816:           mode: \"review\"\n817:           sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n818:           parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n819:           lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n820:           generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n821:           continuedFromRun: null\n822:           reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n823:           reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n824:           # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n825:           reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n826:           # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n827:           reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n828:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n829:           reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n830:           severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n831:           crossReference:\n832:             core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n833:             overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n834:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n835:           # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n836:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n837:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n838:           antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n839:           # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n840:           expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n841:           expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n842:           expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n843:           # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n844:           expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n845:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n846:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n847:           stuckThreshold: 2\n848:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n849:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n850:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n851:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n852:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n853:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n854:           status: \"initialized\"\n855:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n856:           executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n857:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n858: \n859:       step_frontier_scope:\n860:         description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n861:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n862:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n863:         note: |\n864:           Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n865:           commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n866:           list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n867:           <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n868:           label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n869:           too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n870:           other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n871:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n872:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n873:         outputs:\n874:           - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n875:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n876: \n877:       step_frontier_seed:\n878:         description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n879:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n880:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n881:         skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n882:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n883:         instructions: |\n884:           Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n885:           exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n886:           The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n887:           a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n888:           only once its config exists.\n889:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n890:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n891:         outputs:\n892:           - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n893:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n894: \n895:       step_frontier_budget:\n896:         description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n897:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n898:         skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n899:         skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n900:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n901:         note: |\n902:           The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n903:           is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n904:           where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n905:           traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n906:           custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n907:           the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n908:           A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n909:         command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n910:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n911:         outputs:\n912:           - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n913:           - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n914:         on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n915:         on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n916: \n917:       step_create_state_log:\n918:         action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n919:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n920:         note: |\n921:           The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n922:           it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n923:           rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n924:           commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n925:           the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n926:           in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n927:         command: |\n928:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n929:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n930:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n931:           node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n932:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n933:           STATUS=$?\n934:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n935:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n936:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n937: \n938:       step_record_restarted_run:\n939:         skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n940:         action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n941:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n942:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n943: \n944:       step_create_findings_registry:\n945:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n946:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n947:         content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n948:         output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n949: \n950:       step_create_strategy:\n951:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n952:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n953:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n954:         populate:\n955:           review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n956:           review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n957:           dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n958:           scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n959:           cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n960:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n961:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n962:           stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n963:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n964: \n965:       step_seed_coverage_graph:\n966:         action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n967:         fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n968:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n969:         transform: |\n970:           1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n971:           2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n972:              or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n973:           3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n974:           4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n975:           5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n976:              returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n977:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n978:         outputs:\n979:           - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n980:           - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n981:           - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n982:         on_warning:\n983:           log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n984:           proceed: true\n985: \n986:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n987:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n988:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n989:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n990:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n991:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n992: \n993:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n994:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n995:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n996:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n997:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n998: \n999:       step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n1000:         action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n1001:         enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n1002:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1003:         note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n1004:         command: |\n1005:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1006:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1007:         on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n1008: \n1009:       step_init_complete:\n1010:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n1011:         set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n1012: \n1013:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n1014:       gate_init_approval:\n1015:         applies_to: confirm\n1016:         type: approval_gate\n1017:         purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n1018:         present: |\n1019:           ## Review Initialization Complete\n1020: \n1021:           **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n1022:           **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n1023:           **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n1024:           **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n1025:           **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n1026:           **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n1027: \n1028:           **Files in scope:**\n1029:           {review_scope_files_summary}\n1030: \n1031:           Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n1032:           **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n1033: \n1034:           Options:\n1035:           A) Start review loop\n1036:           B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n1037:           C) Cancel\n1038:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1039:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1040:         on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1041:         on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n1042:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1043: \n1044:   # ════════\n1045:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n1046:   # ════════\n1047:   phase_loop:\n1048:     purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n1049:     repeat: true\n1050:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1051:     steps:\n1052: \n1053:       step_refresh_lock:\n1054:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n1055:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1056:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n1057: \n1058:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n1059:         action: \"Record the legacy review state move once per session, after the run is open\"\n1060:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1061:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n1062:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.migration\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"legacyArtifacts\":[\"deep-research-config.json\",\"deep-research-state.jsonl\",\".deep-research-pause\"],\"canonicalArtifacts\":[\"deep-review-config.json\",\"deep-review-state.jsonl\",\".deep-review-pause\"]}}'\n1063:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n1064: \n1065:       step_read_state:\n1066:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n1067:         read:\n1068:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1069:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1070:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1071:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1072:         extract:\n1073:           - iteration_count: \"Count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration'; a redispatched run counts once\"\n1074:           - highest_run: \"Highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration', else 0\"\n1075:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1076:           - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n1077:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n1078:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n1079:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n1080:           - traceability_in_run: \"true when reviewDimensions in deep-review-config.json is absent, which means the default four dimensions, or contains 'traceability'; false when it is a list without it\"\n1081:           - next_dimension: \"When max_iterations >= 2, current_iteration == max_iterations, unfinished_core_protocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, 'traceability': the last iteration under the cap finishes those core protocols. Otherwise, when depth_mode == 'expansive' and registry.frontier.activeNextDimension in {state_paths.findings_registry} is non-empty, that dimension: the active frontier node's next uncovered dimension. Otherwise the next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md.\"\n1082:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n1083:           - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n1084:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n1085:           - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n1086:           - p0_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P0 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, the reducer's deduplicated count of open findings, else 0\"\n1087:           - p1_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P1 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, else 0\"\n1088:           - p2_count: \"findingsBySeverity.P2 from {state_paths.findings_registry}, else 0\"\n1089:           - unfinished_core_protocols: \"registry.traceability.unfinishedCoreProtocols from {state_paths.findings_registry} as a JSON array, else []\"\n1090:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n1091:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n1092:           - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n1093:           - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n1094:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n1095:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n1096:           - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n1097:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n1098:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n1099:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n1100:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n1101:           - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n1102:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n1103:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n1104:           - depth_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.depthMode when it is 'expansive'; any other or missing value is 'default'\"\n1105:           - active_frontier_node: \"When depth_mode == 'expansive', registry.frontier.activeNodeId from {state_paths.findings_registry}; else, or when it is null, an empty string\"\n1106:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n1107:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n1108:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n1109:           - unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"Under the same condition as next_dimension's traceability case, return 'This is the last iteration under the cap. Finish these core traceability protocols: <ids, comma-separated>. Record one traceabilityChecks.results[] entry for each. A result raised from partial to pass needs a file:line reference in evidenceRefs, or it stays partial.' Else return an empty string.\"\n1110: \n1111:       step_check_max_duration:\n1112:         action: \"Stop the loop when the run has used its wall-clock budget, and still synthesize\"\n1113:         command: |\n1114:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs max-duration \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1115:         outputs:\n1116:           - duration_reached: \"reached from the JSON output\"\n1117:           - elapsed_minutes: \"elapsedMinutes from the JSON output\"\n1118:         note: \"The clock starts at the createdAt of the current generation's config. A resume keeps it and a restart resets it, so paused and waiting time counts.\"\n1119:         if_reached:\n1120:           when: \"duration_reached == true\"\n1121:           set: { decision: \"STOP\", reason: \"maxDurationReached\", stopReason: \"maxDurationReached\" }\n1122:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"elapsedMinutes\":{elapsed_minutes},\"maxDurationMinutes\":{config.maxDurationMinutes},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1123:           log: \"Duration limit reached after {elapsed_minutes} minutes. Skipping dispatch and entering synthesis with partial findings.\"\n1124:           run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1125:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1126:           note: \"The stop row is printed, not appended: the gateway refuses an event it has no ledger stem for. The reason reaches the synthesis report through the bound reason.\"\n1127:         if_not_reached:\n1128:           action: \"Continue with the iteration\"\n1129: \n1130:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n1131:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n1132:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n1133:         if_exists:\n1134:           set:\n1135:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n1136:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n1137:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n1138:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n1139:         if_not_exists:\n1140:           proceed: true\n1141: \n1142:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n1143:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n1144:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n1145:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1146:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1147:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n1148: \n1149:       step_graph_convergence:\n1150:         action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n1151:         fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1152:         inspect:\n1153:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1154:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1155:         transform: |\n1156:           1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n1157:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n1158:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n1159:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n1160:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n1161:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --depth-mode \"{depth_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" {convergence_write_arg}'\n1162:         note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output. On a BLOCKED decision, {convergence_write_arg} passes --record-blocked-stop on a live run, which makes the script append the deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded event for this iteration through the append gateway itself, once per iteration and blocker set, so a leaf that never reaches step_emit_blocked_stop still leaves the block in the ledger. It records on an empty graph and on a graph that cannot be read as well. The event names graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}, the graph_convergence_evaluated event this step appends after the script returns. A dry run binds {convergence_write_arg} to --read-only, so the script appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event.\"\n1163:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n1164:         dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1165:         on_missing_counters: \"If loop_counters_json is missing from the output, halt with stop reason error. Never bind a default counter. Run step_release_lock before the halt returns control.\"\n1166:         outputs:\n1167:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1168:           - stop_decision: \"Tool stop_decision object: decision, stopReason, reasonDetail, weightedStopScore, signals, gates, blockedBy, graphDecision, inputs\"\n1169:           - loop_counters_json: \"Tool loop_counters_json object: stuckCount and consecutiveFailureCount, both rebuilt from the state log on this pass; under expansive depth stuckCount counts only the active frontier node's own iterations\"\n1170:           - stuck_count: \"loop_counters_json.stuckCount\"\n1171:           - consecutive_failure_count: \"loop_counters_json.consecutiveFailureCount\"\n1172:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n1173:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n1174:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n1175:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n1176:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n1177:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n1178:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1179:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n1180:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n1181:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n1182:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n1183:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n1184:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n1185:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n1186:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n1187:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n1188:           - blocked_stop_record: \"Present only when stop_decision.decision == BLOCKED: status recorded, already_recorded or failed, the run, the recoveryStrategy code, the recoveryHint and the gateResults rows the event carries.\"\n1189:         on_blocked_stop_record_failed: \"When blocked_stop_record.status == failed the script exits with the gateway status after printing the decision. Treat it as a gateway refusal under state_write_protocol.refusal_handling: halt, and never write the event by hand.\"\n1190: \n1191:       step_check_convergence:\n1192:         action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n1193:         algorithm: |\n1194:           The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n1195:           The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n1196:           The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n1197:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n1198:           1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n1199:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n1200:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n1201:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n1202:           4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n1203:           4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n1204:           4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n1205:           5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n1206:           6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n1207:           Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n1208:             decision = stop_decision.decision\n1209:             stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n1210:             reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1211:             reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1212:             weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n1213:             stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n1214:             blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n1215:             blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n1216:             convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n1217:             convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n1218:             dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n1219:             dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1220:             dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1221:             p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n1222:             active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n1223:             evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n1224:             avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n1225:             hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n1226:             claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n1227:             claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n1228:             fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n1229:             security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n1230:             fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n1231:             fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n1232:             candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n1233:             candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n1234:             candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n1235:             graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n1236:             graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n1237:             graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n1238:             graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n1239:             graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n1240:             recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy: blocked_stop_record.recoveryHint when present, else built as follows. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, also say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n1241:           If stop_decision is missing from the step_graph_convergence output, do not decide by hand: halt and report the script output.\n1242:         outputs:\n1243:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n1244:           - reason: \"stop_decision.stopReason when set, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\"\n1245:           - reason_detail: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail, the fine cause behind the decision\"\n1246:           - weighted_stop_score: \"stop_decision.weightedStopScore, for diagnostics only\"\n1247:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1248:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1249:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1250:           - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n1251:           - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n1252:           - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n1253:           - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n1254:           - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n1255:           - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n1256:           - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n1257:           - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n1258:           - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n1259:           - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1260]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\", \"offset\": 676, \"limit\": 700}"},"time":{"start":1795201554877,"end":1795201555211}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201555298,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa59da19001NxZVg1KlqfyDPY","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa59d437001fgIXVR9zBcAwJw","type":"tool","id":"call_3ff68ee11c4ff21169a3a115","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -la specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/ && echo \"--- frontier-nodes ---\" && cat specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/frontier-nodes.jsonl && echo \"--- invocation-metadata ---\" && cat specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/invocation-metadata.json"},"output":"total 16\ndrwx------@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff   288 Nov 20 20:05 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 michelkerkmeester  staff   128 Nov 20 20:05 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff    64 Nov 20 20:05 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff    96 Nov 20 20:05 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff   224 Nov 20 20:05 deep-review-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff   224 Nov 20 20:05 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  2264 Nov 20 20:05 frontier-nodes.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff   481 Nov 20 20:05 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff    96 Nov 20 20:05 locks-and-fencing-v1\n--- frontier-nodes ---\n{\"nodeId\":\"F-1-002\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\",\"question\":\"Cross-CLI adapter contract and sandbox: is the adapter capability record true for every kind, does a requested sandbox mode reach codex, pi, dsh and harness argv, and is the opencode workspace-write default with compensating enforcement sound?\",\"status\":\"open\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":0,\"dedupeKey\":\"cross cli adapter contract and sandbox is the adapter capability record true for every kind does a requested sandbox mode reach codex pi dsh and harness argv and is the opencode workspace write default with compensating enforcement sound\"}\n{\"nodeId\":\"F-1-004\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts\",\"question\":\"Gateway identity: does the append gateway mint event id, idempotency key, producer and epoch for model-written review and research rows, and refuse a reused key with different content instead of replaying the old receipt?\",\"status\":\"open\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":0,\"dedupeKey\":\"gateway identity does the append gateway mint event id idempotency key producer and epoch for model written review and research rows and refuse a reused key with different content instead of replaying the old receipt\"}\n{\"nodeId\":\"F-1-006\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":\".skilled/commands/deep .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog\",\"question\":\"Docs and contracts: do the command docs, compiled contracts, references, feature catalogs and playbooks describe what the round 5 and 6 code now does?\",\"status\":\"open\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":0,\"dedupeKey\":\"docs and contracts do the command docs compiled contracts references feature catalogs and playbooks describe what the round 5 and 6 code now does\"}\n--- invocation-metadata ---\n{\"effectiveConfig\":{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"executable\":\"opencode\",\"executableVersion\":