ps that write reads the configured budget.\n450:// A defaulted expansive budget is sized from the seed: two iterations for each node\n451:// on every level the frontier may still reach (the seeded nodes plus one node per\n455:// ceiling, which binds for a review from the first seed at the default depth. Twice the node count keeps the half-budget node cap\n456:// above the seed, so the frontier can still grow. A run or lineage with no seeded\n459: * Size a defaulted expansive iteration budget from the seed.\n463: * @param {number} options.seeded - Depth-1 nodes the seed admitted.\n467: * @returns {number} The iteration budget, between the floor and EXPANSIVE_BUDGET_CEILING.\n469:function expansiveBudget({ target, seeded, maxDepth = DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH, dimensions = CANONICAL_REVIEW_DIMENSIONS, loopDefault }) {\n472:  const seededCount = Math.max(0, Math.floor(seeded) || 0);\n473:  if (seededCount === 0) return floor;\n474:  const nodes = seededCount + Math.max(1, Math.floor(maxDepth) || 1) - 1;\n480:// leaves it out, plus any custom names. The budget counts that same set. Loaded on use, the way fanout-run loads this module.\n486:// The budget the run uses after the seed step, and how many nodes past depth 1 the\n487:// node cap still leaves. Only a defaulted budget is derived; a flag, marker, setup\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"12:// Seed, admit, prune and close all pass through this module. The one other\n16:// model executes: relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, monotone budget, acyclicity.\n20:// Only an admitted node reaches the inbox, and the inbox is the only path that\n24:// A review run reads the same store with the review config instead: an admitted\n50:// whether an admitted node queues a question.\n53:// A proposal's question and scope are written by a leaf and copied into later\n61:// The seed step decomposes a target into a documented number of depth-1 nodes:\n64: