{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201610545,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa5ab289001Vva9GVXK60vmNW","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa5aa8b4001g722Tp6lcODoX8","type":"tool","id":"call_83b987c8f3a7f079622de6fc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"executor_missing\\|invocation-metadata\\|executor\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs | head -40"},"output":"27:// When the run's config names a non-native executor, the iteration must also say\n28:// which executor ran it, on its own record or on its iteration_start row, so a run\n29:// whose executor audit never landed cannot pass as a verified iteration. A fan-out\n78:  EXECUTOR_MISSING: 'executor_missing',\n86:const INVOCATION_METADATA = 'invocation-metadata.json';\n355:// The run's executor kind comes from its config, read the way the executor audit\n356:// reads it: kind, then type, then native. A missing config or executor block means\n357:// nothing names a non-native executor, so there is nothing to check.\n365:  const executor = config && typeof config === 'object' ? config.executor : null;\n366:  if (!executor || typeof executor !== 'object' || Array.isArray(executor)) return { kind: null, config };\n367:  const kind = executor.kind ?? executor.type ?? 'native';\n372:// the per-iteration dispatch steps, the pre-dispatch executor audit among them, as\n373:// already satisfied. No executor row is written there, so a lineage is checked\n386:  return Boolean(record) && typeof record.executor === 'object' && record.executor !== null && !Array.isArray(record.executor);\n390:// of the lineage, and its effectiveConfig.kind is the executor it launched. Null\n402:// The pre-dispatch audit records a non-native executor before the leaf runs. On a\n415:      ? `lineage iteration ${iteration} ran under executor kind '${kind}' but ${INVOCATION_METADATA} names '${launched}'`\n416:      : `lineage iteration ${iteration} ran un