{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201631895,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa5afa5b001xYsobbvLY49ESv","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa5af3380010QvlWU72SnKJL4","type":"tool","id":"call_f27f43d15af56b42b6368dee","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the deepseek fan-out lineage of the expansive-depth review over the deep-loop runtime and command surface.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this review lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Populated from config and the bounded context snapshot.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned frontier node and dimension, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview: `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2 -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep` (88 changed files, commit-range target, review target type `files`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- No fixes, no source edits, no refactors: this loop is observation-only.\n- No review of files outside the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under the two pathspecs.\n- No web research and no external resource fetching.\n- No review of the `review/` packet artifacts themselves except as traceability evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence per `convergence.cjs` (composite weighted vote under `convergenceThreshold: 0.1`, all dimensions clean, frontier drained).\n- `maxIterations: 24` reached.\n- Stuck recovery (`stuckThreshold: 2`) or three consecutive failed iterations.\n- Wall-clock budget `maxDurationMinutes: 120` from `createdAt`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006 (all open, depth 1)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (cross-CLI adapter contract and sandbox)\n- Why: the lineage's first open depth-1 node; the adapter capability record and sandbox argv propagation are the highest-blast surface in the range.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` and `.skilled/commands/deep`. 88 files: runtime scripts (`append-mode-event.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `fanout-run.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, `synthesis-closeout.cjs`, `upsert.cjs`), runtime libs (`executor-config.ts`, `executor-audit.ts`, ledger schemas, legacy projections), command assets (`deep-review.yaml`, `deep-research.yaml`, compiled contracts, presentations), skill references and feature catalogs, manual-testing playbooks, and vitest suites.\n- Behavior claims to verify: the range's three commits claim (a) a dry-run convergence call stays read-only, (b) a review row mints identity and refuses a reused key with different content, (c) the blocked-stop record is withheld from a dry run. The expansive-depth frontier, fan-out lineage contract, and executor adapter capability record are the surrounding contracts those fixes touch.\n- Reuse and conventions: the append gateway is the single state-log writer; the reducer owns registry/dashboard/strategy projections; `frontier-admit.cjs` owns the node store; the YAML workflow is the stop-decision consumer and computes no arithmetic of its own.\n- Review risks and gaps: the range is a commit range, so `reviewScopeFiles` is the git diff list, not a glob expansion. Files deleted by the range have nothing to review. The compiled contract markdown is generated from the YAML, so drift between them is a traceability finding, not a code finding.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery; 88 files in scope, see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 24\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: files\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-20T19:07:02.024Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the deepseek fan-out lineage of the expansive-depth review over the deep-loop runtime and command surface.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this review lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** Populated from config and the bounded context snapshot.\\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned frontier node and dimension, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\\n- **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview: `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2 -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep` (88 changed files, commit-range target, review target type `files`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- No fixes, no source edits, no refactors: this loop is observation-only.\\n- No review of files outside the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under the two pathspecs.\\n- No web research and no external resource fetching.\\n- No review of the `review/` packet artifacts themselves except as traceability evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Legal convergence per `convergence.cjs` (composite weighted vote under `convergenceThreshold: 0.1`, all dimensions clean, frontier drained).\\n- `maxIterations: 24` reached.\\n- Stuck recovery (`stuckThreshold: 2`) or three consecutive failed iterations.\\n- Wall-clock budget `maxDurationMinutes: 120` from `createdAt`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006 (all open, depth 1)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (cross-CLI adapter contract and sandbox)\\n- Why: the lineage's first open depth-1 node; the adapter capability record and sandbox argv propagation are the highest-blast surface in the range.\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` and `.skilled/commands/deep`. 88 files: runtime scripts (`append-mode-event.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `fanout-run.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, `synthesis-closeout.cjs`, `upsert.cjs`), runtime libs (`executor-config.ts`, `executor-audit.ts`, ledger schemas, legacy projections), command assets (`deep-review.yaml`, `deep-research.yaml`, compiled contracts, presentations), skill references and feature catalogs, manual-testing playbooks, and vitest suites.\\n- Behavior claims to verify: the range's three commits claim (a) a dry-run convergence call stays read-only, (b) a review row mints identity and refuses a reused key with different content, (c) the blocked-stop record is withheld from a dry run. The expansive-depth frontier, fan-out lineage contract, and executor adapter capability record are the surrounding contracts those fixes touch.\\n- Reuse and conventions: the append gateway is the single state-log writer; the reducer owns registry/dashboard/strategy projections; `frontier-admit.cjs` owns the node store; the YAML workflow is the stop-decision consumer and computes no arithmetic of its own.\\n- Review risks and gaps: the range is a commit range, so `reviewScopeFiles` is the git diff list, not a glob expansion. Files deleted by the range have nothing to review. The compiled contract markdown is generated from the YAML, so drift between them is a traceability finding, not a code finding.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery; 88 files in scope, see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`]\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Max iterations: 24\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: files\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-20T19:07:02.024Z\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795201628763,"end":1795201631895}}}}
