{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795201673610,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa5ba8ce0019vyEsjh8W56BVZ","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa5ba056001nsOkRDmaSdRaPZ","type":"tool","id":"call_b3654c2826d095d60d361498","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":60,"offset":3330,"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, lines 3330-3389\n3330:     promptArgIndexes: [1],\n3331:     executableVersion: resolveExecutableVersion('devin', options),\n3332:     model,\n3333:     reasoningEffort: null,\n3334:     serviceTier: null,\n3335:     resolvedSandbox,\n3336:     resolvedPermission,\n3337:     compensatingControl: resolvedSandbox === 'read-only',\n3338:     webSearch,\n3339:   });\n3340: }\n3341: \n3342: // Provider that fronts each allowlisted Pi model, captured from `pi --list-models`\n3343: // (openai fronts the GPT-6 tunes; minimax fronts its own family; opencode-go fronts\n3344: // Qwen 3.8 Max; DevPass fronts DeepSeek V4 Flash under its bare literal since 2026-09-07, for\n3345: // the same flat-price reason GLM moved there — the direct DeepSeek API provider was retired\n3346: // from the roster). Pi selects a model as `<provider>/<id>`; without the\n3347: // provider prefix it falls back to its default provider and dispatches the wrong\n3348: // model. Hand-duplicated as a plain literal so command construction stays\n3349: // synchronous and unit-testable, matching this file's per-kind convention.\n3350: const PI_MODEL_PROVIDERS = new Map([\n3351:   ['deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017', 'llmgateway'],\n3352:   ['opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash', 'opencode-go'],\n3353:   ['minimax-m3', 'minimax'],\n3354:   ['gpt-6-luna', 'openai'],\n3355:   ['gpt-6-sol', 'openai'],\n3356:   ['gpt-6.1-terra', 'openai'],\n3357:   ['qwen3.8-max', 'opencode-go'],\n3358:   // OpenRouter fronts exactly DeepSeek V4 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash here. Each model id\n3359:   // already carries its upstream provider path, so `${provider}/${model}` yields the\n3360:   // 3-segment openrouter/<upstream>/<model> selector Pi's OpenRouter roster expects.\n3361:   ['deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp', 'openrouter'],\n3362:   ['z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', 'openrouter'],\n3363:   // DevPass (LLM Gateway) fronts GLM-5.3-Flash under a bare literal, so `${provider}/${model}`\n3364:   // yields the two-segment llmgateway/glm-5.3-flash selector the gateway requires: it 400s on a\n3365:   // provider-prefixed id. Distinct from the OpenRouter `z-ai/` literal above. opencode-go also\n3366:   // fronts this model under the same bare literal, and one literal maps to one provider, so the\n3367:   // opencode-go GLM route is direct-dispatch only. DevPass wins the fan-out slot\n3368:   // because it is a flat-price subscription and the other two routes bill per token.\n3369:   ['glm-5.3-flash', 'llmgateway'],\n3370: ]);\n3371: // A provider-qualified literal already carries its route, so the default\n3372: // `${provider}/${model}` composition would repeat the provider. These literals map to the\n3373: // exact selector Pi lists for them instead: opencode-go names the model bare.\n3374: const PI_MODEL_SELECTORS = new Map([\n3375:   ['opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash', 'opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash'],\n3376: ]);\n3377: // Map each shared reasoningEffort level to the name Pi's `--thinking` uses (from the\n3378: // installed `pi --help`): the config's 'none' is Pi's 'off', and the config's 'ultra'\n3379: // caps at Pi's top level 'max'; every other level is identity. A map (not a plain\n3380: // allowlist) is required so a valid reasoningEffort never fails closed on a naming gap.\n3381: const REASONING_TO_PI_THINKING = new Map([\n3382:   ['none', 'off'],\n3383:   ['minimal', 'minimal'],\n3384:   ['low', 'low'],\n3385:   ['medium', 'medium'],\n3386:   ['high', 'high'],\n3387:   ['xhigh', 'xhigh'],\n3388:   ['max', 'max'],\n3389:   ['ultra', 'max'],\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 3390]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, lines 3330-3389\n3330:     promptArgIndexes: [1],\n3331:     executableVersion: resolveExecutableVersion('devin', options),\n3332:     model,\n3333:     reasoningEffort: null,\n3334:     serviceTier: null,\n3335:     resolvedSandbox,\n3336:     resolvedPermission,\n3337:     compensatingControl: resolvedSandbox === 'read-only',\n3338:     webSearch,\n3339:   });\n3340: }\n3341: \n3342: // Provider that fronts each allowlisted Pi model, captured from `pi --list-models`\n3343: // (openai fronts the GPT-6 tunes; minimax fronts its own family; opencode-go fronts\n3344: // Qwen 3.8 Max; DevPass fronts DeepSeek V4 Flash under its bare literal since 2026-09-07, for\n3345: // the same flat-price reason GLM moved there — the direct DeepSeek API provider was retired\n3346: // from the roster). Pi selects a model as `<provider>/<id>`; without the\n3347: // provider prefix it falls back to its default provider and dispatches the wrong\n3348: // model. Hand-duplicated as a plain literal so command construction stays\n3349: // synchronous and unit-testable, matching this file's per-kind convention.\n3350: const PI_MODEL_PROVIDERS = new Map([\n3351:   ['deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017', 'llmgateway'],\n3352:   ['opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash', 'opencode-go'],\n3353:   ['minimax-m3', 'minimax'],\n3354:   ['gpt-6-luna', 'openai'],\n3355:   ['gpt-6-sol', 'openai'],\n3356:   ['gpt-6.1-terra', 'openai'],\n3357:   ['qwen3.8-max', 'opencode-go'],\n3358:   // OpenRouter fronts exactly DeepSeek V4 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash here. Each model id\n3359:   // already carries its upstream provider path, so `${provider}/${model}` yields the\n3360:   // 3-segment openrouter/<upstream>/<model> selector Pi's OpenRouter roster expects.\n3361:   ['deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-visi