d reported; running the guard after the gates would skip\n4836-      // those lanes entirely. The gates keep their own verdict: a finding is recorded on the\n4837-      // ledger and never turns a failed lane into a passing one.\n4838-      //\n4839-      // Uniform across every dispatch kind: diff the working tree for NEW\n4840-      // out-of-artifact-dir writes. Under the default preserve mode the path stays on disk\n4841-      // and is reported, never deleted, since it may be a concurrent parent/sibling write\n4842-      // this leaf cannot be proven to own; restore mode is an explicit opt-in that rolls a\n4843-      // path back. The leaf must still be free to write its iteration file/delta/state\n4844-      // record inside lineageDir; only OUT-of-lineageDir writes are detected. Fails open\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2631:function runLineageProcess(command, cmdArgs, opts) {\n2632-  const { cwd, env, timeoutMs, maxBuffer } = opts;\n2633-  const hasInput = typeof opts.input === 'string';\n2634-\n2635-  return new Promise((resolvePromise) => {\n2636-    let child;\n2637-    try {\n2638-      child = spawn(command, cmdArgs, {\n2639-        cwd,\n2640-        // spawn() moves the working directory but passes the parent's PWD on unchanged,\n2641-        // and some executors read PWD to tell the model where it is.\n2642-        env: cwd ? { ...(env || process.env), PWD: path.resolve(cwd) } : env,\n2643-        stdio: [hasInput ? 'pipe' : 'ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n2644-        detached: process.platform !== 'win32',\n2645-      });\n2646-    } catch (error) {\n2647-      resolvePromise({ status: null, signal: null, stdout: '', error });\n2648-      return;\n2649-    }\n2650-    activeLineageProcesses.add(child);\n2651-    if (typeof opts.onSpawn === 'function') {\n--\n4824:          dispatch: (cmd, args, opts) => runLineageProcess(cmd, args, opts),\n4825-        });\n