{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202062387,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa619482001mil4wdy0YVBCAm","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa6128cc001OTvCJzik4P4xC1","type":"tool","id":"call_b7dcc334b1c64847c2651f90","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"external_directory\" --include=*.ts --include=*.cjs --include=*.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:294:- `cli-opencode`: pass the rendered prompt as the last argument of the command `buildLineageCommand` in `fanout-run.cjs` builds, `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}` with stdin closed. `reasoningEffort` Y rides as the `#Y` suffix on the model. `--auto` is always passed. `dispatch-iteration.cjs` resolves an unset sandbox mode to `workspace-write`, as fan-out does, and under it the builder hands the child an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`; the receipt records `sandboxMode` `workspace-write`. That deny stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but does not confine Bash. **In both modes that run, Bash keeps full OS-level write access.** `danger-full-access` adds no deny, and OpenCode exposes no confinement flag, so an explicit `read-only` fails closed before dispatch. The real containment is (a) the `external_directory` deny on the file tools under `workspace-write`, (b) the prompt-level \"ALLOWED WRITE PATHS\" / \"BANNED OPERATIONS\" contract rendered into the iteration prompt, which relies on the model obeying instructions rather than an OS-level sandbox, and (c) post-dispatch validation catching some violations after the fact. Fetched/reviewed content must be treated as potentially adversarial (untrusted) for prompt-injection purposes.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197:A lineage counts as fulfilled only when its state log holds at least one iteration, a terminal stop row from this attempt (`terminal_gates` for review, a closeout synthesis row for research, where `synthesis_incomplete` does not count), every iteration row before that terminal row in the file, and no row whose stamp carries an explicit zone stamped more than two minutes after the lineage process ended; iteration stamps are written by the model, so they are never compared with the terminal row's stamp. A research lineage writes no stop-check row, so its closeout row must also carry a `stopReason` from the frozen lifecycle enum, and a `maxIterationsReached` stop must have recorded as many distinct iterations as the `maxIterations` cap in the lineage's own config; the failures are `missing_stop_reason`, `unknown_stop_reason` and `max_iterations_unproven`, which an unreadable cap also yields. Review keeps its gate-row check, and the lenient pre-spawn skip check is unchanged. Otherwise it fails even at exit 0. The executor-group `--sandbox-mode` maps to `sandboxMode`. A `cli-claude-code` lineage keeps `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so the runner warns at launch, and if that lineage records nothing its failure names `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. A `cli-opencode` lineage takes the same `workspace-write` default: it runs `--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`, merged into any inherited value (one that is unparseable or not a JSON object fails the build). That stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but not Bash, which can still write anywhere, so the preview records `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating`, never `preventive`. `danger-full-access` is plain `--auto` with no deny, and an explicit `read-only` is refused.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/dispatch-iteration.vitest.ts:504:  // denies external_directory to its file tools. The deny exists only in the child's\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/dispatch-iteration.vitest.ts:524:      it(`hands the child an external_directory deny under workspace-write (sandbox mode ${sandboxMode})`, () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/dispatch-iteration.vitest.ts:528:          permission: { external_directory: 'deny' },\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/dispatch-iteration.vitest.ts:603:        permission: { external_directory: 'deny' },\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts:3826:  it('resolves an unset cli-opencode sandboxMode to workspace-write and hands the child an external_directory deny', async () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts:3880:      permission: { external_directory: 'deny' },\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts:3908:        permission: { bash: 'allow', external_directory: 'allow' },\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts:3914:      permission: { bash: 'allow', external_directory: 'deny' },\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2829:  // rule (external_directory denied for its file tools), and its Bash tool can still write\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2973:// opencode.json, so a workspace-write lineage gets its external_directory deny there. An\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2991:  return JSON.stringify({ ...config, permission: { ...(config.permission || {}), external_directory: 'deny' } });\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3006:  // denied. workspace-write adds an explicit external_directory deny, which stops the file\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3042:    ? `WARN: lineage ${lineage.label || '(cli-opencode)'} runs with --auto and external_directory denied: `\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4166:    // builder honours workspace-write by denying external_directory to the file tools and\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:485:  // with an inline config that denies external_directory to the file tools, carried in the\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:758:  // with an inline config that denies external_directory to the file tools, carried in the\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:290: * external_directory deny for cli-opencode's file tools under workspace-write and a\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:301:  'cli-opencode': false, // no confinement flag exists; workspace-write denies external_directory to the file tools only (Bash can still write outside the working directory), and read-only is refused\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:294:- `cli-opencode`: pass the rendered prompt as the last argument of the command `buildLineageCommand` in `fanout-run.cjs` builds, `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}` with stdin closed. `reasoningEffort` Y rides as the `#Y` suffix on the model. `--auto` is always passed. `dispatch-iteration.cjs` resolves an unset sandbox mode to `workspace-write`, as fan-out does, and under it the builder hands the child an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`; the receipt records `sandboxMode` `workspace-write`. That deny stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but does not confine Bash. **In both modes that run, Bash keeps full OS-level write access.** `danger-full-access` adds no deny, and OpenCode exposes no confinement flag, so an explicit `read-only` fails closed before dispatch.