{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202137888,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa62be3a002SsK6S6H2TTq9ci","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa62b474001F5NmG9BCPqcw38","type":"tool","id":"call_cf89822e708512af339b4bb9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-154\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n3: description: Runtime strategy for the deepseek fan-out lineage of the expansive-depth review over the deep-loop runtime and command surface.\n4: importance_tier: normal\n5: contextType: planning\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: ### Purpose\n13: \n14: Persistent brain for this review lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\n15: \n16: ### Usage\n17: \n18: - **Init:** Populated from config and the bounded context snapshot.\n19: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned frontier node and dimension, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n20: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Review: `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2 -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep` (88 changed files, commit-range target, review target type `files`).\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n31: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n32: - [ ] correctness\n33: - [ ] security\n34: - [ ] traceability\n35: - [ ] maintainability\n36: \n37: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n38: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n39: \n40: - No fixes, no source edits, no refactors: this loop is observation-only.\n41: - No review of files outside the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under the two pathspecs.\n42: - No web research and no external resource fetching.\n43: - No review of the `review/` packet artifacts themselves except as traceability evidence.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n48: \n49: - Legal convergence per `convergence.cjs` (composite weighted vote under `convergenceThreshold: 0.1`, all dimensions clean, frontier drained).\n50: - `maxIterations: 24` reached.\n51: - Stuck recovery (`stuckThreshold: 2`) or three consecutive failed iterations.\n52: - Wall-clock budget `maxDurationMinutes: 120` from `createdAt`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n57: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n58: [None yet]\n59: \n60: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n61: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n62: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n63: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n64: - P1 (Required): 0\n65: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n66: - Resolved: 0\n67: \n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n69: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n70: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n75: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n80: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n81: [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n82: \n83: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n84: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n85: - Completed pivots: 0\n86: - Failed pivots: 0\n87: - Audited overrides: 0\n88: - Swept: none yet\n89: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n90: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n91: \n92: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n93: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n98: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n99: Frontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs): Cross-CLI adapter contract and sandbox: is the adapter capability record true for every kind, does a requested sandbox mode reach codex, pi, dsh and harness argv, and is the opencode workspace-write default with compensating enforcement sound? - review the correctness dimension\n100: \n101: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n102: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n103: \n104: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n105: \n106: - Target pointers: the commit range `17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2` under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` and `.skilled/commands/deep`. 88 files: runtime scripts (`append-mode-event.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `fanout-run.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, `synthesis-closeout.cjs`, `upsert.cjs`), runtime libs (`executor-config.ts`, `executor-audit.ts`, ledger schemas, legacy projections), command assets (`deep-review.yaml`, `deep-research.yaml`, compiled contracts, presentations), skill references and feature catalogs, manual-testing playbooks, and vitest suites.\n107: - Behavior claims to verify: the range's three commits claim (a) a dry-run convergence call stays read-only, (b) a review row mints identity and refuses a reused key with different content, (c) the blocked-stop record is withheld from a dry run. The expansive-depth frontier, fan-out lineage contract, and executor adapter capability record are the surrounding contracts those fixes touch.\n108: - Reuse and conventions: the append gateway is the single state-log writer; the reducer owns registry/dashboard/strategy projections; `frontier-admit.cjs` owns the node store; the YAML workflow is the stop-decision consumer and computes no arithmetic of its own.\n109: - Review risks and gaps: the range is a commit range, so `reviewScopeFiles` is the git diff list, not a glob expansion. Files deleted by the range have nothing to review. The compiled contract markdown is generated from the YAML, so drift between them is a traceability finding, not a code finding.\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n114: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n115: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n116: \n117: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n118: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n119: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n120: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n121: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n122: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n123: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n124: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n125: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n130: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n131: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery; 88 files in scope, see `deep-review-config.json` `reviewScopeFiles`]\n132: \n133: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n134: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n135: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n140: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n141: - Max iterations: 24\n142: - Convergence threshold: 0.1\n143: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n144: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n145: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n146: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n147: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n148: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n149: - Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n150: - Severity threshold: P2\n151: - Review target type: files\n152: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent