{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202151295,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa62ed450011uUxwsRzlGx6B2","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa62e5b4001Jcgw9Sy5zk4diC","type":"tool","id":"call_924b42b5c0495cf70f327c3b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Builder-to-record comparison: reading each `build*LineageCommand` beside its `EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES` row found both P2s without running the suite (iteration 1).\n- Tracing the built command's `env` through `extraEnv` into `runLineageProcess` proved the opencode deny reaches the child in both dispatch paths (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Reading the conformance test as proof of the sandbox contract: its `permission-mode` assertion compares only `read-only` with `danger-full-access`, so it cannot see the dsh `workspace-write` collapse (iteration 1).\n","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-