@@ EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n \n    Q-Exec. Executor (optional, press enter for default):\n      A) Native (default) — dispatch via @deep-review agent with Opus.\n-     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json [--auto] \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is added only under `danger-full-access`, the one explicit sandbox mode cli-opencode accepts. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n+     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is always passed; under `workspace-write` (the default) an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` denies `external_directory` to the file tools, Bash is not confined, and `read-only` is refused. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n       C) cli-claude-code — `claude -p \"PROMPT\" --model X --permission-mode X`, where the permission mode is `acceptEdits` at the default `workspace-write` and `bypassPermissions` with `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. The default cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so a lineage that must record state needs the flag. Optional --effort and optional `--config-dir=PATH` for CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. No service-tier.\n      D) cli-codex — requires the `codex` binary on PATH. Supports `--reasoning-effort` and `--service-tier`.\n      E) cli-cursor — requires `cursor-agent`. Model must be on the enforced allowlist. No `--reasoning-effort` (effort is baked into the model id), no `--service-tier`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md b/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\nindex 5e79754f4a6..3c13d822346 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@ into `config`.\n | `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing. `restart` opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `research/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n | `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n | `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n-| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. `cli-opencode` accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value. |\n+| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. A `cli-opencode` lineage also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies OpenCode's file tools outside the working directory but does not confine Bash, so Bash can still write anywhere; `danger-full-access` drops that deny, and `read-only` is refused. |\n | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md b/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\nindex fc97d45a0c7..f657b90b8a2 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ into `config`.\n | `--restart`, `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing; `restart`, which bare `--restart` selects, opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `review/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n | `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, and an expansive run whose frontier is already drained can re-stop on `frontier_drained` the same way, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n | `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n-| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports is in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. `cli-opencode` accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value. |\n+| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports is in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. A `cli-opencode` lineage also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies OpenCode's file tools outside the working directory but does not confine Bash, so Bash can still write anywhere; `danger-full-access` drops that deny, and `read-only` is refused. |\n | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown b/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown\nindex 9e3f417815d..63c3a380ad7 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown\n@@ -7,12 +7,12 @@\n   \"sourceDigests\": [\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/research.md\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"d3bd39a49afcbe9bb8b0781e8d631a6f42eeb60e096b667b663ec36f2a807663\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"6bad85be5d2db7d7dcd7cafbda46c3b79f430514229cf740cbca3302f141483f\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"815429515b58ad59c39a8a962f6aedfb5f2aad4a9825009704865981354fabb7\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"90d2da6c4ebe154522d300876130c1990c4efc18b3d5b7cf317ce75654ca35fd\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"e3ff2e978d5c86abe21bc5b598922f30168d69f14188733a1bcfbe44a8128610\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"0881ab8c0c50d93e7dbe54d1a4f956c4e05a40b643cf01d3fb9381af1e2c5b0d\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"724f4232b5a774ac6a11261b148a54ec1c6cadef897f7eea417b8371275f3a34\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"49a1fe80dd15e55a6d788320e24583cd214ba2d0b9e5a33302b4862c28af6d4a\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     }\n   ],\n-  \"compiledBodyDigest\": \"457e67576170e00dc2a7d9e5938d0bcd297866dcaa017ff7fb20d87f59dd3a70\"\n+  \"compiledBodyDigest\": \"bcb4d97c1badd13e2ec9cc57e948d1044ccee09e5843804b18649d0a384a7c38\"\n }\n GENERATED_COMMAND_CONTRACT_HEADER_END -->\n # Compiled Command Contract: /deep:research\n@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@ EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n    |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.kind (`native` | `cli-codex` | `cli-claude-code` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-cursor` | `cli-devin` | `cli-pi` | `cli-deepseek-harness` | `cli-mistral-vibe`, `cli-deepseek-harness` as a single lineage or a fan-out and `cli-mistral-vibe` only as a fan-out lineage. `EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` is authoritative)\n    |-- --model=<id> -> config.executor.model (for example `gpt-5.4`)\n    |-- --config-dir=<path> -> config.executor.configDir (cli-claude-code only; must resolve under ~/.claude* or a repository .claude* folder; fan-out sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)\n-   |-- --sandbox-mode=<mode> -> config.executor.sandboxMode (`read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; default `workspace-write`; cli-opencode accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value)\n+   |-- --sandbox-mode=<mode> -> config.executor.sandboxMode (`read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; default `workspace-write`; cli-opencode also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies its file tools outside the working directory but not Bash; `read-only` is refused)\n    |-- --reasoning-effort=<level> -> config.executor.reasoningEffort (`none` | `minimal` | `low` | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` | `max`)\n    |-- --service-tier=<tier> -> config.executor.serviceTier (`priority` | `standard` | `fast`)\n    |-- --executor-timeout=<seconds> -> config.executor.timeoutSeconds (positive integer, default `900`)\n@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n \n    Q-Exec. Executor (optional, press enter for default):\n      A) Native (default) — dispatch via @deep-research agent with Opus.\n-     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json [--auto] \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is added only under `danger-full-access`, the one explicit sandbox mode cli-opencode accepts. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n+     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is always passed; under `workspace-write` (the default) an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` denies `external_directory` to the file tools, Bash is not confined, and `read-only` is refused. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n      C) cli-claude-code — `claude -p \"PROMPT\" --model X --permission-mode X`, where the permission mode is `acceptEdits` at the default `workspace-write` and `bypassPermissions` with `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`; the default cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so a lineage that must record state needs the flag. Optional --effort and optional `--config-dir=PATH` for CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. No service-tier.\n      D) cli-codex — requires the `codex` binary on PATH. Supports `--reasoning-effort` and `--service-tier`.\n      E) cli-cursor — requires `cursor-agent`. Model must be on the enforced allowlist. No `--reasoning-effort` (effort is baked into the model id), no `--service-tier`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown b/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown\nindex 1f904b76dfb..1415bde9511 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown\n@@ -7,12 +7,12 @@\n   \"sourceDigests\": [\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/review.md\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"f294cd132901b610bed73a1d4face3af7351e1579a7f300866ac36329be53c3c\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"32705f606390949d6ecd34304995fcaaae6a4db8aab66510b18294d8388c3f77\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"ebbe814e1f8dc9340d8585868b1e4f2b9cf9735177d8424e91c9dddf94f016ea\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"04f1c2a361cafcd95f20532ab7ff0b38ec62e3fdda2eaa77b95555bec39d93f6\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"8231b8fa37de61b217adc27b77a37fa765d3f06abd332efa09bc24d06315ac1d\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"092d2d95264facdd99706cd490bf5180bb8c47e300ddcca93d04cf399057271e\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"9e01026998fdc7bd6dcba3f446f31d943104b0e5ef6276bb387705a5b5019721\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"f51ef29cc427ff1b4dd9d3d165d1dd4c12dec0b44051610d8bfdcaadb8367202\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@\n     },\n     {\n       \"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\",\n-      \"sha256\": \"cce24cf3e1536e5b4cf71cc62b897423c0ebad2bda2a691749827e1626e1e996\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"e90f6181e9896f5e9cb5bdcf6df63a2278b579f60a602c54e3992e514d8472d7\",\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     },\n     {\n@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@\n       \"section\": \"full\"\n     }\n   ],\n-  \"compiledBodyDigest\": \"03fa107803e109884442858fa531c8137f4df1e9050a6d0eb228b9f631ed9882\"\n+  \"compiledBodyDigest\": \"e575ad4dfa420b06ff08e78c19d2323526519245d3107fe2df1b6715ce066d6b\"\n }\n GENERATED_COMMAND_CONTRACT_HEADER_END -->\n # Compiled Command Contract: /deep:review\n@@ -284,7 +284,7 @@ EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n    |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.kind (`native` | `cli-codex` | `cli-claude-code` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-cursor` | `cli-devin` | `cli-pi` | `cli-deepseek-harness` | `cli-mistral-vibe`. Every kind runs in `:auto` and `:confirm`, `cli-deepseek-harness` as a single lineage or a fan-out and `cli-mistral-vibe` only as a fan-out lineage. `EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` is authoritative)\n    |-- --model=<id> -> config.executor.model (for example `gpt-5.4`)\n    |-- --config-dir=<path> -> config.executor.configDir (cli-claude-code only; must resolve under ~/.claude* or a repository .claude* folder; fan-out sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)\n-   |-- --sandbox-mode=<mode> -> config.executor.sandboxMode (`read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; default `workspace-write`; cli-opencode accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value)\n+   |-- --sandbox-mode=<mode> -> config.executor.sandboxMode (`read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; default `workspace-write`; cli-opencode also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies its file tools outside the working directory but not Bash; `read-only` is refused)\n    |-- --reasoning-effort=<level> -> config.executor.reasoningEffort (`none` | `minimal` | `low` | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` | `max`)\n    |-- --service-tier=<tier> -> config.executor.serviceTier (`priority` | `standard` | `fast`)\n    |-- --executor-timeout=<seconds> -> config.executor.timeoutSeconds (positive integer, default `900`)\n@@ -363,7 +363,7 @@ EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n \n    Q-Exec. Executor (optional, press enter for default):\n      A) Native (default) — dispatch via @deep-review agent with Opus.\n-     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json [--auto] \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is added only under `danger-full-access`, the one explicit sandbox mode cli-opencode accepts. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n+     B) cli-opencode — `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}`, with `reasoningEffort` Y on the model id. `--auto` is always passed; under `workspace-write` (the default) an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` denies `external_directory` to the file tools, Bash is not confined, and `read-only` is refused. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash and GLM-5.3-Flash are pinned to `max`. No `--agent`: the default agent runs. No service-tier.\n       C) cli-claude-code — `claude -p \"PROMPT\" --model X --permission-mode X`, where the permission mode is `acceptEdits` at the default `workspace-write` and `bypassPermissions` with `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. The default cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so a lineage that must record state needs the flag. Optional --effort and optional `--config-dir=PATH` for CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. No service-tier.\n      D) cli-codex — requires the `codex` binary on PATH. Supports `--reasoning-effort` and `--service-tier`.\n      E) cli-cursor — requires `cursor-agent`. Model must be on the enforced allowlist. No `--reasoning-effort` (effort is baked into the model id), no `--service-tier`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md b/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\nindex 5e79754f4a6..3c13d822346 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@ into `config`.\n | `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing. `restart` opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `research/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n | `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n | `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n-| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. `cli-opencode` accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value. |\n+| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. A `cli-opencode` lineage also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies OpenCode's file tools outside the working directory but does not confine Bash, so Bash can still write anywhere; `danger-full-access` drops that deny, and `read-only` is refused. |\n | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md b/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\nindex fc97d45a0c7..f657b90b8a2 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ into `config`.\n | `--restart`, `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing; `restart`, which bare `--restart` selects, opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `review/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n | `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, and an expansive run whose frontier is already drained can re-stop on `frontier_drained` the same way, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n | `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n-| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports is in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. `cli-opencode` accepts only `danger-full-access` as an explicit value. |\n+| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--sandbox-mode=(read-only, workspace-write or danger-full-access)`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports is in the presentation asset. A `cli-claude-code` lineage defaults to `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so pass `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` to run it with `bypassPermissions` and let it record state. A `cli-opencode` lineage also defaults to `workspace-write`, which denies OpenCode's file tools outside the working directory but does not confine Bash, so Bash can still write anywhere; `danger-full-access` drops that deny, and `read-only` is refused. |\n | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"git diff 17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2 -- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown .skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown .skilled/commands/deep/review.md .skilled/commands/deep/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202333946,"end":1795202334315}}}}
