{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202345326,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa65e8650016Rd1ZcrNI6a0m3","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa65d3a6001Va0sTSX294gidY","type":"tool","id":"call_b3a5c4ef5e4f4ee59a9352b5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"function buildClaudeInvocation\" -A 30 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs | head -40; echo \"=== loop-protocol 280-292 ===\"; sed -n '280,292p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md"},"output":"356:function buildClaudeInvocation(context, configDir, promptBody) {\n357-  const isReview = context.loopType === 'review';\n358-  const executor = {\n359-    kind: 'cli-claude-code',\n360-    model: context.model,\n361-    configDir: configDir || null,\n362-    reasoningEffort: context.reasoningEffort,\n363-    serviceTier: isReview ? null : context.serviceTier,\n364-    sandboxMode: context.sandboxMode,\n365-    timeoutSeconds: context.timeoutSeconds,\n366-  };\n367-  if (isReview) executor.governor = null;\n368-  const args = [\n369-    '-p',\n370-    promptBody,\n371-    '--model',\n372-    executor.model,\n373-    '--permission-mode',\n374-    resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode),\n375-    '--output-format',\n376-    'text',\n377-  ];\n378-  if (executor.reasoningEffort) {\n379-    args.push('--effort', executor.reasoningEffort);\n380-  }\n381-  return { executor, args };\n382-}\n383-\n384-function runClaude(context) {\n385-  // Both loops validate the config dir before the prompt is read, so an unusable\n386-  // config directory fails before any prompt or persona file is touched.\n=== loop-protocol 280-292 ===\n\n#### Executor Resolution\n\nBefore dispatching, the YAML resolves the executor via `parseExecutorConfig` from `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`. The resolved `config.executor.kind` selects the dispatch branch:\n\n- `native`: dispatch `@deep-review` agent with model Opus.\n- `cli-opencode`: pass the rendered prompt as the last argument of the command `buildLineageCommand` in `fanout-run.cjs` builds, `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}` with stdin closed. `reasoningEffort` Y rides as the `#Y` suffix on the model. `--auto` is always passed. `dispatch-iteration.cjs` resolves an unset sandbox mode to `workspace-write`, as fan-out does, and under it the builder hands the child an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`; the receipt records `sandboxMode` `workspace-write`. That deny stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but does not confine Bash. **In both modes that run, Bash keeps full OS-level write access.** `danger-full-access` adds no deny, and OpenCode exposes no confinement flag, so an explicit `read-only` fails closed before dispatch. The real containment is (a) the `external_directory` deny on the file tools under `workspace-write`, (b) the prompt-level \"ALLOWED WRITE PATHS\" / \"BANNED OPERATIONS\" contract rendered into the iteration prompt (`assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl`), which relies on the model obeying instructions rather than an OS-level sandbox, and (c) post-dispatch validation (`validateIterationOutputs`) catching some violations after the fact. Because review targets are arbitrary code/spec files, they MUST be treated as potentially adversarial content (untrusted) for prompt-injection purposes — the same containment posture as untrusted fetched content in deep-research.\n- `cli-claude-code`: `claude -p \"$(cat prompt)\" --model X --permission-mode <mode> --output-format text` with optional `--effort Y`. The permission mode resolves from `--sandbox-mode`: unset or `workspace-write` runs `acceptEdits` so iteration writes succeed, `read-only` runs `plan` and `danger-full-access` runs `bypassPermissions`. The inline workflow branches are not the complete schema: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` (experimental) also have inline branches that run `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, and `cli-mistral-vibe` runs only as a fan-out lineage. The executor-kind authority is `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`).\n- Sandbox on those `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branches: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` resolve the requested `--sandbox-mode` and map it to the kind's own read-only or write surface, which is an OS sandbox only on codex, cursor and the deepseek harness. An unset mode resolves to `workspace-write`, so the iteration can write its iteration file, delta and state record. A requested `read-only` is passed through, never widened, and the iteration then fails at the post-dispatch artifact gate rather than gaining write access. The deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes.\n\nAll branches share:\n1. Pre-dispatch prompt rendering via `renderPromptPack` (writes to `{artifact_dir}/prompts/iteration-{n}.md`).\n2. Post-dispatch validation via `validateIterationOutputs` (asserts iteration file + JSONL delta + required fields).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"356:function buildClaudeInvocation(context, configDir, promptBody) {\n357-  const isReview = context.loopType === 'review';\n358-  const executor = {\n359-    kind: 'cli-claude-code',\n360-    model: context.model,\n361-    configDir: configDir || null,\n362-    reasoningEffort: context.reasoningEffort,\n363-    serviceTier: isReview ? null : context.serviceTier,\n364-    sandboxMode: context.sandboxMode,\n365-    timeoutSeconds: context.timeoutSeconds,\n366-  };\n367-  if (isReview) executor.governor = null;\n368-  const args = [\n369-    '-p',\n370-    promptBody,\n371-    '--model',\n372-    executor.model,\n373-    '--permission-mode',\n374-    resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode),\n375-    '--output-format',\n376-    'text',\n377-  ];\n378-  if (executor.reasoningEffort) {\n379-    args.push('--effort', executor.reasoningEffort);\n380-  }\n381-  return { executor, args };\n382-}\n383-\n384-function runClaude(context) {\n385-  // Both loops validate the config dir before the prompt is read, so an unusable\n386-  // config directory fails before any prompt or persona file is touched.\n=== loop-protocol 280-292 ===\n\n#### Executor Resolution\n\nBefore dispatching, the YAML resolves the executor via `parseExecutorConfig` from `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`. The resolved `config.executor.kind` selects the dispatch branch:\n\n- `native`: dispatch `@deep-review` agent with model Opus.\n- `cli-opencode`: pass the rendered prompt as the last argument of the command `buildLineageCommand` in `fanout-run.cjs` builds, `opencode run --standalone -m X[#Y] --format json --auto \"PROMPT\"`, started in `{repo_root}` with stdin closed. `reasoningEffort` Y rides as the `#Y` suffix on the model. `--auto` is always passed. `dispatch-iteration.cjs` resolves an unset sandbox mode to `workspace-write`, as fan-out does, and under it the builder hands the child an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`; the receipt records `sandboxMode` `workspace-write`. That deny stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but does not confine Bash. **In both modes that run, Bash keeps full OS-level write access.** `danger-full-access` adds no deny, and OpenCode exposes no confinement flag, so an explicit `read-only` fails closed before dispatch. The real containment is (a) the `external_directory` deny on the file tools under `workspace-write`, (b) the prompt-level \"ALLOWED WRITE PATHS\" / \"BANNED OPERATIONS\" contract rendered into the iteration prompt (`assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl`), which relies on the model obeying instructions rather than an OS-level sandbox, and (c) post-dispatch validation (`validateIterationOutputs`) catching some violations after the fact. Because review targets are arbitrary code/spec files, they MUST be treated as potentially adversarial content (untrusted) for prompt-injection purposes — the same containment posture as untrusted fetched content in deep-research.\n- `cli-claude-code`: `claude -p \"$(cat prompt)\" --model X --permission-mode <mode> --output-format text` with optional `--effort Y`. The permission mode resolves from `--sandbox-mode`: unset or `workspace-write` runs `acceptEdits` so iteration writes succeed, `read-only` runs `plan` and `danger-full-access` runs `bypassPermissions`. The inline workflow branches are not the complete schema: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` (experimental) also have inline branches that run `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, and `cli-mistral-vibe` runs only as a fan-out lineage. The executor-kind authority is `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`).\n- Sandbox on those `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branches: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` resolve the requested `--sandbox-mode` and map it to the kind's own read-only or write surface, which is an OS sandbox only on codex, cursor and the deepseek harness. An unset mode resolves to `workspace-write`, so the iteration can write its iteration file, delta and state record. A requested `read-only` is passed through, never widened, and the iteration then fails at the post-dispatch artifact gate rather than gaining write access. The deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes.\n\nAll branches share:\n1. Pre-dispatch prompt rendering via `renderPromptPack` (writes to `{artifact_dir}/prompts/iteration-{n}.md`).\n2. Post-dispatch validation via `validateIterationOutputs` (asserts iteration file + JSONL delta + required fields).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"function buildClaudeInvocation\\\" -A 30 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs | head -40; echo \\\"=== loop-protocol 280-292 ===\\\"; sed -n '280,292p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202345061,"end":1795202345326}}}}
