{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202350088,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa65fadf001x7xRyA6HbU11aD","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa65ee1b001wWEV3CI25Ei9Qx","type":"tool","id":"call_a0ba3eb1d98fdc9bdd1d399e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"stream-json\\|output-format\\|deepseek harness\\|danger-full-access\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md | head -20"},"output":"110:A `cli-claude-code` lineage runs `claude -p` with `--output-format stream-json --verbose`, so its\n197:A lineage counts as fulfilled only when its state log holds at least one iteration, a terminal stop row from this attempt (`terminal_gates` for review, a closeout synthesis row for research, where `synthesis_incomplete` does not count), every iteration row before that terminal row in the file, and no row whose stamp carries an explicit zone stamped more than two minutes after the lineage process ended; iteration stamps are written by the model, so they are never compared with the terminal row's stamp. A research lineage writes no stop-check row, so its closeout row must also carry a `stopReason` from the frozen lifecycle enum, and a `maxIterationsReached` stop must have recorded as many distinct iterations as the `maxIterations` cap in the lineage's own config; the failures are `missing_stop_reason`, `unknown_stop_reason` and `max_iterations_unproven`, which an unreadable cap also yields. Review keeps its gate-row check, and the lenient pre-spawn skip check is unchanged. Otherwise it fails even at exit 0. The executor-group `--sandbox-mode` maps to `sandboxMode`. A `cli-claude-code` lineage keeps `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so the runner warns at launch, and if that lineage records nothing its failure names `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. A `cli-opencode` lineage takes the same `workspace-write` default: it runs `--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`, merged into any inherited value (one that is unparseable or not a JSON object fails the build). That stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but not Bash, which can still write anywhere, so the preview records `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating`, never `preventive`. `danger-full-access` is plain `--auto` with no deny, and an explicit `read-only` is refused.\n203:`orchestration-summary.json` carries `provider_cost_usd: {total, by_lineage}`, each CLI lineage's provider cost in USD over its live and rotated logs: the sum of an opencode log's `step_finish` costs, or, for a cli-claude-code stream-json log, the last `result` event's `total_cost_usd`, which is already the attempt's whole spend. A log with no cost record, such as a cli-cursor lineage's text log, makes that lineage's cost null (unknown), and the total stays null while any lineage is unknown.\n216:| `scripts/lib/cli-guards.cjs` | `readClaudeStreamFinalText`, which the pending-question and quota checks read a claude stream-json log through |\n231:| `tests/unit/fanout-claude-stream-json.vitest.ts` | The claude stream-json argv, its last-result cost, and the pending-question and quota checks reading the final answer |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"110:A `cli-claude-code` lineage runs `claude -p` with `--output-format stream-json --verbose`, so its\n197:A lineage counts as fulfilled only when its state log holds at least one iteration, a terminal stop row from this attempt (`terminal_gates` for review, a closeout synthesis row for research, where `synthesis_incomplete` does not count), every iteration row before that terminal row in the file, and no row whose stamp carries an explicit zone stamped more than two minutes after the lineage process ended; iteration stamps are written by the model, so they are never compared with the terminal row's stamp. A research lineage writes no stop-check row, so its closeout row must also carry a `stopReason` from the frozen lifecycle enum, and a `maxIterationsReached` stop must have recorded as many distinct iterations as the `maxIterations` cap in the lineage's own config; the failures are `missing_stop_reason`, `unknown_stop_reason` and `max_iterations_unproven`, which an unreadable cap also yields. Review keeps its gate-row check, and the lenient pre-spawn skip check is unchanged. Otherwise it fails even at exit 0. The executor-group `--sandbox-mode` maps to `sandboxMode`. A `cli-claude-code` lineage keeps `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so the runner warns at launch, and if that lineage records nothing its failure names `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. A `cli-opencode` lineage takes the same `workspace-write` default: it runs `--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`, merged into any inherited value (one that is unparseable or not a JSON object fails the build). That stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but not Bash, which can still write anywhere, so the preview records `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating`, never `preventive`. `danger-full-access` is plain `--auto` with no deny, and an explicit `read-only` is refused.\n203:`orchestration-summary.json` carries `provider_cost_usd: {total, by_lineage}`, each CLI lineage's provider cost in USD over its live and rotated logs: the sum of an opencode log's `step_finish` costs, or, for a cli-claude-code stream-json log, the last `result` event's `total_cost_usd`, which is already the attempt's whole spend. A log with no cost record, such as a cli-cursor lineage's text log, makes that lineage's cost null (unknown), and the total stays null while any lineage is unknown.\n216:| `scripts/lib/cli-guards.cjs` | `readClaudeStreamFinalText`, which the pending-question and quota checks read a claude stream-json log through |\n231:| `tests/unit/fanout-claude-stream-json.vitest.ts` | The claude stream-json argv, its last-result cost, and the pending-question and quota checks reading the final answer |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"stream-json\\\\|output-format\\\\|deepseek harness\\\\|danger-full-access\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202349791,"end":1795202350088}}}}
