{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202353807,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa660939002ACDJ3Xfgz2m02A","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa65ff8f001QBzInACESWpIQF","type":"tool","id":"call_86e316e6de5b06ac206ebd22","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git diff 17a9ddbcb68..555487146e2 -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md | head -120"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\nindex c192006ae21..9eeec018001 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"composite convergence vote\"\n importance_tier: important\n contextType: implementation\n-version: 1.11.25.0\n+version: 1.11.28.0\n ---\n \n # Deep Review Convergence\n@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ Every pivot dispatches three seats, or six when its first attempt misses quorum,\n \n #### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n \n-`step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n+`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_convergence` in `deep-review.yaml` runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event), and on a BLOCKED decision it appends a `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event through the append gateway, which projects to this row. The workflow never writes it by hand. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n \n ```json\n {\n@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ Every pivot dispatches three seats, or six when its first attempt misses quorum,\n ```\n \n - `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n-- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n+- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set `convergence.cjs` records. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n - `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n - `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.\n - When the graph convergence verdict is `STOP_BLOCKED`, fold the graph blocker gate name into `blockedBy` and preserve the structured blocker objects under `graphBlockerDetail`.\n@@ -453,7 +453,7 @@ A new critical finding always signals significant remaining work. The 0.50 floor\n \n ## 6. LEGAL-STOP GATE BUNDLE\n \n-> **GATE MODEL, two naming conventions mapped to one authoritative set.** The authoritative producer is `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`, which emits **9 gates** with the `Gate` suffix: `convergenceGate` / `dimensionCoverageGate` / `p0ResolutionGate` / `evidenceDensityGate` / `hotspotSaturationGate` / `claimAdjudicationGate` / `fixCompletenessReplayGate` / `candidateCoverageGate` / `graphlessFallbackGate`. The §1 event shape mirrors this set verbatim and the reducer reads those names verbatim, so treat the event shape as authoritative when writing or reading JSONL state. The §6 table below is the high-level conceptual model and uses descriptive names WITHOUT the `Gate` suffix where one reads more naturally (for example `findingStability` maps to `convergenceGate`); each row carries its event-shape name so the mapping is explicit. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. The gate-model drift cluster (LG-0013, LG-0016, LG-0031, LG-0032) has been reconciled.\n+> **GATE MODEL, two naming conventions mapped to one authoritative set.** The authoritative producer is `convergence.cjs`, which the `step_graph_convergence` step in `deep-review.yaml` runs with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event) and which records **9 gates** with the `Gate` suffix: `convergenceGate` / `dimensionCoverageGate` / `p0ResolutionGate` / `evidenceDensityGate` / `hotspotSaturationGate` / `claimAdjudicationGate` / `fixCompletenessReplayGate` / `candidateCoverageGate` / `graphlessFallbackGate`. The §1 event shape mirrors this set verbatim and the reducer reads those names verbatim, so treat the event shape as authoritative when writing or reading JSONL state. The §6 table below is the high-level conceptual model and uses descriptive names WITHOUT the `Gate` suffix where one reads more naturally (for example `findingStability` maps to `convergenceGate`); each row carries its event-shape name so the mapping is explicit. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. The gate-model drift cluster (LG-0013, LG-0016, LG-0031, LG-0032) has been reconciled.\n \n Deep review treats STOP as legal only when the full review-specific gate bundle passes together. Convergence math may request STOP, but the workflow must still evaluate these 9 gates and persist a blocked-stop event when any gate fails.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md\nindex cac7259a829..02148f3c71f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"review iteration status enum\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: implementation\n-version: 1.11.3.0\n+version: 1.11.6.0\n ---\n \n # Deep Review State Transitions and Quality Gates\n@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ Five escalating tiers, attempted in order:\n \n ## 4. REVIEW QUALITY GATES\n \n-Evidence, Scope, and Coverage are the contract-level binary gates defined in `review-mode-contract.yaml` under `qualityGates`, evaluated after the composite convergence score exceeds the `compositeStopScore` threshold. They are necessary but not sufficient on their own: the review-specific legal-stop decision expands them into a **9-gate bundle** (`convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, `graphlessFallbackGate`) emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`. STOP is legal only when the full 9-gate bundle passes together. The authoritative gate model, event shape, and evaluation pseudocode live in `references/convergence/convergence.md` §6 \"Legal-Stop Gate Bundle\"; the 3-gate table and pseudocode below illustrate the contract-level layer only, not the complete STOP-legality check.\n+Evidence, Scope, and Coverage are the contract-level binary gates defined in `review-mode-contract.yaml` under `qualityGates`, evaluated after the composite convergence score exceeds the `compositeStopScore` threshold. They are necessary but not sufficient on their own: the review-specific legal-stop decision expands them into a **9-gate bundle** (`convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, `graphlessFallbackGate`) that `convergence.cjs` evaluates and records. STOP is legal only when the full 9-gate bundle passes together. The authoritative gate model, event shape, and evaluation pseudocode live in `references/convergence/convergence.md` §6 \"Legal-Stop Gate Bundle\"; the 3-gate table and pseudocode below illustrate the contract-level layer only, not the complete STOP-legality check.\n \n ### Gate Definitions\n \n@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ function checkReviewQualityGates(state, config, coverage):\n   return { passed: true }\n ```\n \n-The contract-level check above is illustrative; it is the review-specific 9-gate bundle that actually gates STOP. When that bundle fails, the workflow does not silently override STOP to CONTINUE -- it persists a first-class `blocked_stop` event with the failing gate names and the full `gateResults` bundle:\n+The contract-level check above is illustrative; it is the review-specific 9-gate bundle that actually gates STOP. When that bundle fails, the workflow does not silently override STOP to CONTINUE -- `convergence.cjs`, run with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event), persists a first-class `blocked_stop` event through the append gateway with the failing gate names and the full `gateResults` bundle:\n \n ```json\n {\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":N,\"blockedBy\":[\"<gate-name>\", \"...\"],\"gateResults\":{\"...\":\"...\"},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"<reason>\",\"timestamp\":\"<ISO-8601>\",\"sessionId\":\"<session-id>\",\"generation\":N}\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md\nindex b7b155c23a2..970409d4462 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"configure executor\"\n   - \"permission-mode normalization\"\n   - \"deep-loop dispatch configuration\"\n-version: 1.4.0.4\n+version: 1.4.1.0\n ---\n \n # Executor config\n@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@ This feature belongs to the executor group and is catalogued as F001 in the `run\n \n Schema, parsing, defaults, supported flags, sandbox and permission-mode normalization.\n \n+`EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES` sits beside `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` and records, for each executor kind, its binary, prompt channel (argv, stdin or a prompt file), log format, cost source, effort surface, sandbox surface and resume. Resume is artifact resume for every kind: no builder passes a model-session resume flag. A table-driven conformance test checks every record against the fan-out command builders, the single-iteration dispatcher and the provider-cost reader, so a builder that drifts from its record fails the test. The cost reader returns a cost only for opencode and claude; every other kind reads unknown, never zero.\n+\n The implementation is source-backed and covered by runtime-owned tests under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/`. Treat this as shipped behavior, not a roadmap claim.\n \n ---\n@@ -43,6 +45,7 @@ The implementation is source-backed and covered by runtime-owned tests under `.s\n | File | Type | Role |\n |---|---|---|\n | `tests/unit/executor-config.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Primary regression coverage for Executor config. |\n+| `tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Conformance of each kind's capability record to the builders and the cost reader. |\n \n ---\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\nindex c192006ae21..9eeec018001 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"composite convergence vote\"\n importance_tier: important\n contextType: implementation\n-version: 1.11.25.0\n+version: 1.11.28.0\n ---\n \n # Deep Review Convergence\n@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ Every pivot dispatches three seats, or six when its first attempt misses quorum,\n \n #### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n \n-`step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n+`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_convergence` in `deep-review.yaml` runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event), and on a BLOCKED decision it appends a `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event through the append gateway, which projects to this row. The workflow never writes it by hand. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n \n ```json\n {\n@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ Every pivot dispatches three seats, or six when its first attempt misses quorum,\n ```\n \n - `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n-- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reduc