{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202376852,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa6648900027RW4W0fD2AUFaU","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa663adc001Q1QBR3I1bORSnc","type":"tool","id":"call_1cae8fd462024e06cc7f713e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 3 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-006: correctness**\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog`\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the command docs and compiled contracts, `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md`, `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`, `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md`, `deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:108-112` and `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:115-119` (`--executor` sandbox paragraph)\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown:284-290,363-370`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown:279-285,342-349`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt:142,222`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:131,195`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:137-180,453-458`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:284-289`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md:113-160`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md:97-101`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:26-48`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197,203,216,231`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29-53`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:61,81`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The executor catalog claims the conformance test fails on any builder drift, but its `permission-mode` assertion cannot see a same-mode collapse** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:29` -- The catalog states that \"a builder that drifts from its record fails the test\". For the `permission-mode` surface the test asserts only that `read-only` differs from `danger-full-access` (`executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:308-312`), so a builder that emits the same permission mode for `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` passes. That is exactly the dsh collapse reported as R1-P2-001, and the catalog's stated safety net does not catch it. The claim is actionable in one place: the assertion should compare all three modes pairwise for a `permission-mode` surface.\n   - Finding class: matrix/evidence\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \"permission-mode\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts` returns the single assertion pair at 308-312; no other test asserts the dsh permission mode for `workspace-write` against `danger-full-access`. The catalog sentence is the only place that claims drift detection for the record as a whole.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"executor adapter conformance test\", \"runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md\", \"dsh command builder\"]\n   - Case: a maintainer changes the dsh builder so `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` both emit `--permission-mode workspace-write` (the current state). The conformance suite stays green, and the catalog still tells the reader that drift cannot survive the suite.\n\n## Findings - Refined\n\n1. **R2-P2-001 refined: the feature catalog repeats the identity claim the projection contradicts** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29` -- The catalog says the gateway \"drops the row's `eventId`, `idempotencyKey`, `producer` and `authorityEpoch`\" and that \"None of the four is kept as a claim\". The drop applies to the envelope metadata only; the review record travels whole as `data.record` and the projection spreads it, so a model-written `eventId` or `idempotencyKey` survives in the projected row. This is the same root cause as R2-P2-001, now stated as a documented guarantee rather than only a code comment, so the fix must correct the catalog sentence as well as the projection or the strip.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: the catalog sentence and the code comment (`append-mode-event.cjs:104-107`) make the same claim; both are contradicted by the single projection spread at `deep-review-state-contract.ts:291-296`. No third statement of the claim was found.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"append-mode-event CLI\", \"runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md\", \"deep-review-state-contract projection\"]\n   - Case: an operator reads the catalog to learn what the state log can contain, concludes a model cannot put an `eventId` into a row, and writes a correlation check that trusts the state-log field.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:111`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md:97` | The three commits' doc claims match the code: the opencode sandbox paragraph matches the builder, the blocked-stop record is attributed to `convergence.cjs` with `--read-only` on a dry run, and the iteration row time is described as gateway-set with `claimedTimestamp`. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:29`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29` | Two catalog claims overstate what the code guarantees: the drift-detection sentence (P2-1) and the identity-drop sentence (refinement of R2-P2-001). The rest of the catalog checked (fanout-run, convergence-script, executor-config capability record) matches the builders. |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | - | The manual-testing playbooks describe operator scenarios, not a capability this node's code claims; no playbook claim was found to contradict the range. Recorded `notApplicable` rather than `pass` because no playbook was exercised. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288` already states that \"the deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes\". That corrects the iteration-1 edge-case note that the narrowing was undocumented: the behavior is documented, and R1-P2-001 stands only on the provenance mismatch (`sandboxMode` and `sandboxEnforcement` in `effectiveConfig`), not on the narrowing being hidden.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197,203` matches the fan-out builders: claude `--output-format stream-json --verbose`, opencode `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating` under `workspace-write`, and `danger-full-access` as plain `--auto` with no deny.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140,456` and `loop-state-and-gates.md:113,157` both attribute the blocked-stop record to `convergence.cjs` and name `--read-only` for the dry run, matching the YAML's `step_bind_convergence_write_arg`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Compiled contracts are generated.** `deep-review.contract.markdown` and `deep-research.contract.markdown` carry `sourceDigests` for `review.md`, the presentation asset and the YAML. Their body text matches the edited sources, so no hand-edit drift was found; a digest mismatch would be a generation failure, not a review finding.\n- **Two claude log formats are both correct.** `loop-protocol.md:287` describes `--output-format text` for the `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branch, which still emits text (`dispatch-iteration.cjs:375-376`), while the fan-out builder emits `stream-json` (`fanout-run.cjs:2923-2925`). The doc names the branch it describes, so this is not drift.\n- **`playbook_capability` marked `notApplicable`.** The playbooks in scope are operator procedures; none asserts a capability the range changed. Marking it `pass` would claim a check that was not run.\n- **Ratio denominator correction.** Iterations 1 and 2 reported `newFindingsRatio` on an iteration-local denominator (1.0 each). The contract compares new against accumulated findings, so this iteration uses the accumulated denominator and later iterations follow it. The earlier values overstate novelty, which delays a stop rather than forcing one; the correction is recorded here rather than rewritten, because the ledger is append-only.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Opencode sandbox docs.** `review.md:111`, `research.md:118`, both presentations, both compiled contracts and `loop-protocol.md:286` all describe the same behavior: `--auto` always, `workspace-write` denies `external_directory` to file tools but not Bash, `danger-full-access` adds no deny, `read-only` is refused.\n- **Blocked-stop attribution.** The convergence reference and the state-and-gates reference both name `convergence.cjs` as the producer and `--read-only` as the dry-run argument, matching the YAML binding.\n- **Iteration row time.** `state-jsonl.md:97` and `append-mode-event-script.md:33` both describe the gateway clock plus `claimedTimestamp`, matching `deep-review-state-contract.ts:291-296`.\n- **Executor capability catalog.** `executor-config.md:29` correctly describes the record's fields and the cost reader's opencode/claude-only cost, which matches `EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES` and `fanout-salvage.cjs`.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Compiled-contract drift.** Ruled out: the body text of both compiled contracts matches the edited `review.md`/`research.md` and presentation assets, and the digest headers were regenerated in the same commit.\n- **A separate finding for the dsh narrowing being undocumented.** Ruled out after reading `loop-protocol.md:288`, which documents it; the surviving issue is the provenance mismatch already recorded as R1-P2-001.\n- **A finding for the claude `--output-format` difference between dispatch paths.** Ruled out: the reference names the `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branch, and that branch still emits text.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (active, correctness covered; the reducer's breadth-first rule now returns to the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\n- Focus area: the trust boundary between the parent environment and the child for the three node files: `buildExecutorDispatchEnv`'s per-kind allowlist, the dsh persona patch path resolution under `.dsh/agents`, and whether an inherited `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` can re-enable a denied path.\n- Reason: all three depth-1 nodes now have one correctness visit and no P0/P1; the next pass should rotate to security on the node with the highest-blast surface.\n- Rotation status: correctness covered on F-1-002, F-1-004 and F-1-006; security next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (doc-to-code comparison found one overstated guarantee and one refinement); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: `executor-audit.ts` env allowlist and `buildExecutorDispatchEnv`, `fanout-run.cjs` dsh patch path construction, and the opencode inline-config merge.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 3 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-006: correctness**\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog`\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the command docs and compiled contracts, `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md`, `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`, `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md`, `deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md`, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:108-112` and `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:115-119` (`--executor` sandbox paragraph)\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.markdown:284-290,363-370`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown:279-285,342-349`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt:142,222`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:131,195`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:137-180,453-458`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:284-289`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md:113-160`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md:97-101`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:26-48`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197,203,216,231`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29-53`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:61,81`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The executor catalog claims the conformance test fails on any builder drift, but its `permission-mode` assertion cannot see a same-mode collapse** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:29` -- The catalog states that \\\"a builder that drifts from its record fails the test\\\". For the `permission-mode` surface the test asserts only that `read-only` differs from `danger-full-access` (`executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:308-312`), so a builder that emits the same permission mode for `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` passes. That is exactly the dsh collapse reported as R1-P2-001, and the catalog's stated safety net does not catch it. The claim is actionable in one place: the assertion should compare all three modes pairwise for a `permission-mode` surface.\\n   - Finding class: matrix/evidence\\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"permission-mode\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts` returns the single assertion pair at 308-312; no other test asserts the dsh permission mode for `workspace-write` against `danger-full-access`. The catalog sentence is the only place that claims drift detection for the record as a whole.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"executor adapter conformance test\\\", \\\"runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md\\\", \\\"dsh command builder\\\"]\\n   - Case: a maintainer changes the dsh builder so `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` both emit `--permission-mode workspace-write` (the current state). The conformance suite stays green, and the catalog still tells the reader that drift cannot survive the suite.\\n\\n## Findings - Refined\\n\\n1. **R2-P2-001 refined: the feature catalog repeats the identity claim the projection contradicts** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29` -- The catalog says the gateway \\\"drops the row's `eventId`, `idempotencyKey`, `producer` and `authorityEpoch`\\\" and that \\\"None of the four is kept as a claim\\\". The drop applies to the envelope metadata only; the review record travels whole as `data.record` and the projection spreads it, so a model-written `eventId` or `idempotencyKey` survives in the projected row. This is the same root cause as R2-P2-001, now stated as a documented guarantee rather than only a code comment, so the fix must correct the catalog sentence as well as the projection or the strip.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: the catalog sentence and the code comment (`append-mode-event.cjs:104-107`) make the same claim; both are contradicted by the single projection spread at `deep-review-state-contract.ts:291-296`. No third statement of the claim was found.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"append-mode-event CLI\\\", \\\"runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md\\\", \\\"deep-review-state-contract projection\\\"]\\n   - Case: an operator reads the catalog to learn what the state log can contain, concludes a model cannot put an `eventId` into a row, and writes a correlation check that trusts the state-log field.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:111`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md:97` | The three commits' doc claims match the code: the opencode sandbox paragraph matches the builder, the blocked-stop record is attributed to `convergence.cjs` with `--read-only` on a dry run, and the iteration row time is described as gateway-set with `claimedTimestamp`. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/executor/executor-config.md:29`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29` | Two catalog claims overstate what the code guarantees: the drift-detection sentence (P2-1) and the identity-drop sentence (refinement of R2-P2-001). The rest of the catalog checked (fanout-run, convergence-script, executor-config capability record) matches the builders. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | - | The manual-testing playbooks describe operator scenarios, not a capability this node's code claims; no playbook claim was found to contradict the range. Recorded `notApplicable` rather than `pass` because no playbook was exercised. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288` already states that \\\"the deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes\\\". That corrects the iteration-1 edge-case note that the narrowing was undocumented: the behavior is documented, and R1-P2-001 stands only on the provenance mismatch (`sandboxMode` and `sandboxEnforcement` in `effectiveConfig`), not on the narrowing being hidden.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197,203` matches the fan-out builders: claude `--output-format stream-json --verbose`, opencode `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating` under `workspace-write`, and `danger-full-access` as plain `--auto` with no deny.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140,456` and `loop-state-and-gates.md:113,157` both attribute the blocked-stop record to `convergence.cjs` and name `--read-only` for the dry run, matching the YAML's `step_bind_convergence_write_arg`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Compiled contracts are generated.** `deep-review.contract.markdown` and `deep-research.contract.markdown` carry `sourceDigests` for `review.md`, the presentation asset and the YAML. Their body text matches the edited sources, so no hand-edit drift was found; a digest mismatch would be a generation failure, not a review finding.\\n- **Two claude log formats are both correct.** `loop-protocol.md:287` describes `--output-format text` for the `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branch, which still emits text (`dispatch-iteration.cjs:375-376`), while the fan-out builder emits `stream-json` (`fanout-run.cjs:2923-2925`). The doc names the branch it describes, so this is not drift.\\n- **`playbook_capability` marked `notApplicable`.** The playbooks in scope are operator procedures; none asserts a capability the range changed. Marking it `pass` would claim a check that was not run.\\n- **Ratio denominator correction.** Iterations 1 and 2 reported `newFindingsRatio` on an iteration-local denominator (1.0 each). The contract compares new against accumulated findings, so this iteration uses the accumulated denominator and later iterations follow it. The earlier values overstate novelty, which delays a stop rather than forcing one; the correction is recorded here rather than rewritten, because the ledger is append-only.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Opencode sandbox docs.** `review.md:111`, `research.md:118`, both presentations, both compiled contracts and `loop-protocol.md:286` all describe the same behavior: `--auto` always, `workspace-write` denies `external_directory` to file tools but not Bash, `danger-full-access` adds no deny, `read-only` is refused.\\n- **Blocked-stop attribution.** The convergence reference and the state-and-gates reference both name `convergence.cjs` as the producer and `--read-only` as the dry-run argument, matching the YAML binding.\\n- **Iteration row time.** `state-jsonl.md:97` and `append-mode-event-script.md:33` both describe the gateway clock plus `claimedTimestamp`, matching `deep-review-state-contract.ts:291-296`.\\n- **Executor capability catalog.** `executor-config.md:29` correctly describes the record's fields and the cost reader's opencode/claude-only cost, which matches `EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES` and `fanout-salvage.cjs`.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Compiled-contract drift.** Ruled out: the body text of both compiled contracts matches the edited `review.md`/`research.md` and presentation assets, and the digest headers were regenerated in the same commit.\\n- **A separate finding for the dsh narrowing being undocumented.** Ruled out after reading `loop-protocol.md:288`, which documents it; the surviving issue is the provenance mismatch already recorded as R1-P2-001.\\n- **A finding for the claude `--output-format` difference between dispatch paths.** Ruled out: the reference names the `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branch, and that branch still emits text.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (active, correctness covered; the reducer's breadth-first rule now returns to the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\\n- Focus area: the trust boundary between the parent environment and the child for the three node files: `buildExecutorDispatchEnv`'s per-kind allowlist, the dsh persona patch path resolution under `.dsh/agents`, and whether an inherited `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` can re-enable a denied path.\\n- Reason: all three depth-1 nodes now have one correctness visit and no P0/P1; the next pass should rotate to security on the node with the highest-blast surface.\\n- Rotation status: correctness covered on F-1-002, F-1-004 and F-1-006; security next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (doc-to-code comparison found one overstated guarantee and one refinement); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: `executor-audit.ts` env allowlist and `buildExecutorDispatchEnv`, `fanout-run.cjs` dsh patch path construction, and the opencode inline-config merge.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202369680,"end":1795202376852}}}}
