{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795202422711,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"id":"prt_1fa6717b7001SKtOhzjInfN27a","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa671038001GcR2Mwi8sT1Skf","type":"step-start","snapshot":"1f50c59920c277eec2587bc98346be3b9fe98bf6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202425748,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa672230002orYic0Kj1TbViE","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa671038001GcR2Mwi8sT1Skf","type":"tool","id":"call_9517e66a94126c44097cbabb","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"cli-pi\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt | head -5; echo \"=== pi sandbox docs ===\"; grep -rn \"cli-pi\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md | head -5; echo \"=== env common allowlist ===\"; sed -n '100,142p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts"},"output":"50:  executor: native  # one of: native | cli-codex | cli-claude-code | cli-opencode | cli-cursor | cli-devin | cli-pi | cli-deepseek-harness | cli-mistral-vibe, the last one fan-out only (`EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`)\n139:   |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.kind (`native` | `cli-codex` | `cli-claude-code` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-cursor` | `cli-devin` | `cli-pi` | `cli-deepseek-harness` | `cli-mistral-vibe`. Every kind runs in `:auto` and `:confirm`, `cli-deepseek-harness` as a single lineage or a fan-out and `cli-mistral-vibe` only as a fan-out lineage. `EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` is authoritative)\n177:   - Invalid combinations fail fast with clear errors: an unknown executor kind (schema enum), a field the kind does not support (`EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, e.g. `--service-tier` on `cli-cursor`), an off-allowlist model on `cli-cursor`/`cli-devin`/`cli-pi`, and a missing executor binary\n226:     G) cli-pi — requires `pi`. Model must be on the enforced allowlist. `reasoningEffort` maps to `--thinking`. No `--service-tier`, no sandbox flag.\n228:     D-H build their commands through the shared fan-out command builder (`LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`). Per-kind flag support (`EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`) and the cli-cursor/cli-devin/cli-pi model allowlists (`CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS`) are owned by `executor-config.ts`; this contract does not restate them. Off-allowlist model or missing binary fails closed — a requested CLI executor never degrades to native.\n=== pi sandbox docs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:287:- `cli-claude-code`: `claude -p \"$(cat prompt)\" --model X --permission-mode <mode> --output-format text` with optional `--effort Y`. The permission mode resolves from `--sandbox-mode`: unset or `workspace-write` runs `acceptEdits` so iteration writes succeed, `read-only` runs `plan` and `danger-full-access` runs `bypassPermissions`. The inline workflow branches are not the complete schema: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` (experimental) also have inline branches that run `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, and `cli-mistral-vibe` runs only as a fan-out lineage. The executor-kind authority is `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`).\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288:- Sandbox on those `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branches: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` resolve the requested `--sandbox-mode` and map it to the kind's own read-only or write surface, which is an OS sandbox only on codex, cursor and the deepseek harness. An unset mode resolves to `workspace-write`, so the iteration can write its iteration file, delta and state record. A requested `read-only` is passed through, never widened, and the iteration then fails at the post-dispatch artifact gate rather than gaining write access. The deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes.\n=== env common allowlist ===\n  // a fabricated CLI-native one.\n  'cli-cursor': ['SPECKIT_CURSOR_STATE_DIR'],\n  // `devin --help` exposes DEVIN_MODEL, DEVIN_PERMISSION_MODE, and DEVIN_SANDBOX\n  // only (checked live) — no DEVIN_HOME-style state-dir override exists, so the\n  // repo-owned detection var is the sole entry rather than a fabricated one.\n  'cli-devin': ['SPECKIT_DEVIN_STATE_DIR'],\n  'cli-pi': ['SPECKIT_PI_STATE_DIR'],\n  'cli-deepseek-harness': ['SPECKIT_DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_STATE_DIR', 'DSH_HOME'],\n  // Vibe reads its own home override, so an inherited VIBE_HOME is lineage state and not\n  // a pass-through variable.\n  'cli-mistral-vibe': ['SPECKIT_MISTRAL_VIBE_STATE_DIR', 'VIBE_HOME'],\n};\n\nconst EXECUTOR_DEFAULT_HOME_DIR_BY_KIND: Partial<Record<ExecutorKind, string>> = {\n  'cli-codex': '.codex',\n  'cli-claude-code': '.claude',\n  'cli-opencode': '.opencode',\n  'cli-cursor': '.cursor',\n  'cli-devin': '.devin',\n  'cli-pi': '.pi',\n  'cli-deepseek-harness': '.dsh',\n  'cli-mistral-vibe': '.vibe',\n};\n\n// Two of the five recursion layers ask \"is the caller sitting inside this CLI right now\" —\n// ancestry and lockfile. Pi has no in-process delegation of its own, so for pi that question\n// has no useful answer left: refusing on it leaves a Pi session with no way to hand work out\n// at all. The layers that bound a runaway spawn chain, lineage and stack, are deliberately\n// NOT listed here and still apply to every kind, this one included.\nconst SELF_PRESENCE_EXEMPT_KINDS: ReadonlySet<ExecutorKind> = new Set<ExecutorKind>(['cli-pi']);\n\nconst EXECUTOR_COMMON_ENV_ALLOWLIST = new Set([\n  'PATH',\n  'HOME',\n  'LANG',\n  'TMPDIR',\n  'NODE_PATH',\n  'TERM',\n  // macOS credential auth for CLI executors (e.g. claude OAuth keychain lookup)\n  // keys on the user identity + CoreFoundation locale; without these a dispatched\n  // CLI reports \"Not logged in\" even with a valid config dir.\n  'USER',\n  'LOGNAME',\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"50:  executor: native  # one of: native | cli-codex | cli-claude-code | cli-opencode | cli-cursor | cli-devin | cli-pi | cli-deepseek-harness | cli-mistral-vibe, the last one fan-out only (`EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`)\n139:   |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.kind (`native` | `cli-codex` | `cli-claude-code` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-cursor` | `cli-devin` | `cli-pi` | `cli-deepseek-harness` | `cli-mistral-vibe`. Every kind runs in `:auto` and `:confirm`, `cli-deepseek-harness` as a single lineage or a fan-out and `cli-mistral-vibe` only as a fan-out lineage. `EXECUTOR_KINDS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` is authoritative)\n177:   - Invalid combinations fail fast with clear errors: an unknown executor kind (schema enum), a field the kind does not support (`EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, e.g. `--service-tier` on `cli-cursor`), an off-allowlist model on `cli-cursor`/`cli-devin`/`cli-pi`, and a missing executor binary\n226:     G) cli-pi — requires `pi`. Model must be on the enforced allowlist. `reasoningEffort` maps to `--thinking`. No `--service-tier`, no sandbox flag.\n228:     D-H build their commands through the shared fan-out command builder (`LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`). Per-kind flag support (`EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`) and the cli-cursor/cli-devin/cli-pi model allowlists (`CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS`) are owned by `executor-config.ts`; this contract does not restate them. Off-allowlist model or missing binary fails closed — a requested CLI executor never degrades to native.\n=== pi sandbox docs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:287:- `cli-claude-code`: `claude -p \"$(cat prompt)\" --model X --permission-mode <mode> --output-format text` with optional `--effort Y`. The permission mode resolves from `--sandbox-mode`: unset or `workspace-write` runs `acceptEdits` so iteration writes succeed, `read-only` runs `plan` and `danger-full-access` runs `bypassPermissions`. The inline workflow branches are not the complete schema: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` (experimental) also have inline branches that run `dispatch-iteration.cjs`, and `cli-mistral-vibe` runs only as a fan-out lineage. The executor-kind authority is `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`).\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288:- Sandbox on those `dispatch-iteration.cjs` branches: `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` resolve the requested `--sandbox-mode` and map it to the kind's own read-only or write surface, which is an OS sandbox only on codex, cursor and the deepseek harness. An unset mode resolves to `workspace-write`, so the iteration can write its iteration file, delta and state record. A requested `read-only` is passed through, never widened, and the iteration then fails at the post-dispatch artifact gate rather than gaining write access. The deepseek harness narrows `danger-full-access` to `workspace-write`, and pi builds the same command for both write modes.\n=== env common allowlist ===\n  // a fabricated CLI-native one.\n  'cli-cursor': ['SPECKIT_CURSOR_STATE_DIR'],\n  // `devin --help` exposes DEVIN_MODEL, DEVIN_PERMISSION_MODE, and DEVIN_SANDBOX\n  // only (checked live) — no DEVIN_HOME-style state-dir override exists, so the\n  // repo-owned detection var is the sole entry rather than a fabricated one.\n  'cli-devin': ['SPECKIT_DEVIN_STATE_DIR'],\n  'cli-pi': ['SPECKIT_PI_STATE_DIR'],\n  'cli-deepseek-harness': ['SPECKIT_DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_STATE_DIR', 'DSH_HOME'],\n  // Vibe reads its own home override, so an inherited VIBE_HOME is lineage state and not\n  // a pass-through variable.\n  'cli-mistral-vibe': ['SPECKIT_MISTRAL_VIBE_STATE_DIR', 'VIBE_HOME'],\n};\n\nconst EXECUTOR_DEFAULT_HOME_DIR_BY_KIND: Partial<Record<ExecutorKind, string>> = {\n  'cli-codex': '.codex',\n  'cli-claude-code': '.claude',\n  'cli-opencode': '.opencode',\n  'cli-cursor': '.cursor',\n  'cli-devin': '.devin',\n  'cli-pi': '.pi',\n  'cli-deepseek-harness': '.dsh',\n  'cli-mistral-vibe': '.vibe',\n};\n\n// Two of the five recursion layers ask \"is the caller sitting inside this CLI right now\" —\n// ancestry and lockfile. Pi has no in-process delegation of its own, so for pi that question\n// has no useful answer left: refusing on it leaves a Pi session with no way to hand work out\n// at all. The layers that bound a runaway spawn chain, lineage and stack, are deliberately\n// NOT listed here and still apply to every kind, this one included.\nconst SELF_PRESENCE_EXEMPT_KINDS: ReadonlySet<ExecutorKind> = new Set<ExecutorKind>(['cli-pi']);\n\nconst EXECUTOR_COMMON_ENV_ALLOWLIST = new Set([\n  'PATH',\n  'HOME',\n  'LANG',\n  'TMPDIR',\n  'NODE_PATH',\n  'TERM',\n  // macOS credential auth for CLI executors (e.g. claude OAuth keychain lookup)\n  // keys on the user identity + CoreFoundation locale; without these a dispatched\n  // CLI reports \"Not logged in\" even with a valid config dir.\n  'USER',\n  'LOGNAME',\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"cli-pi\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt | head -5; echo \\\"=== pi sandbox docs ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"cli-pi\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md | head -5; echo \\\"=== env common allowlist ===\\\"; sed -n '100,142p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202425392,"end":1795202425748}}}}
