{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202490331,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa681147001bmz0Frq6dz4tdg","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa68061600145PmOrxtNMvoUk","type":"tool","id":"call_1ec6ee614db46e014669f702","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 5 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-004: security**\n- Dimension: security\n- Frontier node: F-1-004 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts`\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the three node files, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs:240-330,429-495,532-540` (authority admission, ledger construction, cutover binding, canonical-envelope passthrough, review meta)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:540-610,640-700` (pre-append checks, authorization request, epoch source, projection refresh)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:370-440` (`findIdempotentReplay`, `eventContentDigest`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts:280-310` (projection row construction)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29-33` | The catalog's identity and timing description matches the CLI's behavior for both the model-row and canonical-envelope paths, including the documented caller-identity exception for a canonical envelope. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:607` builds the authorization request with `authorityEpoch: admission.epoch`, the epoch the gateway admitted, not the caller's `identity.authorityEpoch`. A forged epoch in a canonical envelope is therefore recorded as data and never used to authorize the append.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:669-672` resolves the projection contract from `options.runDirectory`, so the projection writes inside the run the caller named rather than a path derived from the event payload.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs:270-290` constructs the ledger and authorization gateway with `rootDirectory: runDirectory`, so every ledger, audit and fence file lands under the run directory the CLI was given.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **`--run-directory` is caller-controlled.** The gateway does not sandbox the caller; it orders and authorizes writes inside the directory the caller names. The agent invoking it already holds filesystem write authority, so the gateway is not the containment boundary — the fan-out write-containment guard is. Recorded as a boundary, not a finding.\n- **Cutover binding falls back to `process.cwd()`.** When the run directory cannot resolve a binding, the CLI retries from the working directory rather than fabricating an identity. The fallback is deliberate and fails closed if both attempts fail; it does not let an append proceed unauthorized.\n- **Canonical envelopes keep caller identity.** The catalog documents this, and the authorization path ignores the caller's epoch, so the exception is provenance-only.\n- **`eventContentDigest` transforms both sides identically.** A caller cannot make two different payloads compare equal by injecting a head value, because the same nulling applies to the existing and incoming payloads.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Authorization epoch is server-side.** The admission epoch, not the envelope's, authorizes the append.\n- **Projection path is run-scoped.** The contract is resolved from the run directory, and the projection writes the state log there.\n- **Idempotency conflict is refused before append.** The conflict return precedes the authorize/append loop.\n- **Ledger, audit and fence files share one root.** All three are constructed from `runDirectory`, so a run cannot scatter its ledger across directories.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A privilege escalation through a forged `identity.authorityEpoch`.** Ruled out: the authorization request uses `admission.epoch`, and the caller's value is never read for authorization.\n- **A path-traversal write through the projection.** Ruled out: the projection contract and the state-log path are both resolved from the run directory, and no event field contributes a path segment.\n- **A cross-run append through `--run-directory`.** Ruled out as a gateway finding: the caller already holds filesystem write authority, so naming another directory is not an escalation the gateway can prevent; containment is the fan-out guard's job.\n- **A digest-collision replay bypass.** Ruled out: the digest is computed over the payload with the same head-nulling on both sides, and a different payload produces a different digest.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (active, correctness covered; the reducer's breadth-first rule selects the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\n- Focus area: docs and contracts as a security surface: whether any shipped help, reference or playbook tells an operator a confinement control exists when it does not, or omits one that does, beyond the pi line already reported as R4-P2-001.\n- Reason: F-1-004 security is clean; the docs node has had only a correctness pass and carries the operator-facing security claims.\n- Rotation status: F-1-004 correctness and security covered; F-1-006 security next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (the epoch-source check is the decisive evidence); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: the sandbox and containment paragraphs in both presentations, `loop-protocol.md` §Executor Resolution, and the manual-testing playbooks.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 005\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 5 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-004: security**\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Frontier node: F-1-004 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts`\\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the three node files, `runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs:240-330,429-495,532-540` (authority admission, ledger construction, cutover binding, canonical-envelope passthrough, review meta)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:540-610,640-700` (pre-append checks, authorization request, epoch source, projection refresh)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:370-440` (`findIdempotentReplay`, `eventContentDigest`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts:280-310` (projection row construction)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/append-mode-event-script.md:29-33` | The catalog's identity and timing description matches the CLI's behavior for both the model-row and canonical-envelope paths, including the documented caller-identity exception for a canonical envelope. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:607` builds the authorization request with `authorityEpoch: admission.epoch`, the epoch the gateway admitted, not the caller's `identity.authorityEpoch`. A forged epoch in a canonical envelope is therefore recorded as data and never used to authorize the append.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts:669-672` resolves the projection contract from `options.runDirectory`, so the projection writes inside the run the caller named rather than a path derived from the event payload.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs:270-290` constructs the ledger and authorization gateway with `rootDirectory: runDirectory`, so every ledger, audit and fence file lands under the run directory the CLI was given.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **`--run-directory` is caller-controlled.** The gateway does not sandbox the caller; it orders and authorizes writes inside the directory the caller names. The agent invoking it already holds filesystem write authority, so the gateway is not the containment boundary — the fan-out write-containment guard is. Recorded as a boundary, not a finding.\\n- **Cutover binding falls back to `process.cwd()`.** When the run directory cannot resolve a binding, the CLI retries from the working directory rather than fabricating an identity. The fallback is deliberate and fails closed if both attempts fail; it does not let an append proceed unauthorized.\\n- **Canonical envelopes keep caller identity.** The catalog documents this, and the authorization path ignores the caller's epoch, so the exception is provenance-only.\\n- **`eventContentDigest` transforms both sides identically.** A caller cannot make two different payloads compare equal by injecting a head value, because the same nulling applies to the existing and incoming payloads.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Authorization epoch is server-side.** The admission epoch, not the envelope's, authorizes the append.\\n- **Projection path is run-scoped.** The contract is resolved from the run directory, and the projection writes the state log there.\\n- **Idempotency conflict is refused before append.** The conflict return precedes the authorize/append loop.\\n- **Ledger, audit and fence files share one root.** All three are constructed from `runDirectory`, so a run cannot scatter its ledger across directories.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A privilege escalation through a forged `identity.authorityEpoch`.** Ruled out: the authorization request uses `admission.epoch`, and the caller's value is never read for authorization.\\n- **A path-traversal write through the projection.** Ruled out: the projection contract and the state-log path are both resolved from the run directory, and no event field contributes a path segment.\\n- **A cross-run append through `--run-directory`.** Ruled out as a gateway finding: the caller already holds filesystem write authority, so naming another directory is not an escalation the gateway can prevent; containment is the fan-out guard's job.\\n- **A digest-collision replay bypass.** Ruled out: the digest is computed over the payload with the same head-nulling on both sides, and a different payload produces a different digest.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (active, correctness covered; the reducer's breadth-first rule selects the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\\n- Focus area: docs and contracts as a security surface: whether any shipped help, reference or playbook tells an operator a confinement control exists when it does not, or omits one that does, beyond the pi line already reported as R4-P2-001.\\n- Reason: F-1-004 security is clean; the docs node has had only a correctness pass and carries the operator-facing security claims.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-004 correctness and security covered; F-1-006 security next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (the epoch-source check is the decisive evidence); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: the sandbox and containment paragraphs in both presentations, `loop-protocol.md` §Executor Resolution, and the manual-testing playbooks.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202486599,"end":1795202490331}}}}
