{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202531212,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa68b1fe0014mB1epvsv30a7K","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa68a6ba0016fwD5JpNnJeKo7","type":"tool","id":"call_ffa89cec17a172eb2f1283db","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 006\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 6 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-006: security**\n- Dimension: security\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog`\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the command docs, both presentations, `loop-protocol.md`, `fanout-run.md`, the prompt-pack template, and the manual-testing playbooks.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:111`, `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:118` (opencode sandbox paragraph)\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt:142,222,226`, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:131,195,199`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:284-289`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:102-109`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:14,47,104`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/command-flow-stress-tests/resource-map-coverage-gate.md:11-72`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:286-288`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` | Every confinement claim found names the control it relies on and its limit: the opencode deny is called compensating, never preventive; Bash is named as unconfined; read-only is named as refused for opencode and as a tool allowlist for pi. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:14,47,104` | The playbooks use \"sandbox\" only for the fixture directory and the SKIP criterion; none claims a confinement property the runtime does not have. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` | The fan-out catalog's containment paragraph matches the builder and the preview's `sandboxEnforcement` value. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:102-109` states the write contract as a prompt-level rule with an explicit \"BANNED OPERATIONS\" list and a scope-violation protocol, and `loop-protocol.md:286` names that contract as one of the three real containment layers rather than an OS sandbox. The two statements agree.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` describes the opencode default as \"`--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`\" and says the preview records `compensating`, never `preventive`, which matches `fanout-run.cjs:3034` and `sandboxEnforcementFor`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288` names the dsh narrowing and the pi same-command behavior, so the two kinds whose sandbox mode does not map one-to-one are documented where an operator would look.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **`read-only` is not one behavior across kinds.** It is a pass-through flag on codex and cursor, a permission mode on claude and dsh, a tool allowlist on pi, and a refusal on opencode. The docs state each case in the kind's own bullet, and the general sentence at `loop-protocol.md:288` is qualified by the opencode bullet above it. No contradiction found.\n- **The prompt-level write contract is not a sandbox.** It is documented as instruction-following plus post-dispatch validation, and the review's own containment guard is the enforcement layer. Treating the prompt text as a security boundary would be the error; the docs do not make that claim.\n- **Playbook \"sandbox\" means a fixture directory.** The word appears only in that sense and in the SKIP criterion, so it cannot be read as a confinement claim.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Opencode containment description.** Command docs, both presentations, both compiled contracts and the protocol reference all describe the same three layers and the same Bash limitation.\n- **`sandboxEnforcement` vocabulary.** The catalog uses `compensating` and `preventive` with the same meaning the code assigns, and never calls a compensating control preventive.\n- **Playbooks.** No playbook asserts a confinement property; the SKIP criterion is about unavailable dependencies, not about sandboxing.\n- **Prompt pack.** The write contract is stated as a rule with a violation protocol, not as an enforced boundary.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A doc claiming an OS sandbox where only a permission rule exists.** Ruled out: every opencode and pi statement names the control as a permission rule or tool allowlist and names Bash as unconfined.\n- **A doc omitting the opencode read-only refusal.** Ruled out: `review.md`, both presentations, both compiled contracts and `loop-protocol.md:286` all state it.\n- **A playbook claiming confinement.** Ruled out: the word is used only for fixture directories and the SKIP criterion.\n- **A security finding from the pi help line.** Already recorded as R4-P2-001 in the F-1-002 security pass; re-reporting it here would double-count the same sentence.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (open, zero visits; the admitted child of F-1-002)\n- Focus area: the sandbox enforcement label matrix across every executor kind and all three sandbox modes — whether `sandboxEnforcementFor` reports `preventive`, `compensating` or `none` correctly for each kind, including the kinds whose builder emits a different mode than the one requested.\n- Reason: F-1-006 security is clean; the frontier's only unvisited node is the admitted child, and its question is the one R1-P2-001 opened.\n- Rotation status: F-1-006 correctness and security covered; F-2-007 correctness next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (claim-by-claim comparison found no overstatement); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: `sandboxEnforcementFor` and every builder's `confines`/`compensatingControl` argument, plus the conformance test's per-surface assertions.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 006\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 6 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-006: security**\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Frontier node: F-1-006 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog`\\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the command docs, both presentations, `loop-protocol.md`, `fanout-run.md`, the prompt-pack template, and the manual-testing playbooks.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:111`, `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:118` (opencode sandbox paragraph)\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt:142,222,226`, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:131,195,199`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:284-289`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:110,197`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:102-109`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:14,47,104`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/command-flow-stress-tests/resource-map-coverage-gate.md:11-72`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:286-288`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` | Every confinement claim found names the control it relies on and its limit: the opencode deny is called compensating, never preventive; Bash is named as unconfined; read-only is named as refused for opencode and as a tool allowlist for pi. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:14,47,104` | The playbooks use \\\"sandbox\\\" only for the fixture directory and the SKIP criterion; none claims a confinement property the runtime does not have. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` | The fan-out catalog's containment paragraph matches the builder and the preview's `sandboxEnforcement` value. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:102-109` states the write contract as a prompt-level rule with an explicit \\\"BANNED OPERATIONS\\\" list and a scope-violation protocol, and `loop-protocol.md:286` names that contract as one of the three real containment layers rather than an OS sandbox. The two statements agree.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` describes the opencode default as \\\"`--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`\\\" and says the preview records `compensating`, never `preventive`, which matches `fanout-run.cjs:3034` and `sandboxEnforcementFor`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:288` names the dsh narrowing and the pi same-command behavior, so the two kinds whose sandbox mode does not map one-to-one are documented where an operator would look.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **`read-only` is not one behavior across kinds.** It is a pass-through flag on codex and cursor, a permission mode on claude and dsh, a tool allowlist on pi, and a refusal on opencode. The docs state each case in the kind's own bullet, and the general sentence at `loop-protocol.md:288` is qualified by the opencode bullet above it. No contradiction found.\\n- **The prompt-level write contract is not a sandbox.** It is documented as instruction-following plus post-dispatch validation, and the review's own containment guard is the enforcement layer. Treating the prompt text as a security boundary would be the error; the docs do not make that claim.\\n- **Playbook \\\"sandbox\\\" means a fixture directory.** The word appears only in that sense and in the SKIP criterion, so it cannot be read as a confinement claim.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Opencode containment description.** Command docs, both presentations, both compiled contracts and the protocol reference all describe the same three layers and the same Bash limitation.\\n- **`sandboxEnforcement` vocabulary.** The catalog uses `compensating` and `preventive` with the same meaning the code assigns, and never calls a compensating control preventive.\\n- **Playbooks.** No playbook asserts a confinement property; the SKIP criterion is about unavailable dependencies, not about sandboxing.\\n- **Prompt pack.** The write contract is stated as a rule with a violation protocol, not as an enforced boundary.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A doc claiming an OS sandbox where only a permission rule exists.** Ruled out: every opencode and pi statement names the control as a permission rule or tool allowlist and names Bash as unconfined.\\n- **A doc omitting the opencode read-only refusal.** Ruled out: `review.md`, both presentations, both compiled contracts and `loop-protocol.md:286` all state it.\\n- **A playbook claiming confinement.** Ruled out: the word is used only for fixture directories and the SKIP criterion.\\n- **A security finding from the pi help line.** Already recorded as R4-P2-001 in the F-1-002 security pass; re-reporting it here would double-count the same sentence.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (open, zero visits; the admitted child of F-1-002)\\n- Focus area: the sandbox enforcement label matrix across every executor kind and all three sandbox modes — whether `sandboxEnforcementFor` reports `preventive`, `compensating` or `none` correctly for each kind, including the kinds whose builder emits a different mode than the one requested.\\n- Reason: F-1-006 security is clean; the frontier's only unvisited node is the admitted child, and its question is the one R1-P2-001 opened.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-006 correctness and security covered; F-2-007 correctness next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (claim-by-claim comparison found no overstatement); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: `sandboxEnforcementFor` and every builder's `confines`/`compensatingControl` argument, plus the conformance test's per-surface assertions.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time"