rd by its own clock. Any time field on the record, `occurredAt` included, never sets the ledger event time. The ledger projection writes the event time as `timestamp` and keeps the record's own stamp as `claimedTimestamp`, so a wrong or future stamp stays visible without timing the row. Only `type: \"iteration\"` records are timed this way. The workflow's own rows, such as `iteration_start` and the dispatch and containment event rows, keep the `timestamp` their writer gave them.\n\n**Legacy field:** `run`, the older name for `iteration`. Readers still accept it and the fan-out stop-policy validator does not; new records write `iteration`. Event records keep their own `run` field.\n\n**Optional fields:** `parentSessionId`, `continuedFromRun`, `findingsRefined`, `findingRefs`, `traceabilityChecks`, `coverage`, `noveltyJustification`, `ruledOut`, `focusTrack`, `scoreEstimate`, `segment`, `convergenceSignals`, `graphEvents`, `claimedTimestamp` (written by the ledger projection, never by the agent)\n\n| Required Field | Type | Description |\n|---------------|------|-------------|\n| mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"decision\":\"CONTINUE\",\"reason\":\"noStopCandidate\",\"counters\":{\"stuckCount\":1,\"consecutiveFailureCount\":0}}\n\n\nFRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-1-004 at depth 1 of 3, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/mode-append-gateway/append-mode-event.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts. Review dimension for this node: traceability.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-1-004: traceability\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-004\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows 