{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202695752,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa6b35bd0028iT3iqiH8cfUEo","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa6b2080001K2BWop1tqEdR3O","type":"tool","id":"call_0733526b3f2d801cc3b6dd29","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 010\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 10 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-002: maintainability**\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 1, consecutive failures 0.\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the three node files, `executor-config.vitest.ts`, `combo-matrix.vitest.ts`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112-143,197-307,379-430,524-562,620-659` (flag support, capability record, allowlists)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3050-3070,3109-3130,3231-3245,3350-3390,3450-3456` (mirrored allowlists and provider maps)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-config.vitest.ts:966-1118` (allowlist content assertions)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:66-110` (per-model command construction)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:66-74` | The hand-duplicated allowlists are covered by a parity check in the direction that matters: every model in the TypeScript list is built through the fan-out builder, so a model missing from the fan-out set fails the suite. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:70-74` maps `CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DSH_SUPPORTED_MODELS` and `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` into the per-kind model matrix, and the suite builds a command for each entry. A model present in the TypeScript list but absent from the fan-out set throws \"not in the enforced allowlist\" and fails the test, so the duplication is guarded in the fail-closed direction.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-config.vitest.ts:966-1118` pins each allowlist's exact contents, so an accidental removal is caught even before the builder runs.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:191-196` states that the capability record is checked against the builders by a conformance test rather than read by them, which is the documented design for the duplication.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **The reverse parity direction is untested.** A model present in the fan-out set but absent from the TypeScript list would not fail a test. That direction is fail-open only in the sense that the fan-out would accept a model the config rejects; the config is the gate, so the entry is unreachable. Not a finding.\n- **`EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` and `EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES[].sandboxSurface` are parallel records.** They are not derivable from each other — claude's `permission-mode` is preventive, devin's is not — so the duplication is intentional and documented at `executor-config.ts:281-296`.\n- **The capability record is documentation-as-code.** It is read by the conformance test and the catalog, not by the builders, which the record's own comment states. A reader expecting runtime enforcement from it is reading it wrong.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Allowlist duplication is bounded and tested.** Four mirrored lists, each pinned by content assertions and exercised through the builder.\n- **Comment accuracy after the range.** The comments the range rewrote (`executor-config.ts:117-142,281-306`, `fanout-run.cjs:2973-2975,3005-3008`) describe the code beside them.\n- **No dead exports.** Every exported allowlist and predicate has a test or a builder consumer.\n- **Capability record shape.** One frozen record per kind, with a table-driven conformance test, so a new kind cannot be added without a record.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A maintainability finding for the mirrored allowlists.** Ruled out: the fail-closed direction is tested through the builder, and the fail-open direction is unreachable because the config gates first.\n- **A finding for the single-member `ExecutorResumeMode` union.** Ruled out: it documents the contract that no builder resumes a provider session, and the conformance test asserts it for every kind.\n- **A finding for the lazy `require` inside `sandboxEnforcementFor`.** Ruled out: it is the documented way a CJS script loads the TypeScript record, and Node caches the module.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Frontier node: F-1-004 (active; the reducer's breadth-first rule selects the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\n- Focus area: the gateway's maintainability: whether `GATEWAY_IDENTITY_FIELDS` is a denylist that a future identity field would slip past, whether `eventContentDigest`'s head-nulling is explained where a maintainer will find it, and whether the conflict path's stderr write duplicates the JSON line.\n- Reason: F-1-002 maintainability is clean; the gateway node has three dimensions covered and maintainability is its last.\n- Rotation status: F-1-002 all four dimensions covered; F-1-004 maintainability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (parity-test tracing closed the duplication question); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: `GATEWAY_IDENTITY_FIELDS`, `eventContentDigest`, and the conflict stderr path.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 010\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 10 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-1-002: maintainability**\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Frontier node: F-1-002 (depth 1 of 3), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`\\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 1, consecutive failures 0.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the three node files, `executor-config.vitest.ts`, `combo-matrix.vitest.ts`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112-143,197-307,379-430,524-562,620-659` (flag support, capability record, allowlists)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3050-3070,3109-3130,3231-3245,3350-3390,3450-3456` (mirrored allowlists and provider maps)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-config.vitest.ts:966-1118` (allowlist content assertions)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:66-110` (per-model command construction)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. This pass produced no new finding.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:66-74` | The hand-duplicated allowlists are covered by a parity check in the direction that matters: every model in the TypeScript list is built through the fan-out builder, so a model missing from the fan-out set fails the suite. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts:70-74` maps `CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS`, `DSH_SUPPORTED_MODELS` and `VIBE_SUPPORTED_MODELS` into the per-kind model matrix, and the suite builds a command for each entry. A model present in the TypeScript list but absent from the fan-out set throws \\\"not in the enforced allowlist\\\" and fails the test, so the duplication is guarded in the fail-closed direction.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-config.vitest.ts:966-1118` pins each allowlist's exact contents, so an accidental removal is caught even before the builder runs.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:191-196` states that the capability record is checked against the builders by a conformance test rather than read by them, which is the documented design for the duplication.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **The reverse parity direction is untested.** A model present in the fan-out set but absent from the TypeScript list would not fail a test. That direction is fail-open only in the sense that the fan-out would accept a model the config rejects; the config is the gate, so the entry is unreachable. Not a finding.\\n- **`EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` and `EXECUTOR_ADAPTER_CAPABILITIES[].sandboxSurface` are parallel records.** They are not derivable from each other — claude's `permission-mode` is preventive, devin's is not — so the duplication is intentional and documented at `executor-config.ts:281-296`.\\n- **The capability record is documentation-as-code.** It is read by the conformance test and the catalog, not by the builders, which the record's own comment states. A reader expecting runtime enforcement from it is reading it wrong.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Allowlist duplication is bounded and tested.** Four mirrored lists, each pinned by content assertions and exercised through the builder.\\n- **Comment accuracy after the range.** The comments the range rewrote (`executor-config.ts:117-142,281-306`, `fanout-run.cjs:2973-2975,3005-3008`) describe the code beside them.\\n- **No dead exports.** Every exported allowlist and predicate has a test or a builder consumer.\\n- **Capability record shape.** One frozen record per kind, with a table-driven conformance test, so a new kind cannot be added without a record.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A maintainability finding for the mirrored allowlists.** Ruled out: the fail-closed direction is tested through the builder, and the fail-open direction is unreachable because the config gates first.\\n- **A finding for the single-member `ExecutorResumeMode` union.** Ruled out: it documents the contract that no builder resumes a provider session, and the conformance test asserts it for every kind.\\n- **A finding for the lazy `require` inside `sandboxEnforcementFor`.** Ruled out: it is the documented way a CJS script loads the TypeScript record, and Node caches the module.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Frontier node: F-1-004 (active; the reducer's breadth-first rule selects the shallowest node with the fewest visits)\\n- Focus area: the gateway's maintainability: whether `GATEWAY_IDENTITY_FIELDS` is a denylist that a future identity field would slip past, whether `eventContentDigest`'s head-nulling is explained where a maintainer will find it, and whether the conflict path's stderr write duplicates the JSON line.\\n- Reason: F-1-002 maintainability is clean; the gateway node has three dimensions covered and maintainability is its last.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-002 all four dimensions covered; F-1-004 maintainability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (parity-test tracing closed the duplication question); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: `GATEWAY_IDENTITY_FIELDS`, `eventContentDigest`, and the conflict stderr path.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202692541,"end":1795202695752}}}}
