{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202808738,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa6ced3d002lP2Oa5fhcG5PDf","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa6cdb0d001Lr1237dCjumRGZ","type":"tool","id":"call_195284b2dd521347bde2112a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 013\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 13 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-2-007: correctness**\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (depth 2 of 3, child of F-1-002), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts`\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, `fanout-run.cjs` builders and `sandboxEnforcementFor`, `executor-config.ts` capability records.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` (`sandboxEnforcementFor`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2870-2907` (codex)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2909-2960` (claude)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2994-3048` (opencode)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3160-3230` (cursor)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3290-3340` (devin)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3392-3448` (pi)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3560-3626` (dsh)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:281-307` (preventive record and its comments)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`sandboxEnforcementFor` cannot see the fan-out containment guard, so a devin workspace-write lineage records `none` although the capability record names that guard as its compensating control** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3337` -- The devin builder sets `compensatingControl: resolvedSandbox === 'read-only'`, so `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` both report `sandboxEnforcement: none`. The capability record's own comment says devin's confinement for write lineages \"is the fan-out's post-hoc write-containment guard, not an OS boundary\" (`executor-config.ts:303`), and the builder comment repeats it. The guard runs for every lineage, but `sandboxEnforcementFor` only sees the command's own arguments, so the recorded value omits the control the record says is the confinement.\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \"compensatingControl\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` shows the devin site at 3337 and the other builders' sites; `sandboxEnforcementFor` at 2819-2825 reads only `input.confines` and `input.compensatingControl`. The containment guard's enablement is at `fanout-run.cjs:4650-4655` (`containmentEnabled = true`), outside the builder's view.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"devin command builder\", \"sandboxEnforcementFor\", \"invocation-metadata effectiveConfig\", \"fan-out write-containment guard\"]\n   - Case: a devin workspace-write lineage writes a path outside its lineage directory. The containment guard detects, records and quarantines it, but `invocation-metadata.json` says `sandboxEnforcement: none`, so an auditor reading the provenance concludes no control ran at all and cannot tell the guard's report from an unguarded run.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:303`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3337` | The capability record and the builder agree on the mechanism but disagree on what the recorded label should say for devin workspace-write. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4650-4655` enables the write-containment guard for every dispatch kind (`containmentEnabled = true`), so the control the devin record names is real and runs; the gap is only that the label does not mention it.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2821-2824` derives the label from `confines` and `compensatingControl` alone, and neither field can express a runner-level guard.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:303` states the devin compensating control in prose, which is the only place it is recorded.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **The label describes the command, not the run.** Read that way, `none` for devin workspace-write is accurate: the command carries no restriction. The finding is that the field's name and the record's comment invite the other reading, and no other field carries the guard.\n- **The dsh case is the opposite direction.** R1-P2-001 reports a command that is confined while the label says `none`; this finding reports a runner-level control the label cannot see. Both are provenance fidelity, not behavior.\n- **Cursor's read-only is labeled `compensating`.** `--mode plan` is an approval mode and the builder sets `compensatingControl` from its presence, which is the correct label for that mechanism.\n- **Claude's workspace-write is labeled `preventive`.** The record justifies it as the CLI's tool gate running before a write/exec, and print mode cannot run Bash. The label is consistent with the record even though `acceptEdits` auto-approves edits; the record is the authority, so this is not reported as a finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Codex.** `--sandbox` is passed through, `confines` follows the mode, and the label is `preventive` for the two confined modes and `none` for full access.\n- **Opencode.** `workspace-write` sets `compensatingControl` and the label is `compensating`; `danger-full-access` is `none`; `read-only` is refused before the label is computed.\n- **Cursor.** `--sandbox enabled` yields `preventive`, `--sandbox disabled` yields `none`, and `--mode plan` yields `compensating`.\n- **Pi.** `read-only` adds the tool allowlist and `compensatingControl` is derived from that same argv, so the label cannot drift from the command.\n- **Vibe.** No sandbox surface, no compensating control, `none` in every mode, matching the record.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A P1 for claude's `preventive` label under `acceptEdits`.** Ruled out: the capability record is the stated authority and justifies the entry as the CLI's tool gate running before a write/exec, and print mode cannot run Bash. Recorded as a judgment call rather than a finding.\n- **A duplicate of R1-P2-001.** Ruled out: that finding is the dsh command being confined while the label says `none`; this one is a runner-level guard the label cannot see.\n- **A finding for the containment guard itself.** Ruled out: it runs for every kind and reports out-of-scope writes; the gap is the label, not the guard.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (still active; security next)\n- Focus area: whether the containment guard's quarantine copy can itself write outside the lineage directory, and whether a devin `danger-full-access` lineage's guard report is distinguishable from an unguarded run.\n- Reason: F-2-007 correctness produced one P2; the node's remaining risk is the guard's own write path, which correctness did not examine.\n- Rotation status: F-2-007 correctness complete; security next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (builder-by-builder matrix comparison found the devin gap); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: the containment guard's quarantine path construction and its report fields.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-013.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-013.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-013.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 013\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 13 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-2-007: correctness**\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (depth 2 of 3, child of F-1-002), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts`\\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, `fanout-run.cjs` builders and `sandboxEnforcementFor`, `executor-config.ts` capability records.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` (`sandboxEnforcementFor`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2870-2907` (codex)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2909-2960` (claude)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2994-3048` (opencode)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3160-3230` (cursor)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3290-3340` (devin)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3392-3448` (pi)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3560-3626` (dsh)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:281-307` (preventive record and its comments)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`sandboxEnforcementFor` cannot see the fan-out containment guard, so a devin workspace-write lineage records `none` although the capability record names that guard as its compensating control** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3337` -- The devin builder sets `compensatingControl: resolvedSandbox === 'read-only'`, so `workspace-write` and `danger-full-access` both report `sandboxEnforcement: none`. The capability record's own comment says devin's confinement for write lineages \\\"is the fan-out's post-hoc write-containment guard, not an OS boundary\\\" (`executor-config.ts:303`), and the builder comment repeats it. The guard runs for every lineage, but `sandboxEnforcementFor` only sees the command's own arguments, so the recorded value omits the control the record says is the confinement.\\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"compensatingControl\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` shows the devin site at 3337 and the other builders' sites; `sandboxEnforcementFor` at 2819-2825 reads only `input.confines` and `input.compensatingControl`. The containment guard's enablement is at `fanout-run.cjs:4650-4655` (`containmentEnabled = true`), outside the builder's view.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"devin command builder\\\", \\\"sandboxEnforcementFor\\\", \\\"invocation-metadata effectiveConfig\\\", \\\"fan-out write-containment guard\\\"]\\n   - Case: a devin workspace-write lineage writes a path outside its lineage directory. The containment guard detects, records and quarantines it, but `invocation-metadata.json` says `sandboxEnforcement: none`, so an auditor reading the provenance concludes no control ran at all and cannot tell the guard's report from an unguarded run.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:303`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3337` | The capability record and the builder agree on the mechanism but disagree on what the recorded label should say for devin workspace-write. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4650-4655` enables the write-containment guard for every dispatch kind (`containmentEnabled = true`), so the control the devin record names is real and runs; the gap is only that the label does not mention it.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2821-2824` derives the label from `confines` and `compensatingControl` alone, and neither field can express a runner-level guard.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:303` states the devin compensating control in prose, which is the only place it is recorded.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **The label describes the command, not the run.** Read that way, `none` for devin workspace-write is accurate: the command carries no restriction. The finding is that the field's name and the record's comment invite the other reading, and no other field carries the guard.\\n- **The dsh case is the opposite direction.** R1-P2-001 reports a command that is confined while the label says `none`; this finding reports a runner-level control the label cannot see. Both are provenance fidelity, not behavior.\\n- **Cursor's read-only is labeled `compensating`.** `--mode plan` is an approval mode and the builder sets `compensatingControl` from its presence, which is the correct label for that mechanism.\\n- **Claude's workspace-write is labeled `preventive`.** The record justifies it as the CLI's tool gate running before a write/exec, and print mode cannot run Bash. The label is consistent with the record even though `acceptEdits` auto-approves edits; the record is the authority, so this is not reported as a finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Codex.** `--sandbox` is passed through, `confines` follows the mode, and the label is `preventive` for the two confined modes and `none` for full access.\\n- **Opencode.** `workspace-write` sets `compensatingControl` and the label is `compensating`; `danger-full-access` is `none`; `read-only` is refused before the label is computed.\\n- **Cursor.** `--sandbox enabled` yields `preventive`, `--sandbox disabled` yields `none`, and `--mode plan` yields `compensating`.\\n- **Pi.** `read-only` adds the tool allowlist and `compensatingControl` is derived from that same argv, so the label cannot drift from the command.\\n- **Vibe.** No sandbox surface, no compensating control, `none` in every mode, matching the record.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A P1 for claude's `preventive` label under `acceptEdits`.** Ruled out: the capability record is the stated authority and justifies the entry as the CLI's tool gate running before a write/exec, and print mode cannot run Bash. Recorded as a judgment call rather than a finding.\\n- **A duplicate of R1-P2-001.** Ruled out: that finding is the dsh command being confined while the label says `none`; this one is a runner-level guard the label cannot see.\\n- **A finding for the containment guard itself.** Ruled out: it runs for every kind and reports out-of-scope writes; the gap is the label, not the guard.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (still active; security next)\\n- Focus area: whether the containment guard's quarantine copy can itself write outside the lineage directory, and whether a devin `danger-full-access` lineage's guard report is distinguishable from an unguarded run.\\n- Reason: F-2-007 correctness produced one P2; the node's remaining risk is the guard's own write path, which correctness did not examine.\\n- Rotation status: F-2-007 correctness complete; security next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (builder-by-builder matrix comparison found the devin gap); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: the containment guard's quarantine path construction and its report fields.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-013.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202805053,"end":1795202808738}}}}
