{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202872790,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa6df35f002RO56Dlc45t2Ipf","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa6de58a001v1b1dwaTDxs95P","type":"tool","id":"call_fe9237f3e8ee3a0f3c5200f6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"A=specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs block --target review --artifact-dir \"$A\" --node-id F-2-007 --dimension traceability\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"$A\" --node-id F-2-007 --status active --iteration 15 >/dev/null && echo activated\necho \"=== sandboxEnforcement vocabulary ===\"\ngrep -rn \"sandboxEnforcement\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/*.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs | head -12"},"output":"\n\nFRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-2-007 at depth 2 of 3, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts. Review dimension for this node: traceability.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-2-007: traceability\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-2-007\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration's delta with \"parentId\":\"F-2-007\", one per sub-target your evidence opened inside this node. Each row needs \"question\" (what to review), \"scope\" (paths inside the review target) and \"evidence\". The admission step prunes duplicates, anything outside the review target, anything past the depth or fan-out caps, and any budget above one the parent recorded. Never write review/frontier-nodes.jsonl or a coverage surface yourself.activated\n=== sandboxEnforcement vocabulary ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193:`--preview` builds every lineage command without writing: it prints the redacted argv (each prompt replaced by its digest), cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set and the model, reasoning effort and sandbox mode, then exits before any directory, ledger or store exists. In `effective_config`, `permissionMode` is the value the command passes after `--permission-mode`, or null for a kind that passes none (cli-codex, cli-cursor, cli-opencode, cli-pi), `sandboxEnforcement` is `preventive` when the executor's own confinement is on, `compensating` when the builder emits a non-OS restriction and otherwise `none`, and `effortApplied` is `flag`, `baked` (dsh, whose route patch sets the effort) or `none`. The preview JSON also carries `dry_run_halt`, the `child-spawn` halt event for `step_fanout_spawn` that the workflow prints when a dry run halts there, and `topic_digest`, the SHA-256 of the collapsed research topic, null for review. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage prints no command, and a matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197:A lineage counts as fulfilled only when its state log holds at least one iteration, a terminal stop row from this attempt (`terminal_gates` for review, a closeout synthesis row for research, where `synthesis_incomplete` does not count), every iteration row before that terminal row in the file, and no row whose stamp carries an explicit zone stamped more than two minutes after the lineage process ended; iteration stamps are written by the model, so they are never compared with the terminal row's stamp. A research lineage writes no stop-check row, so its closeout row must also carry a `stopReason` from the frozen lifecycle enum, and a `maxIterationsReached` stop must have recorded as many distinct iterations as the `maxIterations` cap in the lineage's own config; the failures are `missing_stop_reason`, `unknown_stop_reason` and `max_iterations_unproven`, which an unreadable cap also yields. Review keeps its gate-row check, and the lenient pre-spawn skip check is unchanged. Otherwise it fails even at exit 0. The executor-group `--sandbox-mode` maps to `sandboxMode`. A `cli-claude-code` lineage keeps `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so the runner warns at launch, and if that lineage records nothing its failure names `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. A `cli-opencode` lineage takes the same `workspace-write` default: it runs `--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`, merged into any inherited value (one that is unparseable or not a JSON object fails the build). That stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but not Bash, which can still write anywhere, so the preview records `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating`, never `preventive`. `danger-full-access` is plain `--auto` with no deny, and an explicit `read-only` is refused.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2819:function sandboxEnforcementFor(input) {\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2849:    sandboxEnforcement: sandboxEnforcementFor(input),\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nFRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-2-007 at depth 2 of 3, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts. Review dimension for this node: traceability.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-2-007: traceability\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-2-007\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration's delta with \"parentId\":\"F-2-007\", one per sub-target your evidence opened inside this node. Each row needs \"question\" (what to review), \"scope\" (paths inside the review target) and \"evidence\". The admission step prunes duplicates, anything outside the review target, anything past the depth or fan-out caps, and any budget above one the parent recorded. Never write review/frontier-nodes.jsonl or a coverage surface yourself.activated\n=== sandboxEnforcement vocabulary ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193:`--preview` builds every lineage command without writing: it prints the redacted argv (each prompt replaced by its digest), cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set and the model, reasoning effort and sandbox mode, then exits before any directory, ledger or store exists. In `effective_config`, `permissionMode` is the value the command passes after `--permission-mode`, or null for a kind that passes none (cli-codex, cli-cursor, cli-opencode, cli-pi), `sandboxEnforcement` is `preventive` when the executor's own confinement is on, `compensating` when the builder emits a non-OS restriction and otherwise `none`, and `effortApplied` is `flag`, `baked` (dsh, whose route patch sets the effort) or `none`. The preview JSON also carries `dry_run_halt`, the `child-spawn` halt event for `step_fanout_spawn` that the workflow prints when a dry run halts there, and `topic_digest`, the SHA-256 of the collapsed research topic, null for review. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage prints no command, and a matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197:A lineage counts as fulfilled only when its state log holds at least one iteration, a terminal stop row from this attempt (`terminal_gates` for review, a closeout synthesis row for research, where `synthesis_incomplete` does not count), every iteration row before that terminal row in the file, and no row whose stamp carries an explicit zone stamped more than two minutes after the lineage process ended; iteration stamps are written by the model, so they are never compared with the terminal row's stamp. A research lineage writes no stop-check row, so its closeout row must also carry a `stopReason` from the frozen lifecycle enum, and a `maxIterationsReached` stop must have recorded as many distinct iterations as the `maxIterations` cap in the lineage's own config; the failures are `missing_stop_reason`, `unknown_stop_reason` and `max_iterations_unproven`, which an unreadable cap also yields. Review keeps its gate-row check, and the lenient pre-spawn skip check is unchanged. Otherwise it fails even at exit 0. The executor-group `--sandbox-mode` maps to `sandboxMode`. A `cli-claude-code` lineage keeps `workspace-write`, which runs `acceptEdits` and cannot run Bash in `-p` mode, so the runner warns at launch, and if that lineage records nothing its failure names `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access`. A `cli-opencode` lineage takes the same `workspace-write` default: it runs `--auto` with an inline `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` that denies `external_directory`, merged into any inherited value (one that is unparseable or not a JSON object fails the build). That stops OpenCode's file tools at the working directory but not Bash, which can still write anywhere, so the preview records `sandboxEnforcement` `compensating`, never `preventive`. `danger-full-access` is plain `--auto` with no deny, and an explicit `read-only` is refused.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2819:function sandboxEnforcementFor(input) {\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2849:    sandboxEnforcement: sandboxEnforcementFor(input),\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"A=specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek\\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs block --target review --artifact-dir \\\"$A\\\" --node-id F-2-007 --dimension traceability\\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \\\"$A\\\" --node-id F-2-007 --status active --iteration 15 >/dev/null && echo activated\\necho \\\"=== sandboxEnforcement vocabulary ===\\\"\\ngrep -rn \\\"sandboxEnforcement\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/*.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202872159,"end":1795202872790}}}}
