{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795202880489,"sessionID":"<redacted>","part":{"partID":"prt_1fa6e04d6002vleNJHJPknMnO4","sessionID":"<redacted>","messageID":"msg_1fa6df9cf001sXlP02Q70LRuQC","type":"tool","id":"call_368d41bf166f223445efa931","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 015\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Iteration: 15 of 24\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-2-007: traceability**\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (depth 2 of 3, child of F-1-002), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts`\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, `fanout-run.md` preview section, `executor-config.ts` capability record, `fanout-run.cjs` label derivation.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193,197` (the `sandboxEnforcement` vocabulary and the opencode/claude paragraphs)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` (`sandboxEnforcementFor`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:160-170,281-307` (surface type and preventive record)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:286-329` (per-surface assertions)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Findings - Refined\n\n1. **R13-P2-001 refined: the catalog's definition makes `none` correct for devin workspace-write, so the fix is the record's comment or the builder's flag, not the label** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193` -- The catalog defines `sandboxEnforcement` as `preventive` when the executor's own confinement is on, `compensating` when the builder emits a non-OS restriction, and `none` otherwise. Under that definition the devin workspace-write label is correct: the builder emits no restriction, and the fan-out guard is not a builder output. The inconsistency is therefore between the capability record's comment (which names the guard as devin's compensating control) and the builder's `compensatingControl` flag, not between the label and the catalog. The fix is one of: set `compensatingControl` for devin workspace-write so the label matches the record, or correct the record's comment to say the guard is a runner-level control the label does not describe.\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\n   - Scope proof: the catalog's definition is the only place the three values are defined; `sandboxEnforcementFor` implements it exactly. The record's comment at `executor-config.ts:303` is the only statement that names the guard as the compensating control.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"devin command builder\", \"executor-config.ts preventive record\", \"fanout-run.md vocabulary\", \"sandboxEnforcementFor\"]\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` | The catalog's three-value definition matches `sandboxEnforcementFor` exactly, and the preview paragraph's per-kind claims match the builders. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193,197` | The vocabulary and the per-kind paragraphs match the code; the one inconsistency is inside the capability record, reported as R13-P2-001. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2819-2825` implements the catalog's definition line for line: `preventive` when the kind's preventive capability is true and the command confines, `compensating` when the builder set the flag, `none` otherwise.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` states the opencode preview records `compensating`, never `preventive`, which matches the builder's `compensatingControl: workspaceWrite` and the record's `false` preventive entry.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:286-329` asserts the sandbox surface per kind but not the enforcement label, which is why the devin gap is not caught by the suite.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **The label and the record answer different questions.** The label describes the command; the record's comment describes the run. Both are defensible; the finding is that nothing states which one `sandboxEnforcement` means when they differ.\n- **The catalog is the only definition.** If it were treated as the authority, the record's comment would be the defect. If the record were the authority, the builder would be. The refinement names both fixes rather than choosing.\n- **The conformance test does not assert the label.** It asserts the surface, so a label regression would not fail the suite. That is the same test gap reported as R3-P2-001, not a new one.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Vocabulary definition.** One definition, implemented exactly.\n- **Preview paragraph.** Per-kind claims match the builders.\n- **Opencode label.** `compensating` under workspace-write, `none` under full access, matching the catalog's explicit statement.\n- **Codex and cursor labels.** Follow the mode and the `confines` flag.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A new finding for the vocabulary.** Ruled out: the catalog and the code agree; the inconsistency is inside the record, already reported.\n- **A finding for the conformance test not asserting the label.** Ruled out as a duplicate of R3-P2-001's test-gap class.\n- **A finding for the catalog's per-kind paragraphs.** Ruled out: every claim checked matches the builders.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (still active; maintainability is its last dimension)\n- Focus area: the conformance test's structure as the drift guard for the capability record: whether its per-surface switch can express the label matrix, and whether the record's hand-maintained comments are the only place the runner-level controls are described.\n- Reason: F-2-007 traceability produced one refinement; maintainability is the node's last dimension and the test is its stated guard.\n- Rotation status: F-2-007 correctness, security and traceability complete; maintainability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (catalog-to-code comparison sharpened the fix direction); no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: the conformance test's switch structure and the record's comment blocks.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-015.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-015.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-015.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 015\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review LEAF, inline executor for this detached lineage)\\n- Session: `fanout-deepseek-1795201537192-sq1ivw`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Iteration: 15 of 24\\n- Focus: **Frontier node F-2-007: traceability**\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (depth 2 of 3, child of F-1-002), scope `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts`\\n- Convergence before dispatch: `CONTINUE` / `noStopCandidate`, stuck 0, consecutive failures 0.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `steer.md` (absent), `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `frontier-nodes.jsonl`, `fanout-run.md` preview section, `executor-config.ts` capability record, `fanout-run.cjs` label derivation.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193,197` (the `sandboxEnforcement` vocabulary and the opencode/claude paragraphs)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` (`sandboxEnforcementFor`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:160-170,281-307` (surface type and preventive record)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:286-329` (per-surface assertions)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Findings - Refined\\n\\n1. **R13-P2-001 refined: the catalog's definition makes `none` correct for devin workspace-write, so the fix is the record's comment or the builder's flag, not the label** -- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193` -- The catalog defines `sandboxEnforcement` as `preventive` when the executor's own confinement is on, `compensating` when the builder emits a non-OS restriction, and `none` otherwise. Under that definition the devin workspace-write label is correct: the builder emits no restriction, and the fan-out guard is not a builder output. The inconsistency is therefore between the capability record's comment (which names the guard as devin's compensating control) and the builder's `compensatingControl` flag, not between the label and the catalog. The fix is one of: set `compensatingControl` for devin workspace-write so the label matches the record, or correct the record's comment to say the guard is a runner-level control the label does not describe.\\n   - Finding class: class-of-bug\\n   - Scope proof: the catalog's definition is the only place the three values are defined; `sandboxEnforcementFor` implements it exactly. The record's comment at `executor-config.ts:303` is the only statement that names the guard as the compensating control.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"devin command builder\\\", \\\"executor-config.ts preventive record\\\", \\\"fanout-run.md vocabulary\\\", \\\"sandboxEnforcementFor\\\"]\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Summary |\\n|----------|--------|----------|---------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2817-2825` | The catalog's three-value definition matches `sandboxEnforcementFor` exactly, and the preview paragraph's per-kind claims match the builders. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | - | No spec checklist for a commit-range target. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | - | No agent definition in the range. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | - | No runtime mirror in the range. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:193,197` | The vocabulary and the per-kind paragraphs match the code; the one inconsistency is inside the capability record, reported as R13-P2-001. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2819-2825` implements the catalog's definition line for line: `preventive` when the kind's preventive capability is true and the command confines, `compensating` when the builder set the flag, `none` otherwise.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md:197` states the opencode preview records `compensating`, never `preventive`, which matches the builder's `compensatingControl: workspaceWrite` and the record's `false` preventive entry.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/executor-adapter-capabilities.vitest.ts:286-329` asserts the sandbox surface per kind but not the enforcement label, which is why the devin gap is not caught by the suite.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **The label and the record answer different questions.** The label describes the command; the record's comment describes the run. Both are defensible; the finding is that nothing states which one `sandboxEnforcement` means when they differ.\\n- **The catalog is the only definition.** If it were treated as the authority, the record's comment would be the defect. If the record were the authority, the builder would be. The refinement names both fixes rather than choosing.\\n- **The conformance test does not assert the label.** It asserts the surface, so a label regression would not fail the suite. That is the same test gap reported as R3-P2-001, not a new one.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Vocabulary definition.** One definition, implemented exactly.\\n- **Preview paragraph.** Per-kind claims match the builders.\\n- **Opencode label.** `compensating` under workspace-write, `none` under full access, matching the catalog's explicit statement.\\n- **Codex and cursor labels.** Follow the mode and the `confines` flag.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A new finding for the vocabulary.** Ruled out: the catalog and the code agree; the inconsistency is inside the record, already reported.\\n- **A finding for the conformance test not asserting the label.** Ruled out as a duplicate of R3-P2-001's test-gap class.\\n- **A finding for the catalog's per-kind paragraphs.** Ruled out: every claim checked matches the builders.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Frontier node: F-2-007 (still active; maintainability is its last dimension)\\n- Focus area: the conformance test's structure as the drift guard for the capability record: whether its per-surface switch can express the label matrix, and whether the record's hand-maintained comments are the only place the runner-level controls are described.\\n- Reason: F-2-007 traceability produced one refinement; maintainability is the node's last dimension and the test is its stated guard.\\n- Rotation status: F-2-007 correctness, security and traceability complete; maintainability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (catalog-to-code comparison sharpened the fix direction); no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: the conformance test's switch structure and the record's comment blocks.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-015.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795202876630,"end":1795202880489}}}}
